1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A071561  DAR Ancestor # A071561]
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/6970298/epaphras-lord Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Epaphras Lord BIRTH	26 Dec 1709 Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	25 Nov 1799 (aged 89) Colchester, New London County, Connecticut, USA BURIAL	 Century Cemetery Marlborough, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA  Show 
2 CONC Map PLOT	187 MEMORIAL ID	6970298 · View Source SHARE  SAVE TOSUGGEST EDITS MEMORIAL PHOTOS 4 FLOWERS 6 from "Biographical Sketches of the Graduates of Yale College (1701-1745)": 
2 CONT
2 CONT EPAPHRAS LORD, fourth son of Richard and Abigail (Warren) Lord, of Hartford, Connecticut, was born in Harford, December 26, 1709. His elder brothers were graduated in 1718 and 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was probably a lawyer, and resided at first in Wethersfield, and then for a short time in Hartford. He was married in Middletown, Connecticut, March 17, 1730/31, to Hope, daughter of Captain George Phillips. She was born March 
2 CONC 17. 1710, and died Decemher 1, 1736, having borne him two sons and a daughter. Before her death he had removed to Colchester, Connecticut, where he was married, November 25, 1742, to Lucy, daughter of the Rev. John Bulkley (Harv. 
2 CONC 1699), the first minister of the town. He reprsented Colchester in the General Assembly at six sessions between 1743 and 1754. In 1747 he headed the list of petitioners for the erection of a new parish in the northwestern part of 
2 CONC the town, which was called Marlborough, and was set off as a distinct townsbip in 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at his residence, in Marlborough Parish, November 25, 1799, in his 90th year. His wife died on the 10th of the following May, in her 81st year. By his second marriage he had six sons and nine daughters; five of these sons,
2 CONC  and one by his first marriage, survived their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by 1st wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Epaphras Lord (1732-1738) 2. Samuel Phillips Lord (1734-1811) 3. Hope Lord Jones (1736-1798)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by 2nd wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Epaphras Lord (1743-1819) [link below] 2. Elisha Lord (1744/45-1819) 3. Dorothy Lord (1746-1752) [link below] 4. Theodore Lord (1747-1845) 5. Lucy Lord Phelps (1748-1822) 6. Jerusha Lord Skinner (1749-1836) [link below] 7. Bulk
2 CONC eley Lord (1751-1751) [link below] 8. Dorothy Lord (1752-1753) [link below] 9. Dorothy Lord Talcott (1753-1839) 10. John Bulkeley Lord (1754-1815) 11. Eunice Lord Coggswell (1756-1787) 12. Caroline Lord Phelps (1758-1819) 13. Lydi
2 CONC a Lord Chapman (1759-1822) 14. Abigail Lord Everett (1761-1845) 15. Ichabod Lord (1762-1840) -THS
