2 CONT
2 CONT Erasmus Phelps BIRTH	8 Jan 1800 Westfield, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA DEATH	24 Jun 1840 (aged 40) Bureau, Bureau County, Illinois, USA BURIAL	 Oakland Cemetery Princeton, Bureau County, Illinois, USA MEMORIAL ID	175706839 
2 CONC · View Source SHARE  SAVE TOSUGGEST EDITS MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 2 Erasmus Phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT The Illinois Free Trader, Ottawa, Ill, July 3, 1840 From the Chicago Democrat. Suicide. Princeton, June 24, 1840.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Sir, - On the 21st instant, an inquest was held on the body of Erasmus Phelps. The body was found in the Bureau, about five miles south of this place. Mr. Phelps, left his boarding house, about three miles from where he was f
2 CONC ound, about 5 o'clock P.M., on Thursday, the 4th inst.; and from the appearance of the body and other circumstances, he had committed suicide by drowning, on the evening of the 4th of June. His coat was found hanging on a bush on 
2 CONC the bank near the body, folded so as to protect the pockets from the wet. He had taken what was valuable or might be injured by the wet, from his vest and pantaloons' pockets and put them in his coat pocket. His hat was lying in t
2 CONC he path near the coat. There was about $10 found in his wallet and a memorandum without date or name, tho' in his hand-writing, stating how he wished his property disposed of, and closing with these words, "For this, I know not wh
2 CONC y I am lead to do it." Mr. Phelps was unmarried, about 40, and universally respected by all that knew him, and has left a handsome property. He had been in ill-health for the last year and a half; and, being of an active business 
2 CONC turn, had become low-spirited and dejected; and, no doubt, committed the act in a fit of despondency. Mr. Phelps has two brothers living in North Carolina, a brother and sister in Westfield, Massachusetts, one in N. York and a bro
2 CONC ther-in-law in Hartford, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Could be interned elsewhere
2 CONT
