1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/228561085/kathleen_louise-phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT Kathleen Louise Steinmeyer Phelps
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 1 Mar 1932
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 13 Jun 2021 (aged 89)
2 CONT Stover, Morgan County, Missouri, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Stover Cemetery
2 CONT Stover, Morgan County, Missouri, USA
2 CONT Memorial ID
2 CONT 228561085 · View Source
2 CONT Memorial
2 CONT Photos 2
2 CONT Flowers 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by Diana
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 1st day of March in 1932, August and Laura Alpers Steinmeyer welcomed a daughter into their family and named her Kathleen Louise. She was baptized and confirmed in the St. Paul Lutheran Church in Stover. She was a graduate 
2 CONC of Stover High School and shortly after graduation moved to Kansas City, where she received her associate degree from Longview Community College.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kathleen married Cecil Dills and to this union four children were born. On July 13, 1966, in Kansas City, Missouri, Kathleen married Clayson Phelps, who preceded her in death December 22, 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kathleen worked for Western-Electric in Lee's Summit, retiring as supervisor.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was in the 90's that Kathleen and Clay decided to move back to her hometown, building a home at the edge of the city limits. It was in Stover that she found time to open her dream shop, Dabber's Depot, where her creative side c
2 CONC ould truly be expressed. She held painting and quilting classes for local residents and also kept busy working at several businesses in town.
2 CONT
2 CONT It was early Sunday morning, June 13, 2021, at the Golden Age Living Center in Stover, that Kathleen Phelps received the promise of eternal life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include three children and their spouses, a daughter-in-law,; a brother and sister-in-law, a sister, fourteen grandchildren and many great grandchildren, along with nieces, nephews, other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband, Clay, Kathleen was preceded in death by her parents, three sons, Gary Dills, Robert Phelps and Richard Phelps, one daughter, Sandy Phelps, two brothers, Vernon Steinmeyer and Marlin Steinmeyer and two s
2 CONC isters, Berniece Hoppen and Norma Steinmeyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family will receive friends from 1:30 p.m. – 2:30 p.m. Thursday, June 17, at the Scrivner-Morrow Funeral Home in Stover.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be 2:30 p.m. Thursday, June 17, at the Scrivner-Morrow Funeral Home in Stover. Interment will be in the Stover Cemetery.
