1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://colchesterhistory.org/wp-content/themes/chs/images/bulk2.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom and his wife Sarah had seven children, the youngest of whom was a son named John who was born in Wethersfield in 1679. John graduated from Harvard in 1699, married Patience Prentice of New London in 1701 and was ordained m
2 CONC inister of the church at Colchester on December 20, 1703. Like his father Gersham, John was not only a minister but also a lawyer and physicians as well. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Chauncy wrote of John Bulkeley that he was one of the greatest geniuses of his day and surpassed his predecessors in the strength of his intellectual power.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and his wife Patience had 12 children, the third of whom was John, and part of this exhibit will focus on his lineal descendents, Eliphalet Adams Bulkeley and Morgan Gardner Bulkeley.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was born in Colchester in 1705 and died here in 1753. His first wife was Mary Gardiner from New London, and after her death he married Abigail Hastings. He was the first Bulkeley to graduate from Yale (1726).
2 CONT
2 CONT John’s younger brother Gershom was born in Colchester in 1708 and died here in 1788. He married Abigail Robbins of Wethersfield in 1733 and they had 8 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom served as a Captain in the 1st Company which fought during the 1757 Campaign in the French and Indian War. Gershom also was Colchester’s deputy to the Connecticut General Assembly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom’s family lineage is displayed in some detail in the exhibit, which tells about the re-discovery and exhumation of “The Tomb of Gershom Bulkeley and his Descendents”.
2 CONT _______________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN OF REV. JOHN AND PATIENCE PRENTICE BULKELEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah, born April 8, 1702; m.1 Jonathan Trumbull; m2, John Wells.
2 CONT # Another daughter, born May 6, 1704, and died about three hours after.
2 CONT # John, born April 19, 1705; m.1, Mary Gardiner, Oct. 29, 1738; m2, Abigail Hastings, April 16, 1751.
2 CONT # Dorothy, born Feb. 28, 1706.
2 CONT # Gershom, born Feb. 14, 1709.
2 CONT # Charles, born Dec. 26, 1710.
2 CONT # Peter, born Nov. 21, 1712.
2 CONT # Patience, born May 21, 1715.
2 CONT # Oliver, born July 29, 1717; died Jan. 1, 1779.
2 CONT # Lucy, born June 29, 1720.
2 CONT # Irene, died Feb. 20, 1722.
2 CONT # Joseph, died Feb. 25, 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/bulkeleyfamilyor00chap/bulkeleyfamilyor00chap_djvu.txt
2 CONT *[http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bulkeley-195 WikiTree Profile]
2 CONT *THE GROTON AVERY CLAN, Vol. I, by Elroy McKendree Avery and Catherine Hitchcock (Tilden) Avery, Cleveland, 1912.  p. 219
2 CONT * http://www.ctgenweb.org/county/conewlondon/towns/colchester.html “The town was originally part of Hartford Co., but on October 13, 1698 application was made by Michael Taintor, Samuel Northam and Nathanial Foote and the land was
2 CONC  transferred to New London and received its name Colchester. Colchester was incorporated into New London Co. on May 11, 1699.”
