2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 3 FLOWERS 0 Martha and William had at least 10 children, 5 of whom were buried in Avondale Section H, near their parents: • Martha Phelps Buckingham Riddell (1864-1945)*, married James D. Riddell • Frederick Willia
2 CONC m "Fred" Buckingham (1866-1913)*, married Anna Barbara Ritz • Norman Phelps Buckingham (1867-1936)*, buried in Masonic Cemetery of British Columbia, Burnaby BC • Jane Maria Buckingham (1870-1870)* • Walter Ellis Buckingham (1871-1
2 CONC 949), buried in Woodlawn Cemetery (Block E), Guelph ON, married Annie Kilgour • Mary Barry Buckingham Marquis (1873-1960)*, buried in Mount Pleasant Cemetery, Mount Pleasant ON, married John D. Archibald Marquis • James Charles Ha
2 CONC rold Buckingham (1876-1883)* • Esther Beatrix Buckingham Hurlburt (1878-1957)*, buried in North Battleford Municipal Cemetery, North Battleford SK, married Frederick Heman Hurlburt. (Esther was enumerated as "Maud Buckingham" in t
2 CONC he 1881 census) • William Alexander Buckingham (1880-1883)* (William was enumerated as "Percy Buckingham" in the 1881 census) • Arthur Gordon Buckingham (1885-1961), buried in Brandon Municipal Cemetery (Section: 27B), Brandon MB,
2 CONC  married Norah May Clarke
2 CONT
2 CONT * linked below
2 CONT
2 CONT (Thanks to Shirley for much of the above information)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------
2 CONT Before 1991 there were 3 gravestones (1 for the parents, 1 for the 2 sons, and the 3rd for the daughter), that by 2015 were replaced by a single stone for the entire family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Per the Perth OGS transcripts, the parents' original stone read: "In memory of / William Buckingham / born Dec. 3, 1832 / at Crediton, Devonshire, England / died June 11, 1915 / Martha Buckingham / born May 7, 1840 / died Jan. 5, 
2 CONC 1935 / He giveth His beloved sleep / "
