2 CONT Funeral services were held on Saturday afternoon, April 5 at 1:30 p.m. at the United Methodist Church in Dallas Center for Beatrice Peitzman, 70. Rev. James Fouke was in charge of the service with organ music provided by Esther Ro
2 CONC yer. The flower committee was Leone Ellerman, Harriett Swain and Evangeline and Bruce Chase. Ushers were Evelyn and Francis Freisz and John Mortimer. Pallbearers were Clair Baldner, Tom Barrett, Bradley Fox, Don Gift, Bill Gift, a
2 CONC nd Everett Randall. Interment was at the Brethren Cemetery at Dallas Center. Bea had been in ill health for many years and was finally a patient at the Health Care Unit at Spurgeon Manor for many months where she passed away on We
2 CONC dnesday, April 2.
2 CONT She is survived by her husband, Dale, one son, Fred of Torrance, California, and one daughter, Mary Jo Bennett of Ankeny and seven grandchildren. She was a very sweet and loving person and will be greatly missed by her family and 
2 CONC her many friends.
