1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE: Death date currently conflicts current: March 22, 1828  Wikitree, FAG and Leftwich book November 27th 1834
2 CONT
2 CONT "James Turner, who married his daughter, Sarah Leftwich, 9 slaves;" * https://www.seekingmyroots.com/members/files/G004082.pdf page 22
2 CONT
2 CONT " (2) Sally (Sarah) Leftwich, b. January 20, 1762, d. November 27, 1834,
2 CONT married Rev. James Turner, August 25, 1778. (See V-2). " 
2 CONT * https://www.seekingmyroots.com/members/files/G004082.pdf page 23
2 CONT
2 CONT "(2) Sally (Sarah) Leftwich (Colonel William, Augustine, Sr.,
2 CONT Thomas, Sr., Ralph), b. January 20, 1762, d. November 27, 1834,
2 CONT married Rev. James Turner, the noted Presbyterian minister,
2 CONT August 25, 1778, in Bedford County, Va. She and her husband
2 CONT are buried in the cemetery at Bedford, Va. There is given at this
2 CONT point two of his oldest children, daughters, who married brothers,
2 CONT John and Price Hopkins, respectively. For the descendants of
2 CONT his other twelve children, see under Turner Family herein. Among issue:
2 CONT VL
2 CONT (1) Mary Tumer, b. August 25, 1779, d. January 10, 1848, married John
2 CONT Hopkins, September 2, 1800. (See VI-1).
2 CONT (2) Elizabeth Turner, b. July 10, 1781, d. July 11, 1810, married Price Hopkins, October 18, 1801. For descendants see "Hopkins of Vll'ginia and
2 CONT Related Families," by Walter L. Hopkins. "
2 CONT * https://www.seekingmyroots.com/members/files/G004082.pdf page 33
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * FAG https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/83421269/sarah-frances-turner
2 CONT
