2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   William Lemuel Murphy (1845 - 1909)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Mentow Baptist Church Cemetery Mentow Bedford County Virginia, USA  Created by: PictureTaker Record added: Feb 26, 2011 Find A Grave Memorial# 66163627
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary from Newspaper: Lynchburg News, Thursday Morning, August 21, 1930
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Lucinda Murphy
2 CONT Bedford; Aug 20- Mrs. Lucinda Jane Murphy, 81, wife of the late William L. Murphy, died at the home of her daughter , Mrs. R.W. Couch, in West Lynchburg Tuesday. Mrs. Murphy had been almost an invalid for several years but paralys
2 CONC is from which she had suffered for the past two weeks was the immediate cause of death. She was a native of Bedford County and a member of Mentow Baptist Church. She was Miss Leftwich before her marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following children survive: Mrs. R. W. Couch, Mrs. J. C. Dobyns and Edgar Murphy of Lynchburg; Mrs. S. E. Howell, of Leesville; Mrs. Bob Krantz of Huddleston; Mrs. O. B. Spitzer of Ronceverte, WV, and Walter Murphy of Evington
2 CONC . One brother, William H. Leftwich of Bedford, survives, also fifty grandchildren, and 21 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Murphy were held this afternoon at Mentow Baptist Church in Bedford County. Rev. J. E. Poteat and Rev. Mr. Hughes conducting the services and interment taking place in the church yard. The granddaughters 
2 CONC of Mrs. Murphy served as flower bearers and the pallbearers were Winfree and Lloyd Dobyns, Wallace Couch, Otha Krantz, Nolan Murphy and Floyd Howell.
