2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ruth and William:
2 CONT *1. Caleb PHELPS4, b 11 Jan 1708/9; m/1 Mary MOORE, who d 20 Apr 1747; m/2 Mary (LATHROP) HENDERSON. r Windsor.
2 CONT *2. Jacob PHELPS4, b 18 Jun 1711; m Abigail ALVORD; r Windsor.
2 CONT *3. Ruth PHELPS4, b 23 Jan 1713/4; m Samuel PHELPS.
2 CONT *4. DAVID3, b 12 May 1686; m Hannah POST. 13
2 CONT *5. BENJAMIN3, b about 1690; m Hannah LEWIS.
2 CONT *6. ELIZABETH3, b about 1690 (Barbour Index states 9 Feb 1684/5; m Windsor 10 Nov 1709 Daniel                    LOOMIS, b 15 Nov 1682, d 1754, son of Daniel and Mary (ELLSWORTH) LOOMIS.  Elizabeth and Daniel lived 2 1/2 miles sou
2 CONC th of Windsor Center which would place them in the Deerfield section of present day Windsor Samuel’s will of 21 Feb 1708/9 left 25 pounds each to Elizabeth, Mindwell, and Sarah, when they become 18 years of age.  This would mean E
2 CONC lizabeth was born after 1689. [~ Barbour Index; Jerijah Barber Manuscript; Loomis Gen; Windsor Hist Soc:Filer Gen,1991,Arnold ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth and Daniel:
2 CONT *1. Daniel LOOMIS4, b 2 Nov 1710; m/1 Sarah GROVER; m/2 Sarah ENOS; r Union CT.
2 CONT *2. Elizabeth LOOMIS4, b 20 May 1712;  m Daniel EGGLESTON; r Bloomfield CT.  He m/2 Mary                                            ROCKWELL.
2 CONT *3. Mary LOOMIS4, b 10 May 1714; m Joseph HOSKINS.
2 CONT *4. Elisha LOOMIS4, b 6 Jun 1716; d Colchester CT 11 Nov 1758.
2 CONT *5. Dorothy LOOMIS4, b 21 Jun 1718; m Ichabod LOOMIS; r Torrington CT.
2 CONT *6. David LOOMIS4, b 13 Mar 1719/20, d before 1752.
2 CONT *7. Sibel LOOMIS4, b 18 Sep 1727; m William ALLEN.
2 CONT *8. MINDWELL3, b 3 Dec 1691; d 3 Dec 1712. 14
2 CONT *9. JOHN3, b 1696; m Jane ALVORD.
2 CONT *10. SARAH3, b Windsor 28 Aug 1698; d Westfield MA 4 Jan 1741/2; m/1 Windsor (“both of Windsor”) 17 Oct 1717 Stephen PALMER, b Windsor 20 Jan 1686, d there 17 Nov 1720, son of Timothy and Hannah (BUEL) PALMER. Sarah m/2 5 Oct 1729
2 CONC  Isaac PHELPS III, b Westfield MA 26 Jan 1692/3, son of Isaac and Mary (MAUDSLY) PHELPS. Sarah lived in Poquonock with her first husband Stephen, and at Westfield with Isaac. Isaac m/2 8 May 1755 Joanna ADAMS. [~ Jerijah Barber Ma
2 CONC nuscript; Corresp:Nancy J Pennington; Phelps Gen ~] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah and Stephen:
2 CONT *1. Stephen PALMER4, 18 Jan 1718/19, m Lydia ‑‑‑. 
2 CONT *2. Timothy PALMER4, 28 Jun 1720; d Windsor 1745/6.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah and Isaac:
2 CONT *1. Sarah PHELPS4,  b Westfield MA 31 Jul 1730, m Thomas MOSELEY.  They had no children.
2 CONT *2. Rebecca PHELPS4, b Westfield 22 Jul 1732, m David DEWEY.  They had no children.
2 CONT *3. ?Isaac PHELPS4, b Westfield 16 Apr 1734; he probably died 13/14 Oct 1753, unmarried, or possibly he could be the Isaac who m/1 Jemima HOLCOMB; m/2 widow Anna (BROWN) PALMER; m/3 Joanna HATHAWAY; r Windsor.
2 CONT *4. Mary PHELPS4, b Windsor 12 Jul 1736; perhaps m/1 Artemus EASTMAN; and she perhaps m/2 Michael GRIFFIN; r Simsbury CT.
2 CONT *5. ?Bathsheba PHELPS4, b Windsor; m Samuel HOLCOMB.
2 CONT *6. ?Theodosia PHELPS4, b Windsor 7 May 1738; m Micah GRIFFIN.
2 CONT *7. ?Lucy PHELPS4, b Windsor 9 Dec 1739; m Stephen GRIFFIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are conflicting accounts of these last 3 children, and of the marriages of Isaac and Mary.
