1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Samuel Barber 
2 CONT *Born before 1 October 1648 - Windsor, Hartford, CT
2 CONT * will  dated Feb 21, 1708/9; died Windsor 12 Mar 1708/09
2 CONT * Son of Sgt. Thomas Barber, of Windsor and Jane Coggins 
2 CONT *Married 1 December 1670, Windsor, Hartford, CT, to Mary Coggin 1644
2 CONT *Married 25 January 1676, Windsor, Hartford, CT, to Ruth Drake 1657
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. SAMUEL2 BARBER (Thomas1), baptised Windsor CT 1 Oct 1648; d there 12 Mar 1708/09; m/1 there 1 Dec 1670 Mary COGGIN, b Taunton MA about 1647, d Windsor 19 May 1676, daughter of Thomas and Joan (...) COGGIN, and sister of Bathshe
2 CONC ba who m Samuel’s brother John2 BARBER. (see Thomas2 Barber for further relationships).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel m/2 Windsor 25 Jan 1676/7 Ruth DRAKE, b 1 Dec 1657, d Windsor 13 Nov 1731,  daughter of John and Hannah (MOORE) DRAKE.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his parents' death just after his 14th birthday, Samuel was placed (4 Feb 1662) in the home of his brother Thomas until age 21. At about the time of his marriage, Samuel apparently went with his brother to Simsbury, but must
2 CONC  have returned to Windsor soon, because all of his family's vital records were recorded in Windsor.  He lived in a house on the original Barber tract, nearly opposite the Windsor Cannery on Poquonock Ave.  This house was first occ
2 CONC upied by his brother John, but was transfered to Samuel when John moved to Springfield. [~ 1909 Barber Gen; Barbour Index; CT Hist Soc:LBBarbour Manuscripts; Early Coggins, English and American, by Geo. E McCracken ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT The dates of birth of the children of this family, as given by the best authorities, are greatly at variance with the clear and unmistakable evidence contained in the father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://brooklyncentre.com/trees/getperson.php?personID=I31075&tree=Brainard
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel and Mary, born at Windsor:
2 CONT
2 CONT *        i                   THOMAS3, b 7 Oct 1671; buried 31 Oct 1673.
2 CONT *       ii                   SAMUEL3, b 26 Jan 1673/4; d Windsor 1 Feb 1722/3; m/1 Hepzibah "Ziba" BROWN, b Windsor 19 Nov 1664,       d 20 Dec 1711, daughter of Peter and Mary (GILLETT) BROWN.                              Samuel 
2 CONC m/2 Windsor 18 Jun 1713, Martha PONDER of Westfield MA, b 1677/8, d Windsor (Blooomfield Church rec) 6 Aug 1758.  Samuel lived in Poquonock (in the northwest part of Windsor), one mile north of the Baptist Meeting House. [~ 1909 B
2 CONC arber Gen; CT Church rec; Stiles:Windsor; Jerijah Barber Manuscript ~] 
2 CONT **Children of Samuel and Hepzibah:
2 CONT ***                  i                   MARY4, b 25 Sep 1704
2 CONT ***                          ii                   WILLIAM4, b 17 Jul 1704; died young. (There is a discrepancy in the birth dates of these first two  children in the Barbour Index)
2 CONT **Children of Samuel and Martha:
2 CONT ***                        iii                   MARTHA4, b 1 May 1714;  died young.
2 CONT ***                          iv                   HEPZIBAH4, b 8 Apr 1716; unmarried.
2 CONT ***                         v                   SAMUEL4, b Poquonock CT 28 Aug 1717. In 1732 he requested his uncle Joseph to be his guardian. 
2 CONT ***                          vi                   THOMAS4, b 5 May 1720; d 1745; unmarried. Thomas went with 500 Connecticut men, joined by                                         3500 others from New England, to take Louisburg, N
2 CONC ova Scotia from the French, so that New England fishing could resume; he died there in 1745 during that venture.  
2 CONT ***                         vii                   EZEKIEL4, b 25 Sep 1721; his uncle Joseph Barber was made his guardian 1735, at the request of   Martha his mother.   He was in active service in the Revolutionary War, and marched
2 CONC  to the  Relief of Boston 1775. 
2 CONT ***                        viii                   BENJAMIN4, b 1723; the L B Barbour Manuscript says a Benjamin Barber m Mary LOOMIS of        Windsor.  Benjamin settled in Harwinton.   He served in the Revolutionary Army.
2 CONT ***                          ix                   JAMES4, b Poquonock 172?
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel and Ruth, born at Windsor:
2 CONT *      iii                   JOHN DRAKE3, b ??25 Jan 1676/7; died young  This birth date is probably incorrect, since it is the same as the       marriage date of Ruth to Samuel.  Probably John Drake was born a bit later, and was 
2 CONC the first child of Ruth, and was named for her father John DRAKE. 
2 CONT *10  iv                    WILLIAM3, b 1678; m Esther BROWN.
2 CONT *       v                    MARY3 "Mercy", b 1680; d 27 Aug 1719; m Windsor 22 Jul 1696 Peter BROWN, b Windsor 12 Mar 1666/7,d there 6 Mar 1739, son of Peter and Mary (GILLETTE) BROWN; r Windsor. Mary died on the born. Peter was 
2 CONC perhaps a grandson of Peter BROWN of Plymouth MA, and of the Mayflower; however, the    Mayflower Society thinks there is not enough proof to allow this connection, and will not allow this to be a valid    connection. [~ Corresp:A
2 CONC rthur K Gibson; CT Hist Soc:Brown Manuscript; Corresp:Carl Jordan; Corresp:Bob Seger ~]
2 CONT **Children of Mary and Peter, born at Windsor:
2 CONT ***                           i                   Peter BROWN4, b 28 Jan 1699/1700; probably the Peter BROWN who m 14 Aug 1722 Rachel SCOTT; r Windsor.
2 CONT ***                         ii                   Dinah BROWN4, b 4 Jan 1701/2; m Dea. Thomas POST; r Hebron.       
2 CONT ***                      iii                   Samuel BROWN4, b 28 Aug 1705; m Mary PHELPS; r Windsor.
2 CONT ***                          iv                   Mary BROWN4, b 28 Aug 1708; m Joseph SEGER III.  Joseph m/1 Mehitable PARSONS.  
2 CONT ***                           v            Benjamin BROWN4, b 11 Aug 1711; m/1 Hannah GRANT; m/2 1760 Widow Mary BROWN (probably the widow of Daniel BROWN); m/3 Hannah ‑‑‑; r Windsor.
2 CONT ***                          vi                   Ebenezer BROWN4, b 27 Aug 1719
2 CONT ***                        vii                   Mindwell BROWN4, twin, b 27 Aug 1719; d Springfield MA 25 Feb 1758; unmarried.
2 CONT *   vi                   HANNAH3, b 4 Oct 1681; died before 1708.
2 CONT *11   vii                   JOSEPH3, b 1681(?); m/1 Hannah ‑‑; m/2 Mary LOOMIS.
2 CONT *  viii                   RUTH3, b 24 Jul 1683; d 2 Aug 1747; m Windsor 18 Apr 1706 William PHELPS, b 4 Feb 1668/9, d 1733, son of Timothy and Mary (GRISWOLD) PHELPS; r Windsor.  William m/1 7 Dec 1699 Abigail MUDGE, who d 24 Apr 
2 CONC     1705, and had 2 children by her.  [~ Stiles:Windsor; Windsor Hist Soc:Filer Gen,1991,Arnold ~] 
2 CONT **Children of Ruth and William:
2 CONT ***                        i                   Caleb PHELPS4, b 11 Jan 1708/9; m/1 Mary MOORE, who d 20 Apr 1747; m/2                                                            Mary (LATHROP) HENDERSON. r Windsor.
2 CONT ***                          ii                   Jacob PHELPS4, b 18 Jun 1711; m Abigail ALVORD; r Windsor.
2 CONT ***                         iii                   Ruth PHELPS4, b 23 Jan 1713/4; m Samuel PHELPS.
2 CONT *12    ix                   DAVID3, b 12 May 1686; m Hannah POST.
2 CONT * 13     x                   BENJAMIN3, b about 1690; m Hannah LEWIS.
2 CONT *       xi                   ELIZABETH3, b about 1690 (Barbour Index states 9 Feb 1684/5; m Windsor 10 Nov 1709 Daniel      LOOMIS, b 15 Nov 1682, d 1754, son of Daniel and Mary (ELLSWORTH) LOOMIS.  Elizabeth and Daniel lived 2 1/
2 CONC 2 miles south of Windsor Center which would place them in the Deerfield section of present day Windsor. Samuel’s will of 21 Feb 1708/9 left 25 pounds each to Elizabeth, Mindwell, and Sarah, when they  become 18 years of age.  This
2 CONC  would mean Elizabeth was born after 1689.  [~ Barbour Index; Jerijah Barber Manuscript; Loomis Gen; Windsor Hist Soc:Filer Gen,1991,Arnold ~]
2 CONT **                                           Children of Elizabeth and Daniel:
2 CONT ***                           i                   Daniel LOOMIS4, b 2 Nov 1710; m/1 Sarah GROVER; m/2 Sarah ENOS; r Union CT.
2 CONT ***                          ii                   Elizabeth LOOMIS4, b 20 May 1712;  m Daniel EGGLESTON; r Bloomfield CT.  He m/2 Mary ROCKWELL.
2 CONT ***                         iii                   Mary LOOMIS4, b 10 May 1714; m Joseph HOSKINS.
2 CONT ***                          iv                   Elisha LOOMIS4, b 6 Jun 1716; d Colchester CT 11 Nov 1758.
2 CONT ***                           v                   Dorothy LOOMIS4, b 21 Jun 1718; m Ichabod LOOMIS; r Torrington CT.
2 CONT ***                          vi                   David LOOMIS4, b 13 Mar 1719/20, d before 1752.
2 CONT ***                         vii                   Sibel LOOMIS4, b 18 Sep 1727; m William ALLEN.
2 CONT *   xii                   MINDWELL3, b 3 Dec 1691; d 3 Dec 1712.
2 CONT * 14  xiii                   JOHN3, b 1696; m Jane ALVORD.
2 CONT *      xiv                   SARAH3, b Windsor 28 Aug 1698; d Westfield MA 4 Jan 1741/2; m/1 Windsor (“both of Windsor”) 17 Oct 1717      Stephen PALMER, b Windsor 20 Jan 1686, d there 17 Nov 1720, son of Timothy and Hannah (BUEL)
2 CONC  PALMER.    Sarah m/2 5 Oct 1729 Isaac PHELPS III, b Westfield MA 26 Jan 1692/3, son of Isaac and Mary (MAUDSLY) PHELPS. Sarah lived in Poquonock with her first husband Stephen, and at Westfield with Isaac. Isaac m/2. 8 May 1755 J
2 CONC oanna ADAMS. [~ Jerijah Barber Manuscript; Corresp:Nancy J Pennington; Phelps Gen ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
