1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Lt-Josiah-Barber/6000000008260562446 by https://www.geni.com/people/Abigail-Barber-Loomis/6000000006440692424
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mary Barber''' was born on 11 January 1666 at Windsor, Hartford Co., CT, daughter of Samuel Barber and Ruth Drake.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilson, Lillian May. Barber Genealogy (Nichols Print., Haverhill, Mass., 1909) Page 41 < [https://archive.org/details/barbergenealogyi00wils/page/43/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT 35. MARY BARBER, 3 (Samuel,2 Thomas,1 ) m. July 22, 1696, Peter Brown, Jr., son of Peter and Mary (Gillett) Brown. He was b. Mch. 12. 1666-7. She d. Aug. 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children : born, Windsor, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 103. I. Peter Brown, b. Jan. 28, 1699; prob. m. Aug. 14, 1722, Rachel Scott.
2 CONT * 104. II. Dinah Brown, b. Jan. 4, 1701-2. -j-
2 CONT * 105. III. Samuel Brown, b. Aug. 28, 1705.
2 CONT * 106. IV. Mary Brown, b. Aug. 28, 1708. -|-
2 CONT * 107. V. Benjamin Brown, b. Aug. 11, 1711.
2 CONT * 108. VI. Ebenezer Brown (twin), b. Aug. 27, 1719 ;
2 CONT * 109. VII. Mindwell Brown (twin ) b. Aug. 27, 1719 d. Feb. 25, 1758
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary and Peter, born at Windsor:
2 CONT *1. Peter BROWN4, b 28 Jan 1699/1700; probably the Peter BROWN who m 14 Aug 1722 Rachel                                            SCOTT; r Windsor.
2 CONT *2. Dinah BROWN4, b 4 Jan 1701/2; m Dea. Thomas POST; r Hebron.
2 CONT *3. Samuel BROWN4, b 28 Aug 1705; m Mary PHELPS; r Windsor.
2 CONT *4. Mary BROWN4, b 28 Aug 1708; m Joseph SEGER III.  Joseph m/1 Mehitable PARSONS.                              
2 CONT *5. Benjamin BROWN4, b 11 Aug 1711; m/1 Hannah GRANT; m/2 1760 Widow Mary BROWN (probably the widow of Daniel BROWN); m/3 Hannah ‑‑‑; r Windsor. 
2 CONT *6. Ebenezer BROWN4, b 27 Aug 1719
2 CONT *7. Mindwell BROWN4, twin, b 27 Aug 1719; d Springfield MA 25 Feb 1758; unmarried.
2 CONT *8. HANNAH3, b 4 Oct 1681; died before 1708. 11
2 CONT *9. JOSEPH3, b 1681(?); m/1 Hannah ‑‑; m/2 Mary LOOMIS.
2 CONT *10. RUTH3, b 24 Jul 1683; d 2 Aug 1747; m Windsor 18 Apr 1706 William PHELPS, b 4 Feb 1668/9, d 1733, son of Timothy and Mary (GRISWOLD) PHELPS; r Windsor.  William m/1 7 Dec 1699 Abigail MUDGE, who d 24 Apr 1705, and had 2 child
2 CONC ren by her.  [~ Stiles:Windsor; Windsor Hist Soc:Filer Gen,1991,Arnold ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Brown, husband of Mary Barber, was the grandson of Peter Brown, the Emigrant, a synopsis of the record being as follows :
2 CONT
2 CONT *Peter Brown, b. in England about 1600; came to Plymouth, Mass., in the "Mayflower " and was one of the signers of the Mayflower Compact.
2 CONT **Peter Brown, b. 1632; m. July, 1658, Mary GiUett. She was probably dau. of Jonathan Gillett, who was b. in England about 1600 and came to Dorchester about 1634.
2 CONT ***Peter Brown, b. Mch. 12, 1666; m. Mary Barber
2 CONT
2 CONT ''[note: not accepted by Mayflower Society''] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Barber Genealogy. Page 26 - 28 < [https://archive.org/details/barbergenealogyi00wils/page/27/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org]  >
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Stiles' " Ancient Windsor" gives Sept. 25, 1704, as the date of birth of the daughter Mary, but in the record of the Brown fam- ily, the same authority states that she married Peter Brown in 1696, or eight years before the date of
2 CONC  her birth. In the Appen- dix of the volume mentioned. Dr. Stiles calls attention to this discrepency. It will be seen, by reference to the wills heretofore mentioned that there was a daughter Mary belonging to this family ; that 
2 CONC she was married prior to the making of her father's will, in Feb., 1708-9, and in her sister Mindwell's will she is specifically mentioned as the wife of Peter Brown. Hence she was evidently one of the older children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Samuel Barber, Sr. Barber, Samuel-Sr.— Windsor ; Inv. ;^598-04-10; taken Mch. 1709, by John Moore, Sr. Job. Drake, Sr. and Thomas Marshall- Will dated 21 February 1708-09.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Item. I declare it to be my will that my three daughters, Elizabeth, Mindwell and Sarah, shall have 25^ apiece paid to each of them when they shall be 18 years of age, to make them equal with ''their two sisters who are married.'
2 CONC ' <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >…. And I give to my five daughters (both those that are married and those that are not) the remainder of my estate which is yet undisposed ot, both personal and real, to be equally divided be- tween my 5 daughters, '''Mary''', Ru
2 CONC th, Elizabeth, Mindwell and Sarah, to them and their heirs forever. I appoint my wife Ruth, and my son-in-law William Phelps to be executors. Will proven Apr. 4, 1709. (Hartford Probate Record)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Mindwell Barber. Estate of Mindwell Barber: Inv. taken Feb. 1712-13. Letters of administration granted to Joseph Barber, brother of deceased. John Moore, John Bissell and James Eno, Distributors. By terms of the will, the 
2 CONC estate was to be divided equally between the brothers and sisters of deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Dist. File of Oct. 24, 1714. To the brothers and sisters of the deceased, children of Samuel Barber ; to Samuel, William, David, Joseph, Benjamin and John ; to Daniel Loomis and his wife Elizabeth ; to '''Peter Brown and his wife
2 CONC  Mary''' ; to William Phelps and his wife Ruth ; to Sarah Barber and to William Bar- ber, son of William Barber, deceased. (Hartford Probate Records.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Ruth Barber, Widow of Samuel, Sr. Barber, Ruth,— Windsor ; Invt. i;84-10-06. Taken Nov. 30, 1731 ; Will dated Nov. 13, 1716.
2 CONT
2 CONT >… Lastly my will is that the remainder of my whole estate be di- vided to and among my children hereafter named in equal shares, viz ; '''Mary Brown''' ; Ruth Phelps ; Elizabeth Loomis and Sarah Barbour (Barber).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
