2 DATE 4 JAN 1741
2 ADDR
3 CITY Westfield
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/37604300/sarah_palmer_phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT "According to Families of Ancient Windsor, Sarah Palmer Phelps is the daughter of Samuel and Ruth (Drake) Barber. She married Stephen Palmer in 1717. He died in 1720. She then married Isaac Phelps in 1729. My other references are 
2 CONC Connecticut Barbers and Descendants of Thomas Barber."
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT 1995 Inventory by Walter Ayers, Westfield Historic Commissioner-w/o Isaac
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sarah BARBER (Samuel BARBER3, Thomas BARBER2, John BARBER1) was born 28 Aug 1698 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, and died 4 Jan 1740 in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT #Stephen PALMER 17 Oct 1717 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, son of Timothy PALMER and Hannah BUELL. He was born 20 Jan 1685 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, and died 17 Nov 1720 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut. 
2 CONT #Isaac PHELPS III 5 Oct 1729 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, son of Isaac PHELPS II and Mary MOSLEY. He was born 26 Jan 1692 in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts, and died in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Barber was born on 28 Aug 1698 to Samuel Barber and Ruth Drake.[1] For many years it has been said that she was a Palmer, as discussed below. However, it can now be seen that she was born a Barber and was the widow of a Palm
2 CONC er.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Palmer (son of Timothy Palmer & Hannah Buell) was the 1st husband of Sarah Barber.  They were the parents of Stephen & Timothy Palmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah married 2nd to widower Isaac Phelps, Jr on October 5, 1729. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah and Isaac:
2 CONT
2 CONT  - Sarah,  (our line) b Westfield MA 31 Jul 1730, m Thomas MOSELEY (sic, I say Morley).  They had no children (sic, I say otherwise!).
2 CONT
2 CONT  - Rebecca, b Westfield 22 Jul 1732, m David DEWEY.  They had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT  - Isaac b Westfield 16 Apr 1734; he probably died 13/14 Oct 1753, unmarried, or possibly he could be the Isaac who m/1 Jemima HOLCOMB; m/2 widow Anna (BROWN) PALMER; m/3 Joanna HATHAWAY; r Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Mary b Windsor 12 Jul 1736; perhaps m/1 Artemus EASTMAN; and she perhaps m/2 Michael GRIFFIN; r Simsbury CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT  - Bathsheba b Windsor; m Samuel HOLCOMB.
2 CONT
2 CONT  - Theodosia PHELPS4, b Windsor 7 May 1738; m Micah GRIFFIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT  - Lucy PHELPS4, b Windsor 9 Dec 1739; m Stephen GRIFFIN.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are conflicting accounts of these last 3 children, and of the marriages of Isaac and Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the widow Palmer when she married Issac, and some mistakenly take Palmer to to be her maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Sarah BARBER b: 28 Aug 1698 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 5 Oct 1729 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT  Bathsheba PHELPS
2 CONT
2 CONT  Isaac PHELPS IV c: 22 Feb 1732 in Westfield, Hampden, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT
