1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see: The Griswold family, England-America : Edward of Windsor, Connecticut, Matthew of Lyme, Connecticut, Michael of Wethersfield, Connecticut by Griswold, Glenn E; https://archive.org/details/griswoldfamily
2 CONC en02gris/page/16 (Steven Ferry, February 8, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~steeles/Steele/d126.htm#P2023
2 CONT
2 CONT =Timothy PHELPS=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Timothy PHELPS''' was born on 1 Sep 1639 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. (18744)(18745) (18746)(18747)  He served in the military in 1707 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. (18748)(18749)  
2 CONT *He died in 1719 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT.(18750) (18751) (18752) He had an estate probated on 6 Oct 1719 in Hartford, Hartford Co., CT.(18753)  He served in the Queen Ann's War.(18754)  *Parents: '''William PHELPS''' and '''A
2 CONC nn DOVER'''.
2 CONT *He was married to '''Mary GRISWOLD''' on 19 Mar 1661 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT.(18755) (18756)(18757) (18758)(18759) 
2 CONT *Children were: 
2 CONT # Timothy PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Joseph PHELPS, 
2 CONT # William PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Cornelius PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Mary PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Samuel PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Nathaniel PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Sarah PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Abigail PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Hannah PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Ann PHELPS, 
2 CONT # Martha PHELPS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Left Windsor CT and helped to found Hebron,CT.  -
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy resided in Windsor, Ct., on the old homestead, on land purchased by his father from the Indians. He was propounded Oct., 1663, and made a freeman 2d May, 1664. May, 1690, "Thos. Allen chosen and allowed Capt. of Tained Ban
2 CONC d in Windsor, and Timothy Phelps, Lieut., and are to be commissioned accordingly."
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service: 1690 Lieutenant
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service: 1696 Captain
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service: 1701 Served in Queen Ann's War
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of the Early Phelps Family in Simsbury and Windsor: (URL:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://family.phelpsinc.com/origins/early_phelps_windsor.htm):
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Will and Testament of Mr. Timothy Phelps of Windsor, in the
2 CONT
2 CONT County of Hartford and Colony of Connecticut in New England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1n the name of God, Amen:
2 CONT
2 CONT I, Timothy Phelps of Windsor, in the town, county and colony aforesaid
2 CONT
2 CONT in New England, being very aged, and yet through the mercy of God
2 CONT
2 CONT retaining a good measure of that understanding and memory that he hath
2 CONT
2 CONT been pleased to bestow upon me, do make and ordain this to be my last
2 CONT
2 CONT will and testa?ment: First, I commit my soul to God in Jesus Christ my
2 CONT
2 CONT saviour and my body to the earth, to be decently entered. As for my
2 CONT
2 CONT estate Real and personal, my just Debts and funeral expenses being
2 CONT
2 CONT deducted and paid by my Ex", I will devise and bequeath as followeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Imprimis. I give, devise and bequeath all my estate what?soever, Both
2 CONT
2 CONT Real and personal, To my three sons William, Cornelius, and Samuell to
2 CONT
2 CONT have and to hold and Improve the same in trust for the use of my wife
2 CONT
2 CONT during her natural life and after her decease my will is and I hereby
2 CONT
2 CONT do give and de?vise all my houseing and Lands with the appurtenances,
2 CONT
2 CONT To my sons Timothy Phelps, William Phelps, Cornelius Phelps, Samuel
2 CONT
2 CONT Phelps, Nathl. Phelps and the heirs of Joseph Phelps, in the Room of
2 CONT
2 CONT their father to be equally divided into Six Equal parts provided
2 CONT
2 CONT always; and it is my will that they pay and make up to their Sisters
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, Hannah, Ann and Mar?tha, my daughters or to their heirs and to
2 CONT
2 CONT the heirs of my daughter Abigail deceased fourty eight pounds as money
2 CONT
2 CONT apiece and my will is that what they have already received as entered
2 CONT
2 CONT upon my book shall be reckoned as part of said sum and if my said sons
2 CONT
2 CONT and the heirs of my son Joseph shall pay their sisters and their heirs
2 CONT
2 CONT above mentioned in equal proportion except that the heirs of Joseph
2 CONT
2 CONT shall pay four pounds more then an equal proportion and my son
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius four pounds less then an equal proportion. And my will
2 CONT
2 CONT further is that my wife shall have the free disposal of all her
2 CONT
2 CONT wearing apparel at her decease and that my grandson Samuel Tiler shall
2 CONT
2 CONT have half of that bequeathed to the heirs of my Daughter Abigail if he
2 CONT
2 CONT liveth with me so long as I live or till he comes to the age of
2 CONT
2 CONT eighteen years and I do hereby nominate and appoint my loving wife
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary to be my executrix and my three sons Wil?liam, Cornelius and Sam'
2 CONT
2 CONT to be my executors to this my last will and testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT In witness whereof that this is my last will and Testament I ye sd
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Phelps have hereto put my hand and seal this Second day of
2 CONT
2 CONT March Anno Domini One thousand Seven hun?dred sixteen or seventeen.
2 CONT
2 CONT his
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy X Phelps.
2 CONT
2 CONT mark and a seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT The said Timothy Phelps signed, sealed & declared this to be his last
2 CONT
2 CONT will & Testament in presence of us.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Mansfield, Thomas Moore.
2 CONT
2 CONT And whereas I being aged and my wife so and not know?ing how long it
2 CONT
2 CONT may please God to continue my life and not knowing what debts and
2 CONT
2 CONT charge may Arise before I leave this world ivy will is that my sons
2 CONT
2 CONT and my daughters & their heirs shall pay their equal parts and shares
2 CONT
2 CONT of my debts and charges after my decease and my daughters Sarah
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah, Ann & Martha & the heirs of Abigail shall have fourty six
2 CONT
2 CONT pounds apiece with what they have already have to be paid as money out
2 CONT
