2 CONC settler] and Mary Dover, was born at Windsor, Connecticut, September 1, 1639, and was married May 19, 1661, to Mary, daughter of Edward Griswold, who was born October 3, 1644; he died 1719.  They had twelve children.  The eldest, 
2 CONC [1] Timothy, who married Martha Crowe, November 4, 1686, removed to Hebron, Connecticut about 1690, and erected a log house on the farm now occupied by Frederick P. Bissell, about one mile south of Hebron Green.  William Shipman o
2 CONC f Saybrook and he were the first two permanent settlers of Hebron, and he serbed as the first town clerk; he died September 28, 1729.  [2] Joseph is mentioned later. [3] William born February 4, 1668 at Windsor, married, first Abi
2 CONC gail Mudge, December 7, 1690, who died April 24, 1705, and second Ruther Barber, April 18, 1706.  [4] Cornelius, born April 26, 1671, married Sarah Mansfiled, November 2, 1704.  [5] Mary, born August 14, 1673, died March 23, 1690.
