2 CONT * [http://www.americanancestors.org/databases/new-england-historical-and-genealogical-register/image/?volumeId=11586&pageName=227&rId=245474685 ''Record of Marriages and Births, in Windsor, CT''], Edited by Samuel H. Parsons, Esq.
2 CONC , NEHGR Vol 5 (1851) page 230* Repository: The New England Historical and Genealogical Register. Boston, MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1847-. (Online database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogi
2 CONC cal Society, 2001-2013.) 
2 CONT *Oliver Seymour Phelps and Andrew Tinkey Servin, The Phelps Family of America and Their English Ancestors : With Copies of Wills, Deeds, Letters, and Other Interesting Papers, Coats of Arms and Valuable Records, Volume I, pp. 84-8
2 CONC 6, 93-97 (Eagle Publishing Co., Pittsfield 1899). ''Copy available at'' https://archive.org/details/phelpsfamilyofam01phel. (Confirming birth date of 1 Sep 1639, marriage to Mary Griswold, transcribed probate and military records,
2 CONC  and listing children)
2 CONT * Source: <span id='S-682020243'>S-682020243</span> Repository: [[#R-1145277326]] Title:  Ancestry Family Trees Publication:  Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com.  Original data:  Family Tree files submitted by Ances
2 CONC try members.   Page:  Ancestry Family Tree Data:  Text:  http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=80656302&pid=819 
2 CONT
2 CONT : See also:
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/historyofsimsbur00phel#page/13/mode/1up ''History of Simsbury''], page 13. ::  NOTE: Timothy Phelps was born at Windsor, Connecticut, and not at Simsbury. Timothy's father William resided at Windsor, 
2 CONC and died there.Timothy's older brother Joseph Phelps, baptized 13 Nov 1628 at Crewkerne, England, was among the first settlers granted land at Simsbury, which was in 1667. They all received grants of meadow lands bordering on the 
2 CONC Connecticut River. <ref>''History of Simsbury'', page 13</ref> Simsbury was an outgrowth of unregulated farming beyond Windsor, and was organized much later, about 1667.  [[Dellinger-332|Dellinger-332]]
2 CONT
