1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''Poquonock''' is a neighborhood under the city governance of Windsor. '''It began''' as an independent settlement, which [https://greenerpasture.com/Places/Details/27 GreenerPasture.com] affirms:
2 CONT >"Pooquonoc, or Pequannock, a post-village of Hartford county, Connecticut, on the N. side of Farmington river, about 12 miles N. by E. from Hartford. It contains 2 cotton mills; also a paper mill, said to be the largest in New En
2 CONC gland."
2 CONT >(Ken Shelley, Granby, CT – 30 Aug 2023)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:''' Wheeler, Richard Anson. 1900. “The Phelps Family.” In ''History of the Town of Stonington, County of New London, Connecticut, from Its First Settlement in 1649 to 1900'', 537–39. New London, Connecticut, USA: Press o
2 CONC f the Day Publishing Company. Available at: [https://archive.org/details/historytownston00wheegoog/page/537/mode/1up?view=theater '''Archive.org].'''— A complete transcription of Phelps pages from this source appears at bottom of 
2 CONC this Overview.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=122946396
2 CONT
2 CONT http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr03/rr03_420.htm#P3842
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Timothy Phelps
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''from''' John Sibun's book ''Our Town's Heritage 1708-1958 Hebron, Connecticut'', published by Douglas Library, Hebron, CT, 1975: 
2 CONT >"The first white men to settle in town were Timothy Phelps and William Shipman, who arrived in Hebron from Windsor in June 1704. The area, then a wilderness, was used by the Indians as a hunting ground, and the few white men who 
2 CONC knew of its existence passed through to other locations. The first two houses were located along Route 85 south of today's center. Approximately on what is now the Hilding driveway, Shipman built his homestead and Phelps construct
2 CONC ed his home across the road on the land now owned by the Porter family. It is possible they worked on their property during the summer months only for the first two years, and returned to their families in Windsor when winter set 
2 CONC in."
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy moved with his younger brother Nathaniel to Hebron in 1690. Hebron was incorporated in 1708, and Timothy was one of the first selectmen. Another brother Joseph moved there later.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 4 Nov 1686 when Timothy was 23, he married '''Martha Crow''' (3257) , daughter of '''Christopher Crow''' (-11 Dec 1680) & '''Mary Burr''' (918) (14 Jan 1641-aft 1715).93 Born ca 1670 in Hartford, CT. Martha died in Hebron, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha was 14 in May 1684. 93
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Their children include:'''
2 CONT >'''1.'''  10609 i.  Sarah Phelps (Died soon) (20 Dec 1687-10 Jul 1688)  
2 CONT >'''2.'''  10610 ii.  Timothy Phelps (Died soon) (29 Jan 1688/9-Feb 1688/9)  
2 CONT >'''3.'''  10611 iii.  Martha Phelps (29 Oct 1690-)  
2 CONT >'''4.''' 10612 iv.  Timothy Phelps (29 Jan 1692/3-28 Sep 1768)  
2 CONT >'''5.'''  10613 v.  Noah Phelps (23 Jan 1693/4-1794)  
2 CONT >'''6.'''  10614 vi.  Cornelius Phelps (5 Mar 1698-16 Aug 1760)  
2 CONT >'''7.'''  10615 vii.  Charles Phelps (26 Jul 1702-18 Oct 1787)  
2 CONT >'''8.'''  10616 viii.  Asahel Phelps (ca 1704-18 Oct 1787)  
2 CONT >'''9.'''  10617 ix.  Hannah Phelps (25 Dec 1706-) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ====Sources
2 CONT '''1.''' page 576. ''New England Marriages prior to 1700'' by Clarence Almon Torrey.
2 CONT '''2.''' ''Commemorative Biographical Record of Tolland and Windham Counties Connecticut''. J H Beers & Co. 1906. page 530: Timothy Phelps married Martha Crowe 4 November 1686, removed to Hebron, Connecticut about 1690, and erecte
2 CONC d a log house on the farm now occupied by Frederick P. Bissell, about one mile south of Hebron Green.  William shipman of Saybrook and he were the first two permanent settlers of Hebron, and he served as the first town clerk; he d
2 CONC ied September 28, 1729. 
2 CONT '''3.''' Page 114. ''Family Directly Descended from all the Royal Families in Europe [491 to 1932]'' by Mrs. [Oscar Herbert] Elizabeth M. Leach Rixford,  Genealogical Publishing Co.
2 CONT '''4'''. Page 204 ''Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut'' Lucius Barnes Barbour, Genealogical Publishing Co, INC  1977
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Birth'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary & Timothy Phelps' son Timothy Phelps, born Windsor, Connecticut, on 01 Nov 1663<ref>"Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F74D-YYV : 11 February 2018
2 CONC ), Timothy Phelps, 01 Nov 1663; citing ; FHL microfilm unknown.</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Phelps resided in Windsor, Ct., up to 1690, when with his younger brother Nathaniel, then unmarried, he removed to Hebron, Ct., though that town was not incorporated till 1708. He was one of the first selectmen on its organiza
2 CONC tion. His brother Joseph removed there later. Mr. Phelps died in Hebron, Ct.
2 CONT
2 CONT >====Sources
2 CONT * '''Welles, Edwin.''' ''Births, Marriages,and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield, and Entered in the Early Land Records of the Colony of Connecticut | Births, Marriages, and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Winds
2 CONC or, and Fairfield'' (Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co., 1898) 
2 CONT * '''Google Books:''' [https://books.google.com/books?id=0woWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA17 Page 17]* 
2 CONT * Phelps, Oliver. ''Space:The Phelps Family of America and Their English Ancestors'' (Eagle Pub. Co., Pittsfield, Mass., 1899).
2 CONT * Dewey, Adalbert M., ed. 1898. “Josiah the First: Branch of Josiah.” In The Life of George Dewey, Rear Admiral, U.S.N., and Dewey Family History. Westfield, Massachusetts, USA.: Dewey Publishing. Available at: [https://archive.or
2 CONC g/details/lifeofgeorgedewe00dewe/page/395/mode/1up?view=theater&q= Archive.org].
2 CONT * ''Biographical Record of Tolland and Windham Counties, Connecticut''], Available at: [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/6556/images/GenRef-Tolland-Windham-000551?pId=551 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT * ''American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI)'', Available at: [https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/1066271:3599?ssrc=pt&tid=174604283&pid=132395969666 Ancestry.com]
2 CONT * ''Connecticut, U.S., Compiled Census and Census Substitutes Index, 1790-1890''], Available at: [https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/2440757:3537?ssrc=pt&tid=174604283&pid=132395969666 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT * ''U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applications, 1889-1970'', Available at: [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/2204/images/32596_242492-00137?pId=1153048 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT
