2 CONT
2 CONT >====Complete Phelps Pages transcribe from:
2 CONT >Wheeler, Richard Anson. 1900. “The Phelps Family.” In ''History of the Town of Stonington, County of New London, Connecticut, from Its First Settlement in 1649 to 1900'', 537–39. New London, Connecticut, USA: Press of the Day Pub
2 CONC lishing Company. Available at: [https://archive.org/details/historytownston00wheegoog/page/537/mode/1up?view=theater '''Archive.org].'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''PHELPS FAMILY'''
2 CONT
2 CONT We learn from the annals of Dorchester, Mass., that William Phelps, the emigrant ancestor of the Phelps family of New England, came to this country in the good ship "Mary and John" in 1630, with one hundred and forty passengers; m
2 CONC ost of them were constituent members of the church formed in Plymouth, England, in 1629. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On reaching this country, they transplated their church in Dorchester in 1630, where they continued to reside until 1635, when the Rev. John Warham and a large majority of the church migrated overland to the Connecticut River, and
2 CONC  formed the town of Windsor, in Connecticut, and translated their church there. Mr. Phelps and wife were prominently active, not only in reorganizing the church, but also in establishing a social centre for their new town. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Later on Mr. Phelps rose to prominence and eminence, and was repeatedly chosen Deputy to the General Court, and held other important official positions.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He m. 1st,''' in England, ——, name and date of marriage not recorded; she d. in Windsor, Conn. 
2 CONT '''He m. his second wife''' in Windsor, Mary Dover, an Englishwoman, in 1638; she d. Nov. 27, 1675. 
2 CONT '''He d.''' July 14, 1672.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BY FIRST MARRIAGE:
2 CONT 2 WILLIAM, b. ——.
2 CONT 3 SAMUEL, b. ——.
2 CONT 4 NATHANIEL, b. ——.
2 CONT 5 JOSEPH, b. ——.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BY SECOND MARRIAGE:
2 CONT 6 TIMOTHY, b. at Windsor, Conn., Sept. 1, 1639, m. Mary Griswold.
2 CONT 7 MARY, b. at Windsor, Conn., May 2, 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Timothy Phelps (No. 6)''' m. Mary, daughter of Edward Griswold, May. 19, 1661. He d. in 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT 8 TIMOTHY, b. Nov. 1, 1668, m. Martha Crow.
2 CONT 9 JOSEPH, b. Sept. 27, 1666.
2 CONT 10 WILLIAM, b. Feb. 4, 1668.
2 CONT 11 CORNELIUS, b. April 26, 1671.
2 CONT 12 MARY, b. Aug. 14, 1673.
2 CONT 13 BAMUEL, b. Jan. 29, 1675.
2 CONT 14 NATHANIEL, b. Jan. 7, 1677.
2 CONT 15 SARAH, b. Dec. 27, 1679.
2 CONT 16 ABIGAIL, b. June 5, 1682.
2 CONT 17 HANNAH, b. Aug. 4, 1684.
2 CONT 18 ANN, b. Oct. 2, 1886.
2 CONT 19 MARTHA, b. Nov. 12, 1668.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Timothy Phelps (No. 8)''' m. Martha Crow, Nov. 4, 1686. He removed from Windsor, Conn, to Hebron, Conn., in 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN: 
2 CONT 20 MARTHA, b. Oct. 28, 1690.
2 CONT 21 TIMOTHY, b. Jan. 29,1683.
2 CONT 28 NOAH, b. Jan. 23, 1694.
2 CONT 23 CORNELIUS, b. March 5, 1698.
2 CONT 24 CHARLES, b. July 6, 1702, m. Hepzibeth Stiles.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charles Phelps (No. 24)''' m. Hepzibeth Stiles, cousin of President Stiles of Yale College in 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT 26 ZERUIAH, b. April 3, 1729.
2 CONT 27 CHARLES, b. Sept. 28, 1732, m. Hannah Denison; 2d, Sally Swan.
2 CONT 28 ASHBEL, b. April 28, 1743.
2 CONT 29 BETHUEL, b. April 25, 1744.
2 CONT 30 JAMES, b. May 29, 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dr. Charles Phelps (No. 27)''' came from Hebron, Conn., and took up his abode in Stonington, now North Stonington, where he built him a residence, near the foot of Cosatuc Hill. He after- wards removed to Stonington, where he s
2 CONC pent the remainder of his life. He was one of the leading physicians of his day and generation, holding the office of Judge of Probate of the town and other offices. He m. 1st, Hannah Denison (No. 175), that family, Nov. 10, 1757;
2 CONC  she d. Sept. 10, 1795, aged 59 yrs. He m. 2d, Sally Swan (No. 93), that family, Feb. 14, 1795. He d. Jan. 11, 1808, aged 76 yrs. His wife survived him and m. 2d, George Hubbard, Esq., Sept. 7, 1809.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BY FIRST MARRIAGE: 
2 CONT 31 WILLIAM, b. Sept. 26, 1758, d. June 10, 1788.
2 CONT 32 HANNAH, b. Dec. 15, 1760, m. Andrew Huntington In 1777.
2 CONT 33 CHARLES, b. Feb. 28, 1768, m. Elizabeth Smith.
2 CONT 34 HEPZIBAH, b. May 13, 1765, I . Ephraim Williams Dec. 28, 1787 (No. 218), that tamily.
2 CONT 35 MARTHA (Patty), b. - , 1787, m. Frederick Allen, d. 1794.
2 CONT 36 JOSEPH D., b. May 16, 1769, m. Hannah Babcock.
2 CONT 37 NANCY or ANN, b. May 8, 1772, m. Nathaniel Palmer Nov. 11, 1790 (No. 357), that family; she d. 1791.
2 CONT 38 JOHN, b. July 8, 1774, d. Oct. 16, 1775.
2 CONT 39 JONATHAN, b. Oct. 30, 1779, m. Nancy or Ann Brown.
2 CONT 40 STILES, b. J u n e 20, 1781, m. Elizabeth or Betsey Denison Brown.
2 CONT 41 POLLY, D. June 10, 1785, d. unmarried in 1847.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BY SECOND MARRIAGE:
2 CONT 42 SWAN WILLIAM, b. June 24, 1797, d. Feb. 7, 1799.
2 CONT 43 BENJAMIN FRANKLIN, b. Dec. 2, 1800, m. Ameabel Wallace.
2 CONT 4 SALLY, b. Oct. 28, 1802, d. 1820.
2 CONT 45 CHARLES E., b. 1808, d. 1888.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joseph D. Phelps (No. 36)''' m. Hannah Babcock (No. 156, that family, Sept. 30, 1792. She d. Aug. 9, 1809; he d. Nov. 2, 1842.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT 46 HANNAH, b. June 1798, m. Thomas Noyes Jan. 28, 1818 (No. 225), that family.
2 CONT 47 CHARLES H., b. 1795, m. Ann R. Hammond.
2 CONT 48 MARTHA, b. 1797, d. Oct. 20, 1834.
2 CONT 49 NANCY, b. March 20, 1800, m. James W. Noyes (No. 824), that family.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charles Phelps (No. 33)''' m. Elizabeth Smith. He d. Dec. 2, 1791- 
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT 50 ELIZABETH, b. ——.
2 CONT 51 ANNE, b. ——.
2 CONT 52 ANN, b. ——. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jonathan Phelps (No. 39)''' m. Nancy or Ann Brown Jan. 26, 1804 (No. 94), Rev. Chad Brown family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN:
2 CONT 68 PELEG B., b. Jan. 23, 1806, m. —— Broadhead. 
2 CONT 64 CHARLES T., b. Dec. 4, 1806, d. 1832.
2 CONT 66 GEORGE ALFRED, b. Oct 14, 1808, d. unmarried. 66 FRANCIS R.. b. Nov. 8, 1810, d. 1831.
2 CONT 67 JAMES H.. b. Oct 29, 1813.
2 CONT 68 JOSEPH D.. b. Sept 12, 1818. 
2 CONT 69 WILLIAM WALLACE, b. Dec. 10, 1821.
2 CONT 60 NANCY B., b. June 14, 1824. 
2 CONT 61 SARAH W., b. Feb. 18, 1827, m. Mortimer Williams.
2 CONT 62 EDMUND, b. Feb. 18, 1827.
2 CONT 63 MARTHA, b. Dec. 18, 1828, m. Gurdon Gates of Mystic, Conn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stiles Phelps (No. 40)''' m. Elizabeth or Betsey Denison Brown Jan. 29, 1781 (No. 90), Rev. Chad Brown family.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN: 
2 CONT 64 HORACE STILES, b. 1801. 
2 CONT 65 WILLIAM BROWN, b. 1803.
2 CONT 66 ELIZABETH DENISON, b. 1805, m. William Woodbridge (No. 80), that family; he d. 1869.
2 CONT 67 CHARLES HENRY, b. 1807, d. 1808.
2 CONT 68 HARRIET BISHOP, b. 1813, m. Arthur Merritt; 2d, Charles Hill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Charles H. Phelps (No. 47)''' m. Ann R. Hammond of Newport, R. I., July 28, 1824 (No. 503), Palmer family. He was lost on the burning steamer Lexington in Long Island Sound Jan. 13, 1840, by which the poor lost a friend and a l
2 CONC iberal benefactor. His widow m. for her second husband Rev. Erskine Edwards, pastor of the Second Congregational Church, Stonington, Conn., and became the parents of two daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BY FIRST MARRIAGE: 
2 CONT 69 ANN HAMMOND, b. 1826, d. 1828. 
2 CONT 70 SARAH, b. 1829, d. 1829.
2 CONT 71 MARTHA ELLEN, b. 1831, m. Eugene Edwards July 11, 1849. 
2 CONT 72 CHARLES, b. in 1834, <L 1888.
2 CONT 73 EMILY, b. In 1836, d. 1838.
2 CONT 74 ERSKINE MASON, b. In 1839, m. Anna E. Wilder Oct. 26, 1864. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''NOTE.—Hon. Erskine Phelps (No. 74)''', Phelps family, and Hon. Samuel D. Babcock (No. 215), Babcock family, whose ancestors were some of the most prominent planters of Stonington, Conn., feeling a deep Interest In the happiness
2 CONC  and welfare of the Inhabitants of their native town, and realising the importance of having a library building for the depository of a Public Library of books and magazines, that may be received from any one or purchased by contr
2 CONC ibutions for that purpose, kindly and generously erected a building in 1899, costing twenty thousand dollars, on Wadawannuck square in Stonington borough, the grounds having been generously given by the descendants of Samuel F. De
2 CONC nison, for the library building.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Timothy W46 PHELPS II 1663–1737 and Martha CROW Phelps 1670–1775
2 CONT Married Anna PINNEY 1712–1789 on 9 Nov 1731 in Hebron, Hartford Co (later Tolland Co.), Connecticut.
