2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Samuel Phelps was born on 29 Jan 1675 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut to [[Phelps-53|Timothy Phelps]] and[[Griswold-32|Mary (Griswold) Phelps]].<ref name="Phelps and Servin Book">Oliver Seymour Phelps and Andrew Tinkey Servin, '
2 CONC 'The Phelps Family of America and Their English Ancestors : With Copies of Wills, Deeds, Letters, and Other Interesting Papers, Coats of Arms and Valuable Records,'' Volume I, pp. 96, 110 (Eagle Publishing Co., Pittsfield 1899). '
2 CONC 'Copy available at'' https://archive.org/details/phelpsfamilyofam01phel.</ref> Samuel married [[Eno-80 | Abigail Eno]] on 03 JUN 1706.<ref name ="Phelps and Servin Book"/> The couple had several children, all born in Windsor, incl
2 CONC uding at least:<ref name = "Phelps and Servin Book"/>
2 CONT * [[Phelps-1700 | Abigail (Phelps) Grant]]* [[Phelps-1716 | Samuel Phelps, Jr.]] (b. 5 Apr 1708/10, m. Ruth Phelps, m2. Damarius Gilender)
2 CONT * James Phelps (b. 12 Aug 1713, d. 3 Apr 1718)
2 CONT * [[Phelps-1717|Matthew Phelps]] (b. 25-28 Jan 1715, unmarried)
2 CONT * [[Phelps-1718|Mary Phelps]] (b. 20 Feb 1718, d. 15 Mar 1718)
2 CONT * [[Phelps-1719|James Phelps]] (b. 23 Jan 1720, m. Hester Fowler)* [[Phelps-1720|Tabatha (Phelps) Moore]] (b. 18 Jan 1721, m. 21 Feb 1739 to Ebenezer Moore (son of William Moore), d. bef 1749, no children
2 CONT * [[Phelps-777|Joshua Phelps]] (b. 13 Oct 1729, m. Hannah Birge)
2 CONT * [[Phelps-1721|Hezekiah Phelps]] (m. Lydia Griswold). Samuel passed away in Windsor, before 1749.<ref name ="Phelps and Servin Book"/> His will was dated October 26, 1741, and the probate recordmentions Samuel, James, Hezekiah, J
2 CONC oshua, and Abigail.<ref name = "Probate Record">Charles William Manwaring, Probate Record for Samuel Phelps - Will and Invt. in Vol XIV, Page 66, A Digest of the Early Connecticut Probate Records: Hartford District, 1729-1750, Vol
2 CONC ume III (R.S. Peck & Co., Hartford 1906), page 322-323. Copy available at https://archive.org/details/digestofearlycon03manw and https://books.google.com/books?id=0P8LAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA323&lpg=PA323&dq=%22jehiel+grant%22+torrington&so
2 CONC urce=bl&ots=xRkWs7K18I&sig=roRowdbaANBCGpjxcCl1vPO3zHI&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwib_Ped5LnOAhVLzGMKHfsdD9YQ6AEIKjAD#v=onepage&q=%22jehiel%20grant%22%20torrington&f=false.</ref> Samuel supposedly bequeathed his "green riding hood, blac
2 CONC k silk crape gown and black taffeta apron" to his daughter Abigail and the remainder of his personal apparel to his four sons,<ref name ="Phelps and Servin Book"/> but his will does not contain this language.<ref name = "Probate R
2 CONC ecord"/> Samuel's will was proven in December 1741, which means he likely passed away around that time.<ref name = "Probate Record"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Notes/Questions ===The original profile has DOB as 227 jan 1677, which is within 8 monthsof a siblings DOB, and a DOD of 23 Sep 1746. S4 has a different DOB and DOD, though the other information is consistent with the original
2 CONC  profile. Since there is a gap in the DOB of siblings Mary and Nathaniel, this profile's DOB has been changed to that of S4.
