2 CONC America and their English ancestors Vol I. Second generation, image 106 Timothy was born in Augustor by 1 September 1639 in Windsor, Connecticut. His parents were William Phelps and his second wife, Ann Dover. He married Mary Gris
2 CONC wold inWindsor 19 March 1661. Mary was the daughter of Edward Griswold of Killingworth, CT. She was born in Windsor and baptized 13 Oct 1644. She died some years before her husband. Mr. Phelps resided in Windsor, CT,on the old hom
2 CONC estead, on land purchased by his father from the Indians. In a deposition taken in Hartford, CT, Mar 1682-3, he is mentioned as son of William, about forty-two years old. In May 1696, the soldiers at Windsor chose Timothy Phelps a
2 CONC s their Captain. He was appointed aLieutenant in 1709 and served under Col. William Whiting, in Capt. Matthew Allyn's Co., in 1607, in the Queen Anne War. He died in 1719. His will, dated 2nd May, 1717, mentions all his children, 
