1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (f/g) Abigail Holcomb Bissell
2 CONT *Birth: 	Jan. 6, 1639 - Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Death: 	Aug. 17, 1688 - Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Holcomb, dau. of Thomas Holcomb and his wife Elizabeth, bapt. of record at Windsor, Conn. on Jan. 6, 1638/9 and d. at Windsor Aug. 17, 1688.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 11, 1658 at Windsor, Conn., Abigail m. of record Samuel Bissell, s. of John Bissell and his unnamed first wife, b. on an unknown date likely in England. He d. testate at Windsor, Conn. Dec. 3, 1700. They had ten children b
2 CONC . at Windsor who are outlined in their father's memorial. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *  Thomas Holcomb (1609 - 1657)
2 CONT *  Elizabeth Holcomb Eno (1617 - 1679) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *  Samuel Bissell (____ - 1700)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *  John Bissell (1659 - 1683)
2 CONT *  Abigail Bissell Eno (1661 - 1728)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Unknown 
2 CONT *Created by: Don Blauvelt
2 CONT *Record added: Apr 14, 2010
2 CONT *Find A Grave Memorial# 51098277 -tcd
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Abigail Holcomb, dau. of Thomas Holcomb and his wife Elizabeth, bapt. of record at Windsor, Conn. Jan. 6, 1638/9 and d. in Windsor Aug. 17, 1688.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like her husband Abigail has no known gravestone, but it is assumed she is interred in Windsor's Palisado Cemetery, which was the only cemetery that existed in Windsor at the time of her death.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 11, 1658 in Windsor, Conn., Abigail m. of record Samuel Bissell, s. of John Bissell and his unnamed first wife, b. circa 1636 likely in England. He d. testate in Windsor, Conn. Dec. 3, 1700. They had ten children b. in Win
2 CONC dsor outlined in their father's memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/51098277/abigail-bissell
2 CONT
2 CONT +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Bissell formerly Holcomb Born 6 Jan 1639 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Daughter of Thomas Holcombe and Elizabeth (Unknown) Eno  Sister of Elizabeth (Holcombe) Ellsworth, Mary (Holcomb) Griswold, Joshua Holcomb, Sarah H
2 CONC olcomb, Benajah Holcomb I, Deborah Holcomb, Nathaniel Holcombe, Deborah (Holcombe) Birge and Jonathan Holcombe  Wife of Samuel Bissell — married 11 Jun 1658 in Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut  Descendants  Mother of John Bis
2 CONC sell, Deborah Bissell, Abigail (Bissell) Eno, Jacob Bissell, Mary (Bissell) Pettibone, Samuel Bissell, Benajah Bissell, Joshua Bissell, Elizabeth (Bissell) Root, Deborah (Bissell) Pettibone and Hannah (Bissell) Phelps  Died 17 Aug
2 CONC  1688 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Abigail Holcombe, daughter of Thomas and Elizabeth (Unknown) Holcombe, was born on 6 Jan., 1638/9 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut.[1]  Name: Abigail Holcombe[2][3][4]  Birth: 6 Jan 1638/9 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONC [5][6]  Baptism: 6 JAN 1638/9 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut[6]  Marriage: 11 JUN 1658 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut[7][4]  Husband: Samuel Bissell[4]  Wife: Abigail Holcombe  Children: all born at Windsor, Hartford County, Conne
2 CONC cticut[4]  Child: John Bissell, born 5 April 1569  Child: Abigail Bissell born 6 July 1661  Child: Jacob Bissell born 28 Mary 1664  Child: Mary Bissell born 15 Sept 1666  Child: Samuel Bissell born 11 Jan 1668  Child: Benajah Biss
2 CONC ell born 30 June 1671  Child: Elizabeth Bissell born 4 Jan 1677  Child: Deborah Bissell born 29 Oct 1679  Death: 17 AUG 1688 Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut[8]  Burial: AUG 1688 Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes  Birth - Windsor (not Granby)  Granby was not settled until eighty-five years after the birth of Abigail Holcombe, and sixty-five years after the death of Thomas Holcombe. He never lived there. Abigail could not pos
2 CONC sibly have been born there.  Robert Charles Anderson in his Great Migration series shows Abigail Holcombe born at Windsor, Connecticut, 6 Jan 1638/9, citing Connecticut Vital Records, also found in transcription at NEHGR Vol 5 pag
2 CONC e 63. Abigail's father, Thomas Holcombe, did not purchase his land at Poquonock until 1640, and possibly did not move there until 1649 when other settlers joined him. Poquonock is on the west side of the Farmington River in Windso
2 CONC r, Connecticut. Thomas Holcombe never lived in Granby, Connecticut, which was not settled until 1723, when it was a part of Simsbury, Connecticut which was not settled until 1664.  The FamilySearch card showing Abigail Holcombe bo
2 CONC rn in Granby[9] is derived from a large tombstone erected in Granby by descendants of Thomas Holcombe. The many errors on it have been propagated over time and multiplied over the Internet. See Genealogical Vandalism - Thomas Holc
2 CONC ombe's Tombstone, by George McCracken, in The American Genealogist Vol. 44, p. 58, January 1968, for details. McCracken, F.A.S.G., F.G.S.P., also documents Holcombe descendants in TAG Vol. 57. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources  ↑ The Great Migration and The Great Migration Begins, New England, 1620-1635, by Robert Charles Anderson, page 966 ↑ The Great Migration and The Great Migration Begins, New England, 1620-1635, by Robert Charles Anderson, 
2 CONC page 966 ↑ Source: #S001408 ↑ 4.0 4.1 4.2 4.3 Records of Marriages and Births in the Town of Windsor, Connecticut, NEHGR Vol 5 (1851), page 63 ↑ Source: #S366 page 63 Windsor Births and Marriages (Accessed 14 July, 2017) ↑ 6.0 6.1
2 CONC  The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Vol. I-III] by Robert Charles Anderson, page 966 ↑ The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Vol. I-III, by Robert Charles Anderson, page 966
2 CONC  ↑ Connecticut Marriages, 1640-1939." Database with images. FamilySearch. http://FamilySearch.org : 11 April 2017. Connecticut State Library, Hartford. ↑ Source: #S237 Page: https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F7WJ-J2Q Accesse
2 CONC d 5 July, 2017 Certainty of Data: 3 The Great Migration and The Great Migration Begins, New England, 1620-1635, by Robert Charles Anderson, (Ancestry.com Operations, Inc., Provo, UT, 2013) Abigail Holcombe page 966 
2 CONT
2 CONT Records of Marriages and Births in the Town of Windsor, Connecticut, The New England Historical and Genealogical Register: NEHGR Vol 5 (1851), page 63  Tom Bredehoft, Pettibone Registry (see Sharp-661). Click the Changes tab for t
2 CONC he details of edits by Tom and others.  Source: S237 Title: Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906, database Publisher: FamilySearch.org [Note: Birth location (Granby) is error, see Research Notes, and actual transcription
2 CONC  of Windsor records in NEHGR Vol 5] 
2 CONT
