1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob Bissell  Born 28 Mar 1664 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Ancestors  Son of Samuel Bissell and Abigail (Holcomb) Bissell  Brother of John Bissell, Deborah Bissell, Abigail (Bissell) Eno, Mary (Bissell) Pett
2 CONC ibone, Samuel Bissell, Benajah Bissell, Joshua Bissell, Elizabeth (Bissell) Root, Deborah (Bissell) Pettibone and Hannah (Bissell) Phelps  Husband of Mary (Gillette) Buell — married before 1689 in Windsor, Hartford County, Connect
2 CONC icut  Descendants  Father of Mary (Bissell) Warren and Jacob Bissell Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Bissell was born on 28 March, 1664 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT.[1][2][3]  He married Mary Gillett before 1689 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. [1][4]  In 1694 Jacob was listed for taxes as was his father, Samuel Bissell, Sen. 
2 CONC in Simsbury, CT[5]  He died on 1 August, 1694 at Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT.[1][6][3] Estate was inventoried on 23 August 1694[6] Final settlement after appeals was settled on 6 Oct., 1712 giving the estate to brothers and sisters
2 CONC  of Jacob Bissell[6]  Sources  ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 Stu Wison's Tree Publisher: Rootsweb Source cited: The American Genealogist 54 <1978): 65-765, 150-158.  ↑ #S246 Page: https://play.google.com/books/reader?id=MQe21xly7AsC&printsec=fron
2 CONC tcover&output=reader&hl=en&pg=GBS.PA63 Accessed 6 July 2017
2 CONT
