2 CONT Sarah Wait Phelps BIRTH	1 Aug 1779 Connecticut, USA DEATH	29 Jan 1860 (aged 80) Wisconsin, USA BURIAL	 New Lisbon City Cemetery New Lisbon, Juneau County, Wisconsin, USA MEMORIAL ID	28234242 · View Source MEMORIAL PHOTOS 1 FLOWERS
2 CONC  3 Daughter of Gen Benjamin Wait & his wife Lois Gilbert. Gen Wait is a Revolutionary War Patriot and one of the founders of the town of Waitsfield, Vermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT History of the town of Waitsfield, Vermont, 1782-1908 : with family genealogies Boston, Mass.: G.E. Littlefield, Matt Bushnell Jones 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT AARON(6) PHELPS (Bissell,(5) Solomon,(4) Nathaniel,(3) Timothy,(2) William(1)) was born in Hebron, Conn., Apr. 15, 1778; lived for many years in W., but rem. in old age to Fountain, Wis., where he died Apr. 30, 1856; selectman, 18
2 CONC 05-6, 1815. He married, Dec. 17, 1797, Sarah, dau. of Benjamin and Lois (Gilbert) Wait, b. abt. 1779; d. Jan. 29, 1860, at Orange, Wis. Children, born in Waitsfield:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. SOLOMON,(7) b. Jan. 7, 1799; d. in Hopkinton, N. H., Nov. 6, 1873; m. Jan. 25, 1829, Betsey Bartlett Gilman. ii. BENJAMIN WAIT, b. Dec. 1, 1801; d. in Durham, Ill.; m. Jan. 1, 1832, Matilda, dau. Jonathan Seaver, b. Aug. 16, 18
2 CONC 09. iii. BISSELL b. Feb. 11, 1804; sett. in Waterloo, Wis.; m. Mar. 6, 1825, Elizabeth Barber of DeKalb, N. Y. iv. AARON, b. Mar. 2, 1806; d. Apr. 23, 1806. v. CHARLES, b. June 18, 1807; d. in Lisbon, Wis., Aug. 26, 1875; m. Aug. 
2 CONC 25, 1833, Ann Parker, dau. Charles and Mary (Russell) Perkins. vi. AARON GILBERT, b. Apr. 21, 1809; d. in Portland, Wis.; m. Feb. 11, 1839, Eliza W. Foster. vii. WATERMAN, b. Mar. 1, 1814; sett. in Hebron, Wis.; m. Oct. 23, 1836, 
2 CONC Mary A. Marble. viii. SOPHRONIA, b. July 13, 1811; m. Oct. 24, 1830, Moses C. Kenyon, of Gouverneur, N. Y. and Portland, Wis.
2 CONT
