2 CONC . (by John Chester, JP) Thomas Avery, both of New London. No vital record exists to state when Charles actually died, and due to the loss of pre-1700 probate records for the New London Probate District, no probate of his estate su
2 CONC rvives. In Donald Lines Jacobus' 1933 published The Bulkeley Family (p. 136), Jacobus claimed Charles died in New London in 1692 and provided the following detail:
