1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Adams, daughter of Eliphalet Adams and Lydia Pygan, married (first) Jonathan Gardner on 13 Nov 1733 and (second) the Honorable John Bulkeley Esq. on 29 Oct 1738 in Colchester. They had the following children r
2 CONC ecorded at Colchester:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Lydia, b. 21 Oct 1739, m. Capt. Robert Latimer on 25 Jun 1761 in New London, CT. One child, Robert, baptized on 19 Dec 1762.
2 CONT 2. Mary, b. 22 May, 1741, d. 1 Jun 1741
2 CONT 3. John, b. 20 May 1742, d. 13 Nov 1742
2 CONT 4. Mary, b. 15 Nov 1743, m. George Buttolph Hurlburt on 13 Oct 1765. George was a 1757 Yale College graduate. No children.
2 CONT 5. Eliphalet, b. 8 Aug 1746, m. 16 Sep 1767 Anna Bulkeley of New London, CT
2 CONT 6. Lucy, b. 2 Aug 1749, m. Capt. John Lamb, a sea captain who gave service at sea during the revolution and died 4 Mar 1804 of a wound received in a shipwreck on the coast of Spain. Lucy was still living on 1 Sep 1807 when she was
2 CONC  granted administration but it is not known when she died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died 24 Jan 1750 in Colchester.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/6949887/mary-bulkeley Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 30 2023, 0:30:41 UTC''
