1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR# [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A016746 A016746]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Buried in Hollenback but name is engraved on ancestor's monument in Linwood Cemetery in Colchester, CT, where there is also a memorial for him. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eliphalet Bulkeley
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel Eliphalet Bulkeley, son of Hon. John Bulkeley and Mary (Adams) Bulkeley. He was a prominent officer in the Connecticut troops in the revolution, a captain of the Colchester company that responded to the Lexington alarm, Ap
2 CONC ril 19, 1775; promoted lieutenant-colonel in May 1780. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 16 September 1767 Anna Bulkeley, of New London, who was his cousin
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT 1. Lydia Ann born 18 May 1768; married Colonel Daniel Watrous
2 CONT 2. Mary Adams born 25 June 1770 married James Worthington 
2 CONT 3. John Charles born 8 August 1772 
2 CONT 4. Patience born December 1774 married Charles Chapman 
2 CONT 5. Jonathan born 8 July 1777 married E. Simons 
2 CONT 6. Pettis born 30 April 1780 
2 CONT 7. Eliphalet born 22 April 1782; died unmarried 
2 CONT 8. Sarah Chauncey born 24 July 1784 married James Bolton
2 CONT 9. Fanny born 6 April 1787 married Henry Lamb
2 CONT 10. Juliana (born 9 May 1789) married Steuben Butler 
2 CONT 11. Orlando born 19 January 1793
