1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Warren, called tobacconist and cardmaker, was an early settler of Exeter, NH, moved to Boston 1668 where he died in July 1677. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first, at Exeter, 21 Oct. 1650, Deborah Wilson (died 26 June 1668). 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Warren married second, at Boston about 1669, Elizabeth (?Royal) (Barlo w) Coombs, widow of John Coombs (died May 1668.)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Warren married third Elizabeth Danson
2 CONT
2 CONT See [TAG 46:132 & TAG 47:17].
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=pavone&id=I15040
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Warren, called tobacconist and cardmaker, was an early settler of Exeter, NH, moved to Boston 1668 where he died in July 1677. He married first, at Exeter, 21 Oct. 1650, Deborah Wilson (died 26 June 1668). 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * John Warren, tobacconist and card maker of Exeter, NH and Boston married first Deborah Wilson, second Elizabeth Combs and third Elizabeth Danson [TAG 46:132 & TAG 47:17]. 
2 CONT * John Warren had 8 children with Deborah, one with Elizabeth (Royall?) and two with Elizabeth Danson. 
2 CONT * He died Jul 1677 in Boston
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
