2 CONT WHITING, WILLIAM SRAncestor #: A124838
2 CONT Service:  CONNECTICUT    Rank(s): PRIVATE
2 CONT Birth:  10-12-1736    WEST HARTFORD HARTFORD CO CONNECTICUT
2 CONT Death:  10-20-1775     WEST HARTFORD HARTFORD CO CONNECTICUT
2 CONT Service Source:  BATES, ROLLS & LISTS OF CT MEN IN THE REV, VOL 8, P 16; JOHNSTON, CT MEN IN THE REV, P 13
2 CONT Service Description:  1) CAPT ABRAHAM SEDGWICK'S CO, HINMAN'S REGT
2 CONT 2) LEX ALARM
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence
2 CONT  1) City: WEST HARTFORD - County: HARTFORD CO - State: CONNECTICUT
2 CONT
2 CONT From Find a Grave https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/57407746/william_lord-whiting
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: Abstract of Graves of Revolutionary Patriots, Vol.4, p. Serial: 11912; Volume: 4
2 CONT
2 CONT William was "of West Hartford" according to Hinman. He served in the Revolutionary War in the summer of 1775 at Ticonderoga, and died that fall at age 39 from an illness contracted while in the service. Mary remained in Hartford d
2 CONC uring the war.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1782 "widow Mary Whiting of Farmington" married Abner Curtis. The couple lived in Farmington, CT, and sold some land, along with son William Whiting, to Jeremiah Wadsworth, Elisha Whiting is witness
