2 CONT
2 CONT Ruby Rose Stofer Phelps BIRTH	4 Feb 1925 Exeter, Fillmore County, Nebraska, USA DEATH	23 Apr 2016 (aged 91) Lincoln, Lancaster County, Nebraska, USA BURIAL	 Carleton Cemetery Carleton, Thayer County, Nebraska, USA MEMORIAL ID	1618
2 CONC 11120 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 1 FLOWERS 0 Ruby Rose (Stofer) Phelps Was born on February 4, 1925, in Exeter, and passed away on April 23, 2016 in Lincoln.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruby was a longtime Thayer County resident having lived in Carleton, Bruning, Davenport, Hebron and Deshler.
2 CONT
2 CONT She retired from the Thayer County Hospital after 40 years of service.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held on April 30, at 10 a.m., at the United Methodist Church in Hebron. Funeral services will be held at 11 a.m. at the church.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial will be in the Carleton Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Good Shepherd Funeral of Omaha is in charge of arrangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hebron Journal-Register, April 27, 2016.
2 CONT ====================
2 CONT Ruby Rose Phelps was born February 4, 1925, in Exeter to John Stofer Jr. and Anna Rose (Elznic) Stofer. She attended school in Carleton and worked on the family farm while at home. She passed away at Bryan East in Lincoln.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruby married Durward Phelps from Palisade on January 4, 1945. To this union three children were born-- Sharla, Rodney (Nancy) and Dennie (Rogene).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruby was a waitress in Little Rock, Ar., when Durward was in the service. After returning from the service, they farmed in Thayer County. She always had a large garden and houseplants. Flowerbeds surrounded the house every year.
2 CONT
2 CONT When the children were raised, she started her third career as a nurse aide at Anabelle's Rest Home. Later, she moved on to Thayer County Hospital where she worked for 40 years until her retirement.
2 CONT
2 CONT When her father could no longer care for her brother, Ruby and Durward welcomed Bernard into their home in 1975. Ruby, Durward and Bernard used to enjoy going to flea markets, craft fairs and threshing bees around the area until h
2 CONC ealth issues stopped them from driving.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Durward's passing in 2007, they remained on the farm, helping each other, until health issues brought them to Parkview Haven in June 2014, where they both resided until her passing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruby has six grandchildren, and 8 great-grandchildren. She is also survived by sisters, Darlene Miller, Bernice (Charles) Polage; brother, Bernard Stofer; as well as a host of nieces, nephews, cousins and many friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services for Ruby Rose took place on April 30 at the United Methodist Church in Hebron, Pastor Mark Baldwin officiated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Songs included "If I'd a Knew You Were Coming, I'd A Bake A Cake," "How Great Thou Art," "Hymn of Promise" "In the Garden," "The Old Rugged Cross" and "I"ll See You Again."
2 CONT
2 CONT Pallbearers included Nicholas Stanoscheck, Eric Stanosheck, Jeremy Phelps, Ron, Scott, Patrick and Andrew Phelps. Honorary bearers were the great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nebraska Signal 11 May 2016 page 5A col. 2 & 3.
