1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Florence M. Lauer, dau. of George Lauer and Mary Fischer,  was born Mar. 17, 1914 in Sisseton, South Dakota; married with '''LESLIE WAYNE HARDING''', son of Frederick A. Harding and Nina C. Lewis. He was born Mar. 
2 CONC 24, 1907 in Bayard, Iowa. He died Dec. 20, 1983 in Sioux Falls, South Dakota; she died there Mar. 18, 2004; both buried at Saint Michael's Cemetery, Sioux Falls, Minnehaha Co., South Dakota.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''FLORENCE M. (Lauer) HARDING'''  ....  Birth:  Mar. 17, 1914  Death:  Mar. 18, 2004 
2 CONT
2 CONT Florence M. Lauer was born on March 17, 1914 in Sisseton, SD, the daughter of George and Mary (Fischer) Lauer. In 1919, she moved to Redwood Falls, MN with her parents. In 1929, they moved back to Sisseton where Florence graduated
2 CONC  from high school. She was employed as a secretary for the AAA Farm Program from 1932-1933. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Florence was married to Les Harding on Dec. 14, 1933. They lived in Sisseton until 1935 when Les accepted the position of County Ag Agent in Minnehaha County. Les died on Dec. 20, 1983. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a member of St. Mary Church, Altar Society group St. Elizabeth Ann, Catholic Daughters of America, Past Grand Regents Club of Catholic Daughters, and Prince of Peace Auxiliary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Grateful for having shared her life are her sons, Stephen (Gerri) Harding, Valley Springs, David (Melanie) Harding, Bethlehem, NH, John Harding, Sioux Falls; daughters, Dorothy Harding, Moab, UT, Linda Harding, Sioux Falls, Elaine
2 CONC  (Glenn) Combs, Owensboro, KY; nine grandchildren, Jeff, Shelli, Christine, Kate, Chad, Mark, Jennifer, Seth, Matthew; five great-grandchildren; sister, Viola Ryan, Hopkins, MN; and several nieces and nephews. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to her husband, one son, Roger, her parents, a brother and two sisters, preceded her in death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Florence thanks you for your support and presence today. An invitation is extended to join them at St. Therese for refreshments and fellowship following the service. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosary & Scripture Service 7:30 pm Sunday, March 21, 2004 Fr. Jim Friedrich, Officiating Rosary led by the Catholic Daughters of America Miller Funeral Home 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mass of Christian Burial 11:00 am Monday, March 22, 2004 St. Therese Catholic Church, Sioux Falls, South Dakota 
2 CONT
2 CONT Interment St. Michael Cemetery, Sioux Falls, South Dakota 
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation begins at 2:00 Sunday with a Rosary at 7:30 at Miller Funeral Home, 507 S. Main. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Miller Funeral Home 507 S. Main Ave. Sioux Falls, SD 57104 605-336-2640 Miller West 6200 W. 41st St. Sioux Falls, SD 57106 605-361-6394 
2 CONT
