2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas is named in his father's will (to receive one shilling), dated
2 CONT 5 Apr 1723 and presented to court 25 Sep 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT From HOPKINS: On Oct. 30, 1707, Thomas Muse, of West'd Co., and John
2 CONT Muse, Jr., of Richmond Co., Va., were granted 265 acres in West'd Co.
2 CONT On Nov. 10, 1711, Nicholas Muse of West'd Co., received a grant of
2 CONT land of 179 acres in West'd Co. on Holling Branch on Great
2 CONT Rappahannock Creek, between the counties of Richmond and West'd.
2 CONT (Northern Neck Grant Book No. 4, p. 60).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note from HOPKINS: Thomas Muse left a will dated Mar. 12, 1729, pro.
2 CONT June 28, 1732 (W. B. 8, p. 532, West'd Co.). On July 26 1718 (V. 6,
2 CONT p. 318, West'd Co.,), John Muse, Jr., leased to Thomas Muse "part of
2 CONT 200 acres of land which I leased of Col. William FitzHugh for my life
2 CONT and my wife, Ann Muse's life, Jan. 17, 1712." On May 26, 1725 (V. 8,
2 CONT p. 118, West'd Co.), Thomas Muse made a deed of gift to sons Thomas
2 CONT and Christopher Muse "the 50 acres now in possession of my oldest son,
2 CONT John Muse, being the same land which I purchased of my brother, John
2 CONT Muse, dec'd July 28, 1718--subj. to the provisions contained in the
2 CONT lease from Col. Wm. FitzHugh, dec'd, to my brother John Muse."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note from SOUTHERN LEGACY: In his will, as dated above, All known
2 CONT children and a granddaughter Mary George are named. The only
2 CONT information to date on his daughters is based on his last will and
2 CONT testament. Will of Thomas Muse Sr, 12 Mar 1729, probated 28 Jun 1732
2 CONT Westmoreland Co., VA, Will & Deeds Bk 8, 1723-1738, part 2, p. 175.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Christy Flynn lists the date of death as 28 June 1736. Greg Howearth
2 CONT lists 12 Mar 1729.)
