1 NOTE Proven son by fathers will (see Thomas Muse).
2 CONT Only John Jr., James and Daniel are proven children of John by his will dated 11 October , 1770, recorded in Westmoreland Co., Virginia
2 CONT Richard is proven through a property deed recorded Westmoreland Co., Virginia where a Henry Fitzba ugh of Stafford Co. Va. leases land to John Muse, planter and his son Richard Muse for the te rm of their natural lives. Also Richa
2 CONC rds Grand Father Richard Sanford in his will dated Marc h 27, 1733, filed Westmoreland Co. left a Negro girl to his daughter Mary Muse and after he r death to her two sons, Richard and John.
2 CONT Ann Muse and Thomas are identified byWest and Fauntleroy as proven children. In "Southe rn Legacy" the refer to a Ann Hall that named Ann and Elizabeth, daughters of John Jr. in he r will.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Lorene Rambo.ged]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes from SOUTHERN LEGACY:
2 CONT In 1725 John's father conveyed to Thomas Muse Jr. 50 acres of land
2 CONT "now in the tenure of my oldest son, John Muse." In 1732 John and his
2 CONT son Richard leased land from Henry FitzHugh. Several deeds are listed
2 CONT proving John and his wife Mary Sanford. (See will of Richard Sanford,
2 CONT 1757).
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of John Muse, 11 Oct 1770, proved 27 Nov 1770, Westmoreland Co.,
2 CONT Va; names Richard and Daniel Muse executors and names "my two sons,
2 CONT Daniel and James Muse and my beloved wife, Eleanor Muse."
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary probably had children unidentified to date. Proven by a
2 CONT deed of gift from their grandfather Richard Sanford are Richard and
2 CONT John. Thomas and Ann are named by other researchers; this source does
2 CONT not think they are proven. John and his second wife Eleanor had two
2 CONT sons proven by John's will. One source suggests that John had 13
2 CONT children.
2 CONT (Jeanne Muse listed date of death as Oct, 1770. Gary Howearth lists
2 CONT Nov, 1770. Rev. McLeod says 11 Oct. 1770.)
