2 CONT Notes  	
2 CONT
2 CONT     ELIZABETH STURMAN (STEWART) MURPHY md. 3rd. about 1712, Thomas Muse, Sr., whose last wife she was. He was the son of John Muse, Sr. b. Eng., 1633, d. West'd. County, Virginia., 1723. In his will dated April 5, 1723: pro. Sept.
2 CONC  25, 1723, he names children: Thomas Muse; dau. Jane Pritchett; dau. Anne Willson; dau. Mary Quesenberry; dau-in-law Anne Muse, wid. of his son John Muse, to whom he leaves his whole estate, with the exception of the legacies to t
2 CONC he children named. Beside the son John, dec'd., there was a son Nicholas 1st, also dec'd, who md. Mary, dau. of John Elliott, Sr., and his wife, Sarah Foxall.
2 CONT     By her marriage to Thomas Muse, Sr., Elizabeth Sturman-Stewart-Murphy had:
2 CONT     (5) Nicholas Muse, 2nd. b. 1713 or 1714, d. 1778, md. 1st, by Nov. 30 1732, Anne (Cullom) Finch, twice a wid. Her first husband was Mark Cullom, Jr., a great-gr. son of Henry Brookes. Her 2nd husband was John Finch, Sr. By Ann
2 CONC , Nicholas Muse 2nd had:
2 CONT     a. Nicholas Muse 3rd, b. about 1733, d. 1768, unmd. and intestate.
2 CONT     b. Mary Muse, b. , md. prior to 1760, Thomas Randall, and left issue.
2 CONT     c. Elizabeth Muse, twin sister to Mary, md. John Washington, who d. 1790, his wife having pre-deceased him. No issue.
2 CONT     d. Anne Muse, youngest dau., b. before 1745, d. 1816, md. April 3, 1766, Lieut. Thomas Washington, bro. to John above. Left issue.
2 CONT     Anne (Cullom-Finch) Muse sued her husband for separate maintenence in 1742, but when the case was called, no one appeared. The case was dropped. She was still living with him in 1745.
2 CONT
2 CONT     (5) Nicholas Muse 2nd, and his wife, Ann, probably had other children, who died. After the death of Anne (Cullum-Finch) Muse, in 1747, or '48, Nicholas md. Nov. 27,1749, in Richmond County, at the home of Henry Asbury, Elizabe
2 CONC th Asbury, dau. of Thos. Asbury and his wife, Anne Walker (Wright) Asbury. By this second marriage, Nicholas had:
2 CONT     e. Jeremiah Muse, b. 1750, d. 1810, unmd.
2 CONT     f. Penelope Muse, b. about 1752, d. unmd. (?) after 1790.
2 CONT     g. Walker Muse, Maj. in the Rev., b. about 1754, d. 1812,
2 CONT     md. Susannah Muse, .wid. of Capt. James Muse. Left one dau.
2 CONT     h. Jesse Muse, b. after 1755, d. 1783, served in Va. Navy during the Rev. Unmd.
2 CONT     ===
2 CONT     1734-1736 Westmoreland County, Virginia Deeds & Will Book 8, Part 5 [Antient Press]; Page 259a
2 CONT     (On margin: ELIZABETH MUSE's Will)
2 CONT     Item. I give and bequeath to my Son, WILLIAM, one Cow, one Calf a pot and passel] and all the Corn I lent him in the year 1733, And the 2 hhds. Corn yt: JOHN MUSE owes me and 30 shillings cash, one table
2 CONT     Item. I give and bequeath to my Son, NICHOLAS MUSE, one Cow, one Earlin, one Stear one blanks, one Shoates, one pail
2 CONT     Item I give and bequeath to my Son, DANIELL, one bed, one pair of sheets, one pair of pillors one pair of blanketts one Chest, 2 basons, 2 dishes, fore plates, one silk rugg.
2 CONT     Item. I give and bequeath to my dafter, ANN CHILTON, one spice morter and pessell one ladle for her nateral life and after her death to ( ) CHILTON;
2 CONT     hem. I give and bequeath to my Dafter, ANN CHILTON, one washing toob
2 CONT     Item. I give and bequeath to my Dafter, ELIZABETH BARNET one bell mettle skillet during her life and after her death to BARBRY ( ? MINER) for ever.
2 CONT     Item. I give and bequeath to my Grand Dafter, MARY MINER my sadell an Bridle and speening wheel.
2 CONT     Item. I give to my two Dafters and MARY MINOR all my wearing cloaths equally devided between them.
2 CONT     1735 May Court. MARY HARVY, DANIEL MUSE, MARY STOWERS sworn touching this Writing as the Will of ELIZA: MUSE
2 CONT     Westmorland ss. This day CHRISTOPHER MUSE made Oath before me that the within Writing was writ by THOMAS MUSE by the request of ELIZABETH MUSE and that it was her desire her Estate should be devided among her Children after he
2 CONC r death as it is within mentioned and that she was in her parfectt senses, Given under my hand this 29th of March 1735
2 CONT     JNO: ELLIOTT
2 CONT     Westmorland ss. At a Court held for the said County the 27th day of May 1735
2 CONT     This Writing purporting to be the Last Will and Testament of ELIZABETH MUSE, deced., was presented into Court by NICHOLAS MUSE and upon the examination of MARY HARVEY, DANIEL MUSE and MARY STOWERS, touching their knowledge of 
2 CONC the said Writing (they being sworn thereto) and by the Deposition of CHRISTOPHER MUSE, it is the opinion of this Court that the same is a good Will tho not signed by the Decedent or dated witnesses or any Exr, therein named. And t
2 CONC hereupon the same is admitted to Record; And upon the mocon of NICHOLAS MUSE, one of the Sons of the said Decedent, he was admitted to make Oath thereto & upon his performing what is usual in such cases, & giving EDWARD MUSE for h
2 CONC is security according to Law, Certificate is granted him for obtaining Letters of Administration thereupon with ye said Will annexed in due in rm Test G TURBERVILE. C. C. W.
2 CONT     Recorded the llth day of June 1735, pr. G. T., C. C. W,
2 CONT     ===
2 CONT     Wills of Westmoreland County, Virginia
2 CONT     MUSE, ELIZABETH, 29 March 1735; 27 May 1735. Sons William, Nicholas and Daniel; daus. Anne Chilton, Elizabeth Barnett, Barbara Minor; granddau Mary Minor and Lettice Chilton.
2 CONT     ===
2 CONT     1734-1736 Westmoreland County, Virginia Deeds & Will Book 8, Part 5 [Antient Press]; Page 288
2 CONT     N THE NAME OF GOD, Amen. I CHRISTOPHER MUSE of Washington Parish in the County of Westmorland being very much afflicted & calling to mind the uncertainty of this life, doe prepare make and declare this my Last Will and Testame
2 CONC nt in manner & forme following; Imprimis. I resign and recommend my immortal Soul in the handes of my blessed Saviour & Redeemer Christ Jesus in firme hope & beliefe through his merytorious death & passion to receive pardon and fo
2 CONC rgiveness of all my sins and a joyfull resurrection at the last day to eternal bliss & happiness and for what worldly Estate God in the abundance of his mercy hath been pleased to allow me, I dispose thereof through his permition 
2 CONC in manner and forme following;
2 CONT     Item. It is my will and desire that my Brother, NICHOLAS MUSE, have my Plantation with the land theirs unto belonging, it being that piece or parcell of land which my Father purchased of my Uncle, JOHN MUSE, as by Deeds of Lea
2 CONC se and Release dated the twenty eighth day of July in the year one thousand seven hundred & eighteen, the which was given me by my Father by Deed of Gift acknowledged in Westmorlend County Court the twenty sixth day of March in ye
2 CONC  year one thousand seven hundred and twenty five for and during the space of seventeen years he paying the annual'. rent reserved in the Deed and at the end of the seventeenth year, then I give my Land with the appurtenances their
2 CONC  unto belonging to my Cosen, THOMAS MUSE, Son of my deced. Brother, THOMAS MUSE, to hold to him and the heirs of his body forever under the several Rents limittations & provisos as are mentioned & containined in the said Deed.
2 CONT     Item. I give to my Cozen, THOMAS MUSE, Son of my deced. Brother, THOMAS MUSE, and to the heirs of his body lawfully begotten all my moveable Estate be it of what nature or quallity soever, but my will is that if my Cozen, THOM
2 CONC AS MUSE, shall depart this life before he attains to the age of twenty one years or without heirs of his body lawfully begotten, then and in such case I give and bequeath to my Brother, NICHOLAS MUSE, his Son. NICHOLAS, my Land wi
2 CONC th the appurtenances theire unto belonging & all my moveable Estate.
2 CONT     And I do hereby appoint my Loving Brother, NICHOLAS MUSE, whole and sole Executor of this my Last Will and Testament and doe hereby revoke all former & other Wills by me att any time made & doe declare this & none other to be 
2 CONC taken for my Last Will and Testament; In Witness whereof I have hereutno sett my hand & affixed my seale this 18th day of January 1734
2 CONT     BENJA. WADDEY, CHRISTOPHER MUSE
2 CONT     THOMAS his mark WODLSTON
2 CONT     Westmorland ss. At a Court held for the said County the 29th day of June 1736
2 CONT     This Last Will and Testament of CHRISTOPHER MUSE, deceased, was presented into Court by NICHOLAS MUSE, his Executor, who made Oath thereto and being proved by the Oath of THOMAS WODLSTON, one of the witnesses thereto, is admit
2 CONC ted to Record; And upon the lmocon of the said Executor and his performing what is usual in such cases, Certificate is granted him for obtaining a Probate thereof in due form
2 CONT     Test, G. TURBERVILE, C. C. W,
2 CONT     Recorded the 13th day of July 1736, pr. G. T., C, C. W.
2 CONT     ===
2 CONT     1736-1738 Westmoreland County, Virginia Deeds & Will Book 8, Part 6 [Antient Press]; Page 328a
2 CONT     THIS INDENTURE made between HENRY FITZHUGH of STAFFORD County, Gent., of one part and NICHOLAS MUSE of Westmorland County of other part; Witnesseth that this Fifth day of May Anno Domini one thousand seven hundred and thirty s
2 CONC ix that HENRY FITZHUGH path and by these presents doth demise sett and to farm lett one tract of land containing One hundred and seventy six acres (where one WILLIAM GLADDIN lived) and bounded, Begining at the mouth of a Branch ma
2 CONC keing into the Great Swamp at a Gumb & runing thence to a Black Gum upon a Hill, thence North 19d. W: 80 po: to a Pohickory standing in or near the line of JOHN MUSE's, thence North 32d. West 196 po. to a red Oak Stump upon a Bran
2 CONC ch, thence along the Branch S: 55d. W: 80 po: to the Great Swamp, thence along the Swamp to the begining in consideration of the rents and duties hereafter mentioned and during the space of the natural life of said NICHOLAS MUSE a
2 CONC nd ANN MUSE his Wife & NICHOLAS MUSE his Son; To have and to hold to NICHOLAS MUSE and his heirs during the term aforesaid together with all houses and appurtenances to the land belonging; paying therefore yearly during the term u
2 CONC nto HENRY FITZHUGH his heirs upon the Plantation & from thence Rolling to a convenient Rolling House on the water side at the Feast of St. Luke being the eighteenth day of October the neat sum of eight hundred pounds of tobacco an
2 CONC d cask to contain the same; as also every year four hens, capons or pullets; and NICHOLAS MUSE will not at any time make over his Lease or Right to any person without the leave of HENRY FITZHUGH and paying one years rent for the s
2 CONC ame and all assignments made contrary to these artickulars shall be void; In Witness whereof the parties above mentioned have hereunto interchangeable set their hands & seals the day & year above written
2 CONT     Sign'd Seald & deliver'd in presents of HENRY FITZHUGH
2 CONT     ROBT. VAULX
2 CONT     DANIEL NEALE
2 CONT     Westmorland ss, At a Court held for the said County the 31st day of January 1737 HENRY FITZHUGH, Esqr., personally acknowledged this Deed of Lease of Land to NICHOLAS MUSE to be his proper act and deed which at the instance of
2 CONC  the said MUSE is admitted to Record
2 CONT     Test G. TURBERVILE, C. C. W.
2 CONT     Recorded the 15th day of February 1737, pr. G. T., C. C. W.
2 CONT
2 CONT
