1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Unknown Origin
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine North was born c. 1628, probably in England. His birth details and his parents are not known. When married to Dorothy, he was living at Ware Parish, Gloucester County, Colony of Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date is an estimate, based on other known dates, such as marriage of a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine married to Dorothy (Unknown). After Augustine's death, Dorothy married, as her 2nd, to Daniel Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 July 1706, an action for "Trover and Conversion" was brought by Daniel Henry & Dorothy, his wife, late Dorothy North, extrx. of last will & testament of Augustine North, decd., agst. Peter Ransone, falls ye writt not being l
2 CONC awfully executed" (Essex County Records Order Book 1703-8, Page 254)."
2 CONT
2 CONT Property and Positions
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated 20 Sep 1652, a patent was assigned (certainly in error of transcription) to Augustine "Horth" and that it was originally granted to William Dudley and "by him assigned." The description was "350 acs. including five pine Isla
2 CONC nds, running N.N.E. by Mr. Thomas Curtis &c."
2 CONT
2 CONT In another publication, the same property (?) is described as, "20 September 1652 - Patent assigned to Augustine North, 400 acres "On W'ward side of North R. of Mockack Bay, on head of Ginger Crk. and including Five Pine Island." 
2 CONC Was originally assigned to William Dudley but due to mistake re-assigned to A. North."
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Augustine North died by 1692, probably at Ware Parish, Gloucester County, Colony of Virginia (p 185).
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy write her will on 19 Dec 1709 and it was probated on 10 Jan 1709/10 at Essex County, Colony of Virginia (p 187).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT They had a daughter, Dorothy North who first married Richard Awbrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Torrence (using wills and deeds as evidence), Augustine and Dorothy North had three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy North; m 1) Richard Awbrey, 2) Thomas Gouldman, 3) Peter Ransone
2 CONT Rose North; m 1) Lee/Ley, 2) Unknown Curtis
2 CONT Mary North; m Thomas Leftwich
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 1.5 Torrence, Clayton, (1927) "Winston of Virginia" Richmond: Whittet & Shepperson HathiTrust.org (Pages 183-87).
2 CONT ↑ Trover is an action to recover damages for property converted by another. Conversion is an equitable action to seek return of the property. Both are still in use today.
2 CONT ↑ Nugent, Nell Marion, (1934) Cavaliers and Pioneers: Abstracts of Virginia Land Patents and Grants, 1623-1800, 1st ed. Richmond: Dietz Print Co., Archive.org (Page 423).
2 CONT ↑ Records of Colonial Gloucester County, Virginia [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2006. Original data: Mason, Polly Cary. Records of Colonial Gloucester County, Virginia. Vol. I and II. Baltimore, 
2 CONC MD, USA: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2000. p 28
2 CONT ↑ Awbrey, Jon A. published Aubrey/Awbrey - Dominion and Decline in 2007
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.colonial-settlers-md-va.us/getperson.php?personID=I129256&tree=tree1
2 CONT Va. Colonial Abstracts Vol 1
