3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 DEC 1709
2 ADDR
3 CITY St. Ann's Parish
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Origin
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy's birth date and place are unknown. Her parents and maiden name are also unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date of "about 1645" is based on c. 1669 birth of eldest daughter Dorothy (North) Awbrey Gouldman Ransone profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy married twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married by c. 1668, as her 1st, to Augustine North.
2 CONT She married between 7 Nov 1698 and 10 Mar 1706, as her 2nd, to Daniel Henry, of St.Anne's Parish, Essex County (p 184). Dorothy removed from Ware Parish, Gloucester County to St. Anne's Parish, Essex County, probably at the time s
2 CONC he married Daniel Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Property
2 CONT
2 CONT Essex County court records show that on 7 November 1698, "Dorothy North of Ware Parish, Gloucester County, widow," purchased for £125 from John Hawkins, of Essex County, some "627 acres, 16 perches" (p 183).
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 July 1706, an action of "trover [?] and Conversion" was brought by Daniel Henry & Dorothy, his wife, late Dorothy North, extrx. of last will & testament of Augustine North, decd., agst. Peter Ransone, falls ye writt not bein
2 CONC g lawfully executed" (Essex County Records Order Book 1703-8, Page 254)."
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel died by 10 April 1708, when Dorothy petitioned the Essex County court for administration of her late husband's estate (p 184).
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 March 1706/7, Daniel Henry and Dorothy his wife late Dorothy North, late of Gloucester County now of St. Ann's widow, to William Thompson of St. Ann's Parish. for 200 Sterling. 627 Acres and 16 perches in St. Ann's Parish bound
2 CONC ed as by patent granted Thomas Hawkins 19 Feb 1662 and belonging to Daniel Henry and Dorothy his wife by a deed of feoffment 7 Nov 1698 made by John Hawkins only son and heir of Thomas Hawkins unto the said Dorthy North Widow.
2 CONT Daniel Henry
2 CONT Dorothy (H) Henry
2 CONT Wit John Butler, Garrett Neaill, Joseph Winge.
2 CONT 10 March 1706/7 Acknowledged by Daniel Henry and Dorothy his wife.
2 CONT Death and Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy wrote her will on 19 Dec 1709 and it was probated on 10 Jan 1709/10 at Essex County, Colony of Virginia (p 187).
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Mrs. Dorothy Henry of St. Ann's Parish, Essex County, mentions "my three granddaughters ... Elizabeth Gouldman, Mary Leftwich, Dorothy Avery." Also mentions "my two daughters Rose Curtis and Dorothy Ransome."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Dorothy and Augustine North:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy North; m 1) Richard Awbrey, 2) Thomas Gouldman, 3) Peter Ransone
2 CONT Rose North; m 1) Lee/Ley, 2) Unknown Curtis
2 CONT Mary North; m Thomas Leftwich
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT What was the relationship between Dorothy (here profiled) and John and Thomas Hawkins?
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 1.5 1.6 1.7 Torrence, Clayton, (1927) "Winston of Virginia" Richmond: Whittet & Shepperson HathiTrust.org (Pages 183-87).
2 CONT ↑ Dorothy MNU North Early Colonial Settlers of Southern Maryland and Virginia's Northern Neck Counties, citing 1706-1718 Essex County Deed & Will Book. by John Frederick Dorman, Page 369-71.
2 CONT ↑ Ariciu, Janet, (23 Dec 2016) "Henry Awbrey." Janet Ariciu family Bush, accessed 25 Feb 2017.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * "Leftwich-Turner families of Virginia and their connections by Hopkins, Walter Lee, 1889-"  https://archive.org/details/leftwichturnerfa00hopk/page/12/mode/2up page 12
