2 CONT WILLS OF Westmoreland County, Virginia 1654-1800 BY AUGUSTA B. FOTHERGILL: Pg 39
2 CONT ROSIER, JOHN, 28 September 1705; 31 October 1705. To Nathaniel Pope clerk of Stafford and practitioner at law all land which I formerly gave to my daughter Elizabeth Leftwich, 130 acres for which he to pay exx. 3500 lbs. of tobacc
2 CONC o ; rest to wife Mary Rozier, exx.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT PATENT BOOK, 2, 1666/1695, BOOK 6, pp. 211/212:
2 CONT
2 CONT 5200 JOHN ASHTON, Will probated Stafford County, 26 Jan. 1682(83), and willed land he inherited from Col. Peter Ashton to James Ashton, their brother. He was formerly of Lowth (Louth). John Ashton's wife's name was Elizabeth and C
2 CONC apt. John Ashton, probably a son. JAMES ASHTON, died, Stafford County, formerly of Kirby-Underwood, Lincolnshire. His Will, dated 18 Aug. 1686 (87), names RICHARD ELKINS, John Ashton, son of Charles Ashton, Justice of Peace, and C
2 CONC ol. Peter Ashton, Sheriff of Northumberland Co.,, Virginia. James Ashton had Godchildren: RICHARD ELKIN, Sarah Mottershead, Miss Rosier, daughter of John Rosier, and Elizabeth Sebastian, and willed RICHARD ELKINS 100 acres of his 
2 CONC land. The Estate "Chatterton" King George, Virginia., now belongs to a Tayloe family.
2 CONT ===
