1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=11750748 Martha Strange was a daughter of Maj. Robert Strange and his wife Elizabeth Early of Bedford Co., Virginia. Her brother, T. Early Strange, was publishe
2 CONC r of The Greensborough Patriot newspaper for a time. Some accounts give her middle initial as C., some as G. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha married Jeduthan Harper Lindsay (1806-1881) on 2 Nov. 1830. He was a son of Col. Robert Lindsay, Jr. (1776-1818) and his wife Letitia Harper (1785-1835, later Mrs. Henry Humphrey). Jed. and his brother Jesse H. Lindsay were
2 CONC  promient in the development of Greensboro, NC. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha and Jed. had eight children: Jesse Harper Lindsay (26 April 1832-18 Sept. 1859), Mary Virginia Lindsay (7 Sept. 1834-5 May 1853), Dr. James  Early Lindsay (22 Sept. 1836-7 Feb. 1892, Surgeon, Confederate Navy, went to Balti
2 CONC more, m. Charlotte Gittings), Robert Henry Lindsay (27 July 1838-4 Nov. 1861, Confederate soldier, died of fever in War), Jeduthan Harper Lindsay, Jr.  (20 March 1840-11 Jan. 1876, Confederate soldier, Co. B, 27th NC), Thomas Stra
2 CONC nge Lindsay (16 Aug. 1843-17 Oct. 1869, Confederate soldier), Ernest Lindsay (24 June 1845-13 Jan. 1902, Confederate soldier,per UNC directory was a banker in St. Joseph, Mo., m. Mehetable "Hettie" McDonald), Dr.  Edward O. Lindsa
2 CONC y (1849-1888, m. Elizabeth).* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/11750748/martha-c_-lindsay Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 7 2020, 1:48:37 UTC''
