2 CONC LjE2OTQwMjI0NDUuNTEuMC4w*_ga_LMK6K2LSJH*OGQxZGMxNDItOTBhMS00NDdlLWE3YjUtZTljOGI2NDRlNWVmLjguMS4xNjk0MDIyNDQ1LjAuMC4w
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Stephenson was born 1834 and almost reached her 100th years. She was born in Kentucky and was 16 years old when her parents left their farm and brought a dozen slaves and two covered wagons to Missouri settling near Gallatin 
2 CONC in Daviess County. It took them a month to come, but it was a wonderful trip especially to the youngsters, with outdoor meals and new sights everyday. After they built their new home,she saw Indians, but they were what people call
2 CONC ed "friendly Indians". 
2 CONT During the Civil War, the Thornhills sided with the South. One day a body of Union Troops passed by their home. Her brother promptly showed his mother's training by yelling "Hurrah for Jeff Davis". The soldiers quickly scared him 
2 CONC into silence.
