2 CONT Source: THE MURPHY FAMILY OF BEDFORD COUNTY VIRGINIA by Kenneth W. Dobyns, 637 South 25th St., Arlington, VA 22202, (703) 684-8514
2 CONT
2 CONT William Lemuel Murphy enlisted in 1863 in Co. G., 28th Reg, Hunton's Brigade, The Patty Layne Rifles, CSA. He served 1 1/2 years. This was a Bedford Co. unit, organized April 1861. When William Lemuel Murphy was a teenager, he los
2 CONC t an eye as a result of a practical joke. His older brother (which one is not recorded, and indeed the record does not show that he had an older brother) had recently married and was living with his bride at an isolated house. You
2 CONC ng William went one night and made noises outside the house as if he were a burglar to scare his brother. He succeeded. His brother came out and shot at the shadowy figure and hit young William in the eye. Because of the effect on
2 CONC  his appearance, in later life he would not allow his picture to be taken. There was apparently one tintype made, but it was subsequently lost.
