1 TITL Deacon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Job Drake was born on 15 June 1651 at Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut.1,2 He was baptized on 15 April 1655 at Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut.3.  Job Drake died on 19 April 1733 at Windsor, Hartford Co., Conn
2 CONC ecticut.7,8 Also known as Dea. Job Drake.7,8
2 CONT
2 CONT * parents: John Drake b. c 1625, d. b 31 Oct 1689 & Hannah Moore b. s 1628, d. 16 Feb 1685/86
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT # He married Elizabeth Alvord, daughter of Benedict Alvord and Jane Newton, at Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut, on 20 March 1671 Married by Capt. Newbery.4,5,6. 6 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Will==
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was dated on 14 March 1732 Job Drake of Windsor. To wife Elizabeth use of all estate during her natural life. To son Jeremiah that lot on which I now dwell which I had of my father, and that which I have which was Joshua'
2 CONC s will's to him forever, he allowign to his mother what above is given to her. To daughter Rebeckah use of the new house during the time she shall remain single. To daughters Elizabeth and Rebeckah and to granddaughter Eunice Drak
2 CONC e, my lott that bounds north on the land of Thomas Stoughton and south on the land of Samuel Moore, to be divided amongst them share and share alike. To daughter Rebeckah, twenty-five pounds out of the estate to be taken as goods 
2 CONC or cattle. To grandson Jonathan Drake my right, interest, share and part of a land called the Equivalent land. Son Jeremiah to have all lands in Windsor not disposed of above. Right, share and interest in lands called the Eastern 
2 CONC Lands to daughter Elizabeth, daughter Rebeckah, son Jeremiah and granddaughter Eunice Drake. After the death of my wife Elizabeth, all of my moveable estate not disposed of to pay debts to be distributed between my three children 
2 CONC and my granddaughter Eunice Drake. Appoints son Jeremiah Drake and "son" Joseph Rockwell as executors. Witnessed by Timothy Edwards, Job Drake, L.S., Joseph Drake, Eliakim Cook. Recorded July 1733.10
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~brouwergenealogydata/Drake/p31.htm#i6831
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John II & Hannah (Moore) Drake
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Alvord - parents of at least four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Job resided on East Windsor Hill, opposite Old Cemetery was a tailor and first deacon of the 2nd Church of Christ in Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Edwards Cemetery, South Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
