2 CONT John Drake 1616–1688/1689
2 CONT Hannah Moore (Drake) 1627–1686</line><line /><line>Additional Support:
2 CONT The Descendants of John Porter of Windsor, Conn. 1635-9, Volume 1 by G.W. Ball pg 118</line><line /><line>John Higley came from England, and was an early settler at Windsor, Conn. Representative, judge of county court. He married 
2 CONC November 9, 1671, Hannah Drake.</line><line /><line>John Drake, with his wife Elizabeth, came from England in the fleet with Winthrop in 1629. Removed to Windsor, Conn., where he was accidentally killed August 17, 1659. Mrs. Eliza
2 CONC beth Drake died October 7, 1681.</line><line /><line>Second Generation, John Drake, born in England, married November 30, 1648, Hannah Moore, born in England, daughter of John Moore, a deacon of the church, gathered in England, wh
2 CONC o came to Dorchester, Mass., May 30, 1630; removed to Windsor in 1635, and died April 18, 1677. John Drake died 1680. She died February 15, 1686.</line><line /><line>New England Families, Genealogical and Memorial: Volume 2 by Wil
2 CONC liam Richard Cutter Pg 1094
2 CONT DRAKE
2 CONT (X) John (8), son of John (7) Drake, was the first settler at Simsbury, Connecticut, but resided at Windsor until 1659, perhaps longer. He died July 7, 1688, aged thirty-nine years, according to his gravestone, though the town rec
2 CONC ords give it July 9, 1689. He married, November 30, 1648, Hannah Moore, who died February 16.. 1686, daughter of Deacon John Moore.
2 CONT Children: Mindwell, November 10. 1671;</line><line /><line>12/12/20
