2 CONC AKE.
2 CONT
2 CONT v MARY2 (Mercy), baptised 12 Oct 1651; d Suffield CT 29 Mar 1725; m/1 Windsor (“both of Windsor”) 8 Jul 1669 John GILLETT, b Windsor 5 Oct 1644, d there 1682, son of Jonathan and Mary (DOLBERE) GILLETT, the Emigrant. Mary m/2 14 J
2 CONC un 1683 Capt. George NORTON of Suffield, baptised Salem MA 28 Mar 1641, d 15 Nov 1696, son of
2 CONT
2 CONT George and Mary (MACHIAS) NORTON; (George was first married to Sarah ‑‑‑, who d in 1682). After her parents' death when she was 9 years old, Mercy was placed by the court (4 Feb 1662/3) in the home of Walter FYLER until age 18, un
2 CONC less she were married sooner (which she was). [~ Corresp:Betty Simonson; IGI:CT; CT Hist Soc:LBBarbour Manuscripts; CT Hist Soc:Fellows Gen; CT Hist Soc:Norton Manujscript; Barbour Index; Stiles:Windsor; Windsor Hist.Soc:DFAW ~]
