1 NAME John /Barber/
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Barber
2 _MARNM Barber
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Springfield Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1642
2 ADDR
3 CITY Windsor
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 BAPM
2 DATE 24 JUL 1642
2 ADDR
3 CITY Windsor
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 JAN 1712
2 ADDR
3 CITY Suffield
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 OCCU b. 7/24/1642 @ findagrave.com
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=39208249
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barber was the son of Thomas and Joan Barber and the husband of Bathsheba Coggin. He served in King Philip's War and participated in Turner's Falls Fight under Capt. William Turner. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John lived in Windsor on the original homestead, which was left to him by his father.  When he moved his family to Springfield MA in 1671 the Windsor home was transferred to his brother Samuel.  John lived in Springfield from 1671
2 CONC  to 1684, during which time he served as Deacon in Christ Church in Springfield, and also as one of the Springfield Selectmen.
2 CONT
2 CONT The year 1684 found the restless John and his family in Suffield CT, where he remained for a time, after which he returned to finish his days in Springfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Suffix: Deacon
2 CONT
2 CONT 1642 - Jul 24 was baptized in Windsor
2 CONT
2 CONT 1662 - June 6, his father's will left the homestead to him & sister, Sarah
2 CONT
2 CONT 1663 - Sep 2, married Bathsheba Coggins in Springfield, CT; 5 children
2 CONT
2 CONT 1664 - his sister signed the homestead over to him
2 CONT
2 CONT 1667 - Apr 8, dau Joanna was born
2 CONT
2 CONT 1669 - Jul 14, son John was born
2 CONT
2 CONT 1671 - he transfered his father's home to his brother Samuel and removed to
2 CONT
2 CONT Springfield, CT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1672 - May 29, dau Return was born but died Dec 17 1673
2 CONT
2 CONT 1674 - Feb 4, son Thomas was born
2 CONT
2 CONT 1677 - Feb 13, dau Mary was born
2 CONT
2 CONT 1684 - removed to Suffield; served as a Deacon and selectman
2 CONT
2 CONT 1688 - wife, Bathsheba died
2 CONT
2 CONT 1689 - May 2, married the widow of Thomas Brancroft, Hannah Gardner
2 CONT
2 CONT 1712 - Jan 17, Deacon John died
2 CONT
2 CONT 1712 - Feb, his will was proven
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference:
2 CONT
2 CONT THE BARBER GENEALOGY
2 CONT
2 CONT DESCENDANTS OF THOMAS BARBER OF WINDSOR, CT; page 20-21
2 CONT
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Barber, Sr., son of Thomas of Windsor, and brother of Thomas of Suffield, born 1642, removed to Springfield 1671, to Suffield 1684, was freeman 1681. He was a deacon, also one of the first Selectmen chosen. Married Bathsheba
2 CONC  Coggin of Springfield, 1665, and reared a family of children before his removal to Suffield. He died May 14, 1712. This surname soon after disappears from Suffield records."
2 CONT
2 CONT John and his sister Sarah received distribution of their father Thomas Barber's estate on 6 June, 1662.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1664 his father's place in Windsor was made over to him, which (1671) he transferred to his brother Samuel and removed to Springfield; then (1684) to Suffield, where he was a deacon, also one of the first selectmen; will made 
2 CONC 4 Feb. 1711/12, Sheldon says he d. 14 May, 1712, and that this surname soon after disappears from Suffield. Ch. b. at W. (Old Ch. Rec.)"
2 CONT
2 CONT "JOHN BARBER, Windsor, son of Thomas of Windsor, married Sept. 1663, Bathsheba Coggin, or Cogens, had Joanna, b. 8 Apr. 1667; John, 14 July 1669; removed to Springfield, there had Return, 1672, who died soon; and Mary, 1678; was d
2 CONC eacon and died 27 Jan. 1712."
2 CONT
2 CONT Torrey gives Bathsheba Coggin as John Barber's first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barber is listed as one of the original proprietors of Suffield, with land grants from the committee. He received 14 Sep 1674 fifty acres on Feather Street, and in 1680 sixty acres on Springfield Road. The same work gives him
2 CONC  on the list drafted 9 Mar 1682 of "ye Names of ye Inhabitants of Suffield" and he was chosen Select man on that date. On 6 Apr 1685 John Barber Senr. was "chosen with Ensigne George Norton to treat with ye Major Phychon in order 
2 CONC to ye procuring a Deed of sale of ye Towneship, yt we purchased of him."
2 CONT --------------------
