2 CONT
2 CONT AKA Barber
2 CONT
2 CONT James Barber Died Octr. 1732. Dorchester, Suffolk, Massachusetts[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Barber and Elizabeth Hide were married at Dorchester, Massachusetts on June 23, 1680. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES Barber, of Dorchester, Massachusetts, a tailor, m. about 1683. He died 13 Oct. 1732, aged a. 80. His widow Elizabeth d. 4 Dec. 1739, aged 81.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth born on August 4, 1681. [2]
2 CONT Elizabeth bapt. 18 May 1684; [3]
2 CONT James, 29 May 1687; mentioned in the probate record. [3]
2 CONT Patience, 20 Oct. 1689; [3]
2 CONT Ebenezer, 1 Nov. 1702 (but he may have been b. some yrs.); and d. [3]
2 CONT James Barber, tailor, of Dorchester, died intestate. His wife, Elizabeth, was named administrator, 7 Nov 1732. Inventory 10 Jan 1732/3, which barely covered his debts. The only child mentioned was James Barber Jr. Also mentioned a
2 CONC  Hezekiah Barber, relationship not mentioned.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorchester Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT 1680: James Barbor and Elizabeth Hide were married by the Worshipful Joseph Dudley Esqr. June 23: 80. (p. 24)
2 CONT 1699: Samuel Howard of Bridgewater was married unto Elizabeth Barbor of Dorchester by ye Reverand Mr. Danforth on December ye 27th: 99. (p. 103) unconfirmed lineage
2 CONT Dorchester Births
2 CONT
2 CONT 1681: Elizabeth the daughter of James Barbor was born August 4th: 81. (p. 18)
2 CONT 1684: Experience the daughter of James Barbor was born February 4th: 84. (p. 31)
2 CONT 1687: James the son of James Barbor was born April 8th: 87. (p. 32)
2 CONT 1699: Patiene the daughter of James Barbar was borne Sept. the 17 1689. (p. 34)
2 CONT Dorchester Deaths
2 CONT
2 CONT 1732: James Barber Died Octr. 1732. (p. 135)
2 CONT 1739: Widow Barber, late wife of James Barber died December 1739. (p. 138) [2]
2 CONT Dorchester Burials
2 CONT
2 CONT Here Lyes ye body of Mr James Barber. He died Oct 13 1732 Aged about 80ty years. (p. 179)
2 CONT Here Lyes ye body of Mrs Elizabeth Barber Widow of Mr James Barber. She decd ye 4th of Decr 1739 in ye 81st year of her age. (p. 236) [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
