1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain Noah Barber, ancestor of the Wapping Barbers, came from Windsor, Connecticut. He took the oath of fidelity to the State of Connecticut 1777/78. He died aged 87 years, Buried in Wapping Old Burying Ground. (
2 CONC Vol 1) - Noah Barber, Sergeant, marched from E. Windsor for relief of Boston, April 7, 1775. ( pg 9) - State of Conn. to Capt. Barber, Dr. Sept 9th, 1779 for the use of a team for transporting baggage of his company to New London,
2 CONC  55 miles (pg. 273)
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of CAPTAIN.  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A005890  DAR Ancestor #  A005890]
