1 NOTE {geni:about_me} SOURCES (1)
2 CONT
2 CONT     The Connecticut Barbers, a genealogy of the descendant of Thomas Barber of Windsor, Conn. by Donald S. Barber, pg. 44;
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTES (1) Joel was born of the Bloomfield Church in Windsor, Connecticut and was raised on his great grandfather's farm in Windsor, Connecticut.  At the age of 22 he married Mary Drake, daughter of Enoch Drake and Mary Barber, and
2 CONC  they had nine children. All of these children were born in Harwinton, Connecticut.  Joel Barber and his wife, Mary Drake, were also second cousins once removed. Connecticut staunchly supported the patriot cause in the Revolutiona
2 CONC ry War because the people had enjoyed comparative freedom from the British crown for man years.  The colony began to prepare for war more than a year before the "shot heard found the world" was fired at Lexington, Massachusetts. J
2 CONC oel Barber is listed in the National Register of the SAR.  He was in Captain Mill's Company of Militia in the Revolution and a private in Enos's 1st Connecticut Regiment.  For his service, Joel Barber was eventually awarded a gran
2 CONC t of land in Linesville, Crawford, Pennsylvania or the adjacent town of Conneaut in the Western Reserve where his son, Eijah later lived in 1840. CITING THIS RECORD The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, "Pedigree Resour
2 CONC ce File," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:ST82-7MY : accessed 2016-02-23), entry for Joel /Barber/. PEDIGREE RESOURCE FILE Person Count 5,110
2 CONT
2 CONT Submission ID MMQ6-2HL
