1 NAME Abraham /Post/
2 GIVN Abraham
2 SURN Post
2 _MARNM Post
2 NICK Lieut. Dea. Abraham Post Sr.
1 NAME Lt. Abraham Post
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1640
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1690
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hebron
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lieut. Dea. Abraham Post Sr.=
2 CONT * BIRTH 1640 Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * OCCUPATION merchant
2 CONT * SERVICE 1680 Commissioned a Lieutenant of the Saybrook Fort
2 CONT * DEATH 1694 (aged 53–54) Old Saybrook, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Burial Details Unknown
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 84881421 photos added by Krista James
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Abraham Post was born in Hartford, Hartford County, Connecticut circa 1640. Abraham died circa 1691 in Saybrook, CT, at age unknown. He married twice. He married Lydia Buckland. Lydia was the daughter of William Buckland and Mary 
2 CONC Bosworth. Lydia died before 1701 at age unknown. He married Mary Jordan circa 1663. Mary was born circa 1640. Mary was the daughter of John Jordan and Ann Bishop. Mary died March 23, 1684/1685 in Saybrook, CT, at age 43. He was ma
2 CONC de a freeman in 1665, an ensign two years later, and became a lieutenant of those concerned with land surveying and dealing with the Indians (notably, Uncas, Sachem of the Mohegans). He left real estate valued at over 487 pounds. 
2 CONC His eldest son Stephen recieved 121 pounds, the other children 53 pounds each.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham married Mary Jordan in 1663 and among other children, they had a son, Abraham, born in 1669. Abraham's year of birth is not certain. He may have been born in 1635 or a little earlier.
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT Then we the subscribers measurers of land for the Proprietors of Oyster River Quarter laid out to Deacon Abraham POST ten acres of land in said Quarter in the Township of SayBrook on the east of some land belonging to his son Abra
2 CONC ham on Black Oak Hill and it bounds westerly 48 rods on said land and north 32 rods On Will HOPKINs land and east 46 rods upon land of Nath'll POST & south 38 rod's upon Common land the north westcorner is a Chestnut tree which is
2 CONC  the northeast corner Abraham POSTs Junr land. The north east corner is a heap of stones which is the northwest corner of the said Nath'll land, the south west corner and south east corners are heaps of stones this was laid out to
2 CONC  him the said Deacon POST as part of his last division of thirty acres to the hundred pounds right agreed upon be the Proprietors of said Quarter
2 CONT
2 CONT Laid out by us
2 CONT *Sam'll JONES
2 CONT *Joshua BUSHNELL
2 CONT *Abraham CHALKER
2 CONT
2 CONT Received June 20th 1736 and entered from the orginall
2 CONT *Per. Sam'll WILLARD Register.  [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT I would contend that Abraham must be buried in an unmarked grave in the Cypress Cemetery which is the oldest cemetery in Old Saybrook and has a tradition stating there were unmarked graves for the early settlers.
2 CONT
2 CONT I would propose that Abraham's father and mother are also buried in the Cypress Cemetery in Old Saybrook as they are both known to have died there. Old Saybrook is where the family had moved by 1649.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Stephen Post 1604–1659
2 CONT Elinor Panton Post 1605–1670
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Mary Jordan Post 1643–1683 (m. 1663)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT John Post 1626–1710
2 CONT Katherine Post Chalker Hill 1627–1693
2 CONT Thomas Post 1628–1701
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Stephen Post 1664–1752
2 CONT Ann Post Parmalee 1667 – unknown
2 CONT Abraham Post Jr 1669–1747
2 CONT Daniel Post 1673–1743
2 CONT Jordan Post 1676–1748
2 CONT Ellinor "Eleanor" Post Parker 1682–1740
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
