1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Saybrook Vital Records from Barbour, 1668-1852 - P Transcribed by Coralynn Brown
2 CONT
2 CONT ·Jordan, son Abram, b May 27, 1676 ·Jordon, m Phebe LAY, Nov 17, 1703 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - --
2 CONT
2 CONT Saybrook Land Records Book 3 Page 191
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed from Jordan POST to Abraham POST
2 CONT
2 CONT To all People to whom these presents shall come Greeting &c. Know ye that I Jordan POST of SayBrook in ye County of New London & Colony of Connecticut in New England husbandman for and in Consideration of ye sum of twenty two poun
2 CONC ds Currant money of the said Colony to me in hand before the Insealing hereof well & truly paid by Abraham POST of s'd Say-Brook in ye County & Colony aboves'd husbandman the Receipt whereof I do hereby acknowledge & myself herewi
2 CONC th fully satisfied and contented & thereof and of every part & parcel thereof Do exonerate acquit & Discharge the said Abraham POST his heirs executors & administrators by these presents have granted sold alienated & by these pres
2 CONC ents have given granted sold alienated & by these presents have given granted sold alienated & by these presents Do freely and fully & absolutely give, grant, sell alienate convey & confirm unto him ye said Abraham POST his heirs 
2 CONC & assigns forever a certain parcel or tract of land scituate & lying in said Say-Brook in ye County & Colony abovd's in Oyster river Quarter at a place Commonly called Pond meadow together with part of said meadow butted and bound
2 CONC ed as follows viz: the said land being by estimation Sixteen acres let it be more or less together, a sixth part of the said Pond meadow bounded northerly & southerly upon the JONES's lands Easterly and westerly upon the Common ye
2 CONC  southwest corner is a Rock with a heap of stones about it from these running Northwardly to, then across s'd meadow to a Wallnut tree at the West Corner of said land then Eastwardly to Chestnut tree at ? standing by a ledge of Ro
2 CONC cks thence Southerly to a white Oak tree marked with stones about it from thence westwardly to ye aforesaid Rock & heap of stones
2 CONT
2 CONT To Have & to hold the said granted & bargained Premises with all the appurtaniances & Commodities to ye same belonging or in any ways appertaining to him the said Abrah'h POST his heirs executors administrators & assigns forever b
2 CONC y these presents have given & granted unto ye said Abraham POST his heirs & assigns forever to make use of possess & Injoy s'd Demised premises with all ye appurtainances free and clear & freely & clearly exonerated and Discharged
2 CONC  of an from all and all manner of former & other gifts grants sales leases mortgages with Intails & all other Incumbrances whatsoever furthermore I ye said Jordan POST for me my heirs executors & administrators Do Covenant & Ingag
2 CONC e the above against ye lawfull claims & Demands of any person or persons whatsoever forever hereafter to Warrant Secure & Defend.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness whereof I have hereunto sett my hand & seal this Seventh day of May in ye Eighth year of the Reign of our Sovereign Lord George King of Great Brittain &c & in the year of our Lord God 1722,
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed & Delivered
2 CONT
2 CONT In presents of us Sam'll JONES Jordan POST
2 CONT
2 CONT Jordan POST (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Saybrook ye 8th of May 1722, Then & there personally appeared ye above named Jordan POST & acknowledged the above Instrument to be his act & deed before me.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel TAYLOR Justice of ye peace & Quoram
2 CONT
2 CONT Rec'd ye 29th of May 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Saybrook Land Records Book 3 Page 192
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed from Jordan POST to Abraham POST, Jun'r
2 CONT
2 CONT To all People to whome these presents shall come Greeting &c. Know ye that I Jordan POST of Say-Brook in ye County of New London & Colony of Connecticut in New England Husbandman for & in Consideration of ye sum of Six pounds Curr
2 CONC ant money of ye s'd Colony to me in hand before ye ensealing hereof well & truly paid by Abraham POST Jun'r in ye County & Colony & Town abovs'd Husbandman: ye Rec't whereof I do hereby acknowledge & myself therewith fully satisfi
2 CONC eld & Contented & thereof & of every part & parcel thereof do exonerate acquit and discharge ye s'd Abraham POST his heirs executors and administrators forever by these presents have given granted sold alienated conveyed & Confirm
2 CONC ed & by these presents do freely fully & absolutely give grant sell alienate convey & confirm unto him he said Abraham POST his heirs & assigns forever a certain parcel or tract of land scituate being and lying in the bounds of Sa
2 CONC yBrook in Oyster River Quarter near Pond meadow Containing by estimation ten acres bit it more or less Bounded East upon Abrah'm POST land Southwardly upon Daniell POST's land westwardly upon ye Common & Northwardly upon the commo
2 CONC n the Northwest Corner is a Wallnut Stub with stones about it the North East Corner is a black oake Tree marked with three chops & stones about it,
2 CONT
2 CONT To Have & to hold ye s'd granted bargained Premises with all the appurtenances ?eges & commodities to ye same belonging or in any wise appertaining to him ye said Abraham POST his heirs & assigns forever to his and their only prop
2 CONC er use benefit & behoofe forever & that the said Abraham POST his heirs & assigns shall & may from time to time & at all times forever hereafter by force & vertue of these presents lawfully peaceably & quietly have hold use occupi
2 CONC e possess & Injoy s'd demised & bargained Premises with all ye appurtainances free from all & all manner of former & Other gifts grants sales leases furthermore I ye s'd Jordan POST for me my heirs executors & administrators Do pr
2 CONC omise Covenant & Grant to & with ye said Abrah'm POST that before the ensealing hereof I am ye true sole & lawfull owner of the above bargained premises & am lawfully seized & possessed of ye same in mine own right as a good perfe
2 CONC ct and absolute estate of Inheritance in fee simple & have in myself good Right & full power to sell alienate convey & confirm s'd bargained premises in manner as aboves'd furthermore I ye said Jordan POST for myself my heirs exec
2 CONC utors & administrators do Covenant & Ingage ye above Demised premises to him the said Abraham POST his heirs & assigns against the claims or demands of any person or persons whatsoever forever here after to Warrant Secure & Defend
2 CONC ,
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand & seal this seventh Day of May in the Eighth year of our Sovereign Lord George King of Great Brittain &c Anno Domini 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed & Delivered In presents of Sam'll JONES James JORDAN
2 CONT
2 CONT Jordan POST (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT SayBrook ye 8th day of May 1722, Then & there personally appeared the above named Jordan POST and acknowledged the above Instrument to be his act and deed before me
2 CONT
2 CONT Dan'll TAYLOR Justice of ye peace & Quarum
2 CONT
2 CONT Rec'd ye 29th day of May 1722
