2 CONT
2 CONT Saybrook Land Records Book 5 Page 377 FHL Film #5538
2 CONT
2 CONT Deed from Jordan POST to Joseph BLAGUE
2 CONT
2 CONT To all People to whom these Presents Shall come Greeting; Know ye that I Jordan POST of Say-Brook, in the County of New London and Colony of Connecticut, in New England for and in Consideration of ye sum of two pounds ten shilling
2 CONC s in money to me in hand paid before the ensealing hereof Joseph BLAGUE of Say-Brook in the County of New london and Colony aforesaid ye receipt whereof I do hereby acknowledge and myself therewith fully satisfied and contented an
2 CONC d thereof and of every part and parcel thereof do exonerate acquit and discharge ye said Joseph BLAGUE his heirs executors administrators forever by these presents have given granted bargained sold conveyed and confirmed and by th
2 CONC ese presents do freely fully and absolutely give grant bargain sell and confirm unto him ye said Joseph BLAGUE his heirs and assigns forever one mesuage or tract of land scituated lying and being in the Town Commons aforesaid cont
2 CONC aining one third part of a hundred pound right.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Have and to Hold ye said granted and bargained premises with all ye appurtenances priveledges and commodities to the same belonging or in any wise appertaining to him ye said Joseph BLAGUE his heirs and assigns forever to his a
2 CONC nd their own proper use benefit and behoof;
2 CONT
2 CONT And I the said Jordon POST for me my heirs Executors administrators Do Covenant promise and grant to ye said Joseph BLAGUE his heirs and assigns that at and before ye ensealing hereof I am the true sole and lawful owner of ye abov
2 CONC e bargained Premises and am lawfully seized and possesed of ye same in my own proper right and absolute estate of inheritance in fee simple and have in myself full power and lawfull authority to bargain sell convey and confirm sd 
2 CONC bargained premises in manner as abovesaid, and that the said Joseph BLAGUE his heirs and assigns shall and may from time to tome and at all times hereafter by force and virtue of these presents Lawfully peaceably and quietly have 
2 CONC hold occupie posses and enjoy the said demised and bargained premises with the appurtenances free and clear and freely acquitted exonerated and discharged of from all and all manner of Former or other gifts grants bargains sales l
2 CONC eases mortgages wills entails Jointers Dowries Judgments executions Incumbrances and extents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Furthermore I the said Jordan POST for myself my heirs executors administrators do Covenant and ingage the above demised premises to him ye said Jos. BLAGUE his heirs and assigns against ye lawfull claims or demands of any person 
2 CONC or persons whatsoever forever to Warrant Secure and defend.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this 3d day of August Anno Domini 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT Singed Sealed and Delivered In presence of us Witnesses Sam'll LORD Rous CROPTON
2 CONT
2 CONT Jordon POST (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Hartford County ss. Hebron Aprill 30th day A.D. 1734. Then and there personally appeared Jordon POST ye grantor and acknowledged ye above written Instrument to be his own free act and deed. Before me Coram Nath'll FOOT Just. of pe
2 CONC ace.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rec'd June 7th 1738 and entered From ye original Per Sam'll WILLARD Register. 
