1 NOTE {geni:about_me} LINE OF NATHANIEL DUNHAM OF WRENTHAM, MA AND HEBRON, CT
2 CONT THIRD GENERATION IN AMERICA
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  OBADIAH 3 DUNHAM (Nathaniel 2 Thomas 1), born 14 Oct. 1701, Wrentham, MA. [1]  He married first in Hebron, CT 7 Oct. 1724 ESTHER POST, [2] daughter of Stephen 3 and Hannah (Hosmer) Post.  She was born 19 Mar. 1698/9; died in G
2 CONC ilead, CT 7 May 1752. [3]  Obadiah  married second in Hebron, CT 6 Dec. 1752 HANNAH PINNEO. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Obadiah 3 and Hannah (Pinneo) Dunham born in Hebron, CT: [5]
2 CONT * 24.     i.  HANNAH 4 DUNHAM, b. 2 Sept. 1753; nfr 
2 CONT * 25.    ii.  ESTHER 4 DUNHAM, b. 17 Dec. 1754; nfr 
2 CONT * 26.   iii.  ANNE 4 DUNHAM, b. 12 July 1756; nfr
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == References:
2 CONT * http://www.dunham-singletary.org/dunhamgenealogy/NATDUN-Generation-3-Obadiah(3)Dunham.html
2 CONT * 1.  Vital Records of Wrentham, Massachusetts to the Year 1850, p. 65.
2 CONT * 2.  TAG 62:20.
2 CONT * 3.  Barbour Collection-Vital Records-Hebron, CT, p. 39.
2 CONT * 4.  Bailey’s Connecticut Marriages, Vol. 3:91.
2 CONT * 5.  Barbour Collection-Vital Records-Hebron, CT, p. 39.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dunham-4330
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obidiah, son of Nathaniel and Mary Dunham, was born in Wrentham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America on 14 October 1701, He married Esther, daughter of Stephen and Hannah (Hosmer) Post in Hebron, Tolland, C
2 CONC onnecticut Colony on 7 October 1724 in Hebron; Obidiah death is undiscovered.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Obidiah Dunham (1701)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obidiah Dunham
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 14 Oct 1701 in Wrentham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay 
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Nathaniel Dunham Sr. and Mary (Unknown) Dunham
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Mary Dunham, Nathaniel Dunham, Mehitable (Dunham) Whitcomb, Thomas Dunham, Nathaniel Dunham Jr., Jabez Dunham and Isaac Dunham [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT [spouse(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [children unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died [date unknown] in Toland County, Connecticut Colony
