2 CONT ** Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZN7-Z4T FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 3 2023, 16:03:21 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Post, third child of Thomas Post and Dinah Brown Post, was born at Hebron, CT in 1736 and died at Lyme, NH in 1811 at the age of 75.  He married Mary Thompson (1741-1770) in 1757 and they had six children, all born in Hebron
2 CONC .  Their children were: John, Mary (Latham), Dinah (Culver), Joseph Otis, and Anne (Mann).  When Mary died, Peter married Ruth Walker (1737-1821) in 1770 and they had six children, all born in Hebron.  Their children were: Benjami
2 CONC n, Ruth, Mindwell (Gardener), Abigail and Aaron (twins), and Abigail (Bliss).  In about 1785 Peter moved from Hebron, CT to Lyme, NH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like his father, Deacon Thomas Post, Peter was active in the community of Hebron.  He was a highway surveyor in 1771, a tithing man in 1773, and a highway surveyor again in 1777.  When Peter moved to New Hampshire he purchased 100
2 CONC 0 acres of land and operated a gristmill and sawmill on it.  Later he built a home on Orford Road, next to Post Pond.  The house was reported to be in good condition in 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently there is some indication that Peter Post served in the Revolutionary War..
2 CONT
2 CONT (For more information about Peter Post see THE POST FAMILY--FOURTEEN GENERATIONS IN AMERICA by Gerald R. Post.)* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/82106515/peter-post Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/pr
2 CONC ojects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 3 2023, 16:12:55 UTC''
