1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Phinehas Post''' (1704–1787), the father of Abner Post, was a lifelong resident of Connecticut whose life spanned the transition from a British colony to an independent nation. He was a descendant of the early S
2 CONC aybrook settlers and spent much of his life in Hebron, Tolland County.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life Summary'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Life Summary'''
2 CONT Birth: December 2, 1704, in Saybrook, Connecticut.
2 CONT Marriage: He married Ann Post on June 25, 1741, in Hebron.
2 CONT Residence: Records place him primarily in Hebron, where he was a member of the community for over four decades.
2 CONT Death: March 21, 1787, in Hebron at the age of 82. He is buried in Hebron, Connecticut.
2 CONT '''
2 CONT Lineage and Descendants'''
2 CONT Phinehas was the son of Stephen Post (1664–1752) and Hannah Hosmer (1670–1751). Through his marriage to Ann, he had several children who continued the Post name in New England:
