1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marriage and Family
2 CONT She married Levin Backus (sometimes recorded as Living Backus) on February 14, 1771, in Hebron, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had several children, including:
2 CONT Ann Backus (b. 1772)
2 CONT Levin Backus Jr. (b. 1773)
2 CONT Ezra Backus (b. 1777)
2 CONT Abner Backus (b. 1780), likely named after her father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical Context
2 CONT Her name "Ann Post Barker" often appears in records because she was born a Post but may have had a prior marriage to a Barker, or the name was recorded to clarify her lineage within the Barker-Backus-Post families of Tolland Count
2 CONC y. Given your previous interest in Abner Post (b. 1783), she would have been of the generation prior, likely his aunt or a close older relative within the same Hebron branch.
