2 CONC e also totally incorrect.   DNA also proved that William Phelps and George Phelps were NOT brothers, another long-held assumption that must be dispelled also.   Because of the DNA findings, we had to re-evaluate Phelps & Servin bo
2 CONC oks.  Please keep in mind that this invaluable source is considered as a SECONDARY SOURCE.  While it is still a great guide, we must verify the info with PRIMARY RECORDS.   Due to the DNA findings, William's birth date is calculat
2 CONC ed to be ca 1593. His first wife Mary (Unknown) was buried in Crewkerne.  He remarried to Anne Dover and had some more children with him.   Please check out the website www.Phelpsfamilyhistory.com for more info:[[http://www.phelps
2 CONC familyhistory.com/index.asp | Phelps Family History website]]  I have vital records from the parish records of St Bartholomew Parish,Crewkerne, Somerset County, England.<ref>www.freereg.org.uk under Crewkerne, Somerset County, Eng
2 CONC land.</ref>  NOTE: Some parish entries arePhelps and others are Phelpes.  This info can also be found in Great Migrations Series, published in 1995. 
