1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Phelps emigrated to America on the Mary & John in 1630 with his Father,Mother & siblings.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Joseph - bap. Nov. 13, 1628, Crewkerne, Somerset, England; <br/>
2 CONT * d. 1683-4, Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT; <br/>
2 CONT * Inv. Mar. 5, 1683/4, Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT. <br/>
2 CONT * Married first Sep. 20, 1600, Windsor, Hartford Co., CT, Hannah NEWTON (not the daughter of Roger Newton) <br/>
2 CONT * Joseph married second on Dec. 19, 1676, Northampton, Hampshire Co., MA, Mary (d. Jan. 16, 1682), widow of Thomas SALMON. <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph and Hannah PHELPS: <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT * Joseph Jr., b. 1667, married first Mary COLLIER; second Sarah CASE and third Mary CASE; 
2 CONT * Hannah, b. abt 1668; 
2 CONT * Timothy abt. 1671, married Rachel MOORE<br/>
2 CONT * Sarah abt. 1672, married John HILL
2 CONT * William abt 1664, died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://kinnexions.com/ancestries/phelps.htm - (NOTE: I do not recommend this site as a reference table. To me, it is a fly by info ceill that has acquired info from other geno sites and families. This site is up for sale to the 
2 CONC highest bidder. I do not consider this site as a good source.) 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Joseph I Phelps b. 13 Nov 1628 England, d. 5 Mar 1684 Simsbury, Hartford, CT He was married on 20 Sep 1660 in Windsor, Hartford, CT to Hannah Newton b. o/a 1635 Windsor, Hartford, CT., d.10 Sep 1675 Simsbury, Hartford, CT. His par
2 CONC ents: Father was Mayor William II Phelps and mother was Mary Ann Dover. Her parents: Father was Anthony Newton and mother is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue's: Joseph II Phelps, Hannah (died young), Timothy Phelps, Sarah Phelps, and William Phelps (died young).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category: Puritanism, North America]] [[Category:17th Century American Immigration]] [[Category:Puritan Great Migration]] [[Category: Mary and John sailed March 20 1630]]
2 CONT {{Puritan Great Migration}}
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT === Baptism ===: Joseph Phelps was baptized at St Bartholomew Church on 13 Nov 1628 in Crewkerne, Somersetshire, England, the son of [[Phelps-54|William Phelps]]<ref>FreeReg.org, baptisms, "Josephe Phelps"</ref> & [[Dover-85|Anne 
2 CONC Dover]]. Joseph was born a twin of Mary Phelps, who died soon.<ref>Source S5::  "The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England 1620-1633, Volumes I-III", page 1446</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT === Siblings ===: His parents were married on  14 Nov 1626 in Crewkerne, Somerset, England,  <ref>Source S885 </ref>, and had the following children:
2 CONT #Child:  [[Phelps-1155|Joseph Phelps]]
2 CONT # Child:  [[Phelps-1156|Mary Phelps]]
2 CONT # Child:  [[Phelps-1157|Cornelius Phelps]]
2 CONT #Child:  [[Phelps-1158|Sarah Phelps]]
2 CONT #Child:  [[Phelps-1159|Timothy Phelps]]
2 CONT
2 CONT === Emigration 1630 on the ''Mary and John'' ===: His parents left England 20 March 1630 on the "Mary and John", with 4 young sons.<ref>Source S3</ref>After residing in Dorchester, Massachusetts Bay Colony, his parents removed to 
2 CONC Windsor (present day state of Connecticut).
2 CONT
2 CONT === Marriages ===: Joseph married his first wife, Hannah Newton, on 20 Sept 1660 at Windsor. He married his second wife, Mary --- Salmon, on 19 Dec 1676 at Simsbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children ===
2 CONT
2 CONT :Children of Joseph and Hannah PHELPS: #Joseph (born 2 August 1667); married first Mary COLLIER; second SarahCASE and third Mary CASE; 
2 CONT #Hannah (born 2 Feb 1668);
2 CONT #Sarah married John HILL;
2 CONT #William died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT :Child of Joseph and 2nd wife Mary:
2 CONT #Timothy (b. ca. 1680); married Rachel MOORE.   
2 CONT
2 CONT == Probate==: Joseph Phelps, Simsbury, probate inventory taken 5 March 1683/84, children: Joseph 17 yrs, Hannah 15 yrs, William 13 yrs, Sarah 11 yrs andTimothy 4 yrs.
2 CONT 28 August 1684. "The Petition of Mary Phelps, Relict to Joseph Phelps,of Symsbury, To the Honourable County Court now sitting at Hartford, Humbly Showeth: That your poor Petitioner, when shee married to JosephPhelps, was a widow, 
2 CONC And was Left by her former husband in somewhat acomfortable Condition. And after shee was married to this man, carried a considerable Estate with her to the value of £40 or £50, but since his decease is left in a very helpless Con
2 CONC dition; having but £6 allowed In Moveable estate, with the third of the Land for life, which will not yield above 20 Shillings per Annum, which is but a very small matter to maintain me, having a young child left By Joseph Phelps,
2 CONC  my deceased husband, to be brought up out of it. Having therefore heard of the Readyness of this Court to hear the cry & to help the fatherlessand the Widow, made me Bold humbly to move your honours that some more of the Estate m
2 CONC ay be settled upon me for the Bringing up of the Child. However, if the matter be difficult, that at least you would be pleased to order that I might have that mare and Cow that is left and waspart of my own Estate which I carried
2 CONC  with me when I married my laterhusband. Hoping your honours will take the matter into serious consideration, I shal not farther enlarge, but, begging Gods presence with you, rest your humble Petitioner. Northapt, 28 August, 1684.
2 CONC  Mary Phelps."<ref>Source S4</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references/>* [https://www.freereg.org.uk/search_records/58184f9be93790eca3dc43c7/show_print_version?search_id=59d90433f493fd8b738de36c FreeReg.org, baptisms, "Josephe Phelps"], free searches of Parish Registers of England
2 CONT * S1. [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=105896653Find A Grave.] Joseph Phelps, born 13 Nov 1628 in Crewkerne, Somerset, England. Died 1684 in Simsbury, Ct. "Joseph PHELPS' father Mr. William Phelps lived on Ea
2 CONC st Street, Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. His brotherWilliam's house is still standing today, but their father's house wasrazed, and the land was leveled and shoved back. The original burialsbehind the house were disleveled. This area
2 CONC  is now Veterans Memorial Cemetery."
2 CONT * S2. [https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Phelps/5639982155350043220 Geni.] Joseph Phelps I, born 13 Nov 1628 in Crewkerne, Somerset, England. Died Feb1684 in Simsbury, Ct. Son of William and Anne Phelps. Husband of Hannah Newton 
