2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT The Phelps & Servin has the incorrect information regarding Sarah Phelps.  She was the daughter of William Phelps and Ann Dover, but she wasNOT born in 1623 in England, but in 1632.  She was born in Dorchester, Massachusetts - bef
2 CONC ore her family moved to Windsor, Connecticutt in 1633.   She married William Wade in Windsor, but died soon after.  There were no children from this union.  See Great Migration book, Vol 3 on her Phelps family. Please check her fa
2 CONC ther William Phelps' Bio/Sources for more detailed information. Vital records were found in Crewkerne Parish, Crewkerne, Co. Somerset,England.  It has several birth/baptism, marriage, and death dates forvarious members of this fam
2 CONC ily.  There was no Sarah Phelps in these records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===William PHELPS and his two wives and their children:===
2 CONT Mary Phelps, first wife
2 CONT *William PHELPS, son
2 CONT *Samuel PHELPS, son
2 CONT *Infant PHELPS, died young
2 CONT *Nathaniel PHELPS, son
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne DOVER Phelps, 2nd wife
2 CONT *Cornelius PHELPS, son, died young
2 CONT *Mary PHELPS, b. 1628 died young
2 CONT *Joseph PHELPS, b. 1629, twin son
2 CONT *Mary PHELPS, b. 1629, twin daughter, died young.
2 CONT *Sarah PHELPS, daughter
2 CONT *Timothy PHELPS, son
2 CONT *Mary PHELPS, daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT All the surviving ones migrated to New England:  *William, 2nd wife Anne, and his kids: William, Samuel, Nathaniel, Joseph.   The last 3 children were born in New England and survived to adulthood: 
2 CONT *Sarah, Timothy, & Mary 
2 CONT
