2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT This is the THIRD MARY PHELPS.  She was born to William PHELPS and Anne DOVER.  The first two Marys died in infancy.  This third Mary survived to adulthood.  Submitted by [[Phelps-191  | Dorothy Phelps]], Monday, September 15, 201
2 CONC 4. Mary was born on 2 Mary 1644 Windsor, Hartford Co., Connecticut, the youngest child, the daughter of [[Phelps-2283|Wiliam Phelps]] and [[Dover-196|Anne Dover]].  She was baptized on 19th of July 1644.   She married Lieut. Thoma
2 CONC s Barber, son of Thomas Barber who immigrated to New England in 1635, on 13 Dec 1660 in Hebron, Hartford Co., Connecticut.  (in Barber Genealogy, it says the marriage date was 13 Dec 1663).
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.  John Barber, b. 1 Nov 1662/1664 Windsor, m. Mary Holcomb. ii. Mary Barber, b. 11 May 1666 Windsor.iii.  Sarah Barber, b. 12 July 1669 Windsor, m. Nov 26, 1701 Andrew Robe.  No issue.iv.  Joanna Barber, b. abt 1670 Windsor, m. 
2 CONC Josiah Adkins on 3 Jan 1710-11.  No issue. v.  Anna Barber, b. abt 1670/1671 Windsor, m. Jonathan Higley.vi.  Thomas Barber, b. 7 Oct 1671/1672 Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT, m. Abigail Buell. vii.  Samuel Barber, b. 17 May 1673, m. 
2 CONC Sarah Holcomb. viii.  A child Barber, b. 1677 Windsor, died young. (NOTE:  These dates were from Phelps & Servin, if you see the date AFTER the slash, that date is from Barber Genealogy. These dates do need to be verified with oth
2 CONC er sources.) In 1669 Massaco was carved from Windsor and made a separate township and named Simsbury.  Mary's husband Thomas Barber and his brother Samuel, and their families moved in 1670 or 1671 to the land (that is now in Simsb
2 CONC ury) that they inherited from their father Thomas Barber.  [This inherited portion of the "Meadow Lands" was lying along Massaco River]. She passed away on 13 Feb 1724 in Simsbury, Hartford Co., Connecticut.
2 CONT
