1 NOTE Apparently he came directly to Windsor, and his first four children were born in England.. He was representative for Windsor 1658-61, removed about 1664 to Killingworth, CT, and was often representative there. He m(2) in 1672 the 
2 CONC widow Sarah (Diamond) Bemis.
2 CONT There are something over 1800 hits on Google for "edward griswold" AND "margaret', and many of them are garbage. I have picked  up several dates etc. from one or two that appear to be based on articles in TAG (from back issues tha
2 CONC t I don't have).
