2 CONT
2 CONT THE GRISWOLD FAMILY; The First Five Generations in America, Compiled and Edited by Esther Griswold French and Robert Lewis French: FRANCIS. According to the records of Salisbury, depositions by two sons of George state that the ol
2 CONC dest son of their grandfather Edward was always reputed to be Francis. Further evidence is given in the deed of gift by Edward when he named his grandchildren by Francis, then his other sons in order of their birth. Since Francis 
2 CONC was married about 1652, he would have been born about 1629. The History of New London by Caulkins identities him erroneously as Francis of Cambridge, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: History of Norwich, Connecticut by Frances Manwaring Caulkins, 1866, Hartford, Case, Lockwood, and Co.
2 CONT
