1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "GEORGE 2 , b. England, 1633 (Edward 1 ); m. in Windsor, Conn., 
2 CONT Oct. 3, 1655, Mary Holcombe, daughter of Thomas and Eliza¬ 
2 CONT beth, who came from England to Dorchester, Mass., and removed 
2 CONT to Windsor 1635. Mary d. Apr. 4, 1708. George made his home 
2 CONT in Poquonoc 1649 where he purchased land from the Indians. 
2 CONT Poquonoc then was about six miles from Windsor and those 
2 CONT families venturing out to this settlement had no protection from 
2 CONT any danger that might come or from the Indians; however, from 
2 CONT the records, we find this family was never molested. Probably 
2 CONT from the fact that he dealt honestly with the Indians and treated 
2 CONT them fairly, they respected him; he was known to be of kindly 
2 CONT disposition. Made freeman 1669; was a large land owner and a 
2 CONT man of high respectability. A sturdy active citizen, but did not 
2 CONT aspire to political office. Died Sept. 3, 1704. His estate, Hartford 
2 CONT Probate, Vol. VII, 108; Vol. IX, 10, 11; Manwaring, II, 70. 
2 CONT Inventory Oct. 2, 1704. An agreement made by the widow and 
2 CONT children for the settlement of the estate is recorded. This agreement also mentions his grand-daughter Abigail Griswold and daughters Mary Cooley and Deborah Moore. 1685 he was mentioned in Windsor Patent. 1676 contributed to the 
2 CONC poor of other colonies. 1679 had a warehouse on the north side of the Rivulet 
2 CONT near the ferry. Trade with England and West Indies."
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see: The Griswold family, England-America : Edward of Windsor, Connecticut, Matthew of Lyme, Connecticut, Michael of Wethersfield, Connecticut by Griswold, Glenn E; https://archive.org/details/griswoldfamilyen02gris/page/16
2 CONC  (Steven Ferry, February 8, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===George Griswold
2 CONT *BIRTH	19 May 1633 Kenilworth, Warwick District, Warwickshire, England
2 CONT *DEATH	3 Sep 1704 (aged 71) Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT George's wife was Mary Holcombe and she takes us all teh way back to the beginning of time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/54932313/george-griswold
2 CONT
2 CONT *Parents: Edward Griswold (1607-1690)  & Margaret (1609-1670)
2 CONT *Spouse: Mary Holcomb (1636-1708)
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children 
2 CONT #Daniel Griswold (1656- )
2 CONT #Tho,as Griswold (1658- )
2 CONT #Edward Griswold (1660- )
2 CONT #Mary Griswold (1663- )
2 CONT #George Griswold 1665-1704
2 CONT #John Griswold (1668- )
2 CONT #Benjamin Griswold 1671- )
2 CONT #Deborah Griswold Moore 1674-1756
2 CONT #Abigail Griswold 1676-1682
2 CONT #Samuel Griswold 1681-1682
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=gwenbj&id=I2008484
2 CONT
2 CONT Savage:
2 CONT
2 CONT >GRISWOLD, GEORGE, Windsor, s. of Edward, b. in Eng. it is said,1638, and there certain. he liv. some yrs. with his f. was freem. 1654, m. 3 Oct. 1655, Mary, d. perhaps, of Thomas Holcomb, had Daniel,b. 1 Oct. 1656; Thomas, 29 Sep
2 CONC t. 1658; Edward, 19 Mar. 1661; Mary, 28Sept. 1663; George, 3 Dec. 1665; John, 17 Sept. 1668; Benjamin, 16 Aug. 1671; Deborah, 30 May 1674; and Abigail, 31 Oct. 1676, wh. d. 7May 1682; beside Samuel, 5 Nov. 1681, who d. inf.; and h
2 CONC e d. 1704. His wid. Mary d. 4 Apr. 1708
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 9, 1700, George testified that he was son of EdwardGriswold and nephew of Matthew and Thomas Griswold. OnJanuary 19, 1737.8, sons George and John testified thatthey were grandsons of Edward Griswold, grand nephews ofMatthew
2 CONC  and Thomas Griswold, and nephews of FrancisGriswold.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:a17485&id=I8467
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Category: Windsor, Connecticut
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT George Griswold, son of Edward, was baptized in 1633 in Kenilworth Parish, England.<ref name="GEGris">Griswold, Glenn E. Griswold. ''The Griswold family : England-America''. Middleboro, Mass.: Griswold Family Association of Americ
2 CONC a, 1935.  Available at Ancestry.com.</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT He made his home in Poquonoc in 1649.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT He married Mary Holcombe, daughter of Thomas and Elizabeth Holcombe, 3Oct. 1655 in :Category: Windsor, Connecticut|Windsor, Connecticut.<ref name="Torry">Torry, Clarence A. ''New England Marriages Prior to1700'' George Griswold.</
2 CONC ref><ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT He was made freeman in 1669.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT George died in 3 Sep. 1704.<ref name="Torry"/><ref>''Massachusetts, Town and Vital Records, 1620-1988'' [http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db=MATownVital&h=75874425&indiv=try&o_vc=Record:OtherRecord&rhSource=2204 Mas Vita
2 CONC l] Actual work is ''Genealogies of Gill, Massachusetts''.</ref> 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Birth ===
2 CONT :: 4 MAY 1633 Kenilworth, Warwickshire, England.{{Citation needed}}
2 CONT
2 CONT === Christening ===
2 CONT :: 19 MAY 1633 Kenilworth, Warwickshire, England.{{Citation needed}}
2 CONT
2 CONT === Children of George and Mary ===
2 CONT Recorded at Windsor.
2 CONT #Daniel, b. Oct. 1, 1656.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Thomas, b. Sept. 29, 1658.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Edward, b. May 19, 1660/1.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Mary, b. Sept. 28, 1663.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #George, b. Dec. 3, 1665. Unm. <ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #John, b. Sept. 17, 1668.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Benjamin, b. Apr. 16, 1671.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Deborah, b. May 30, 1674.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Abigail, b. Oct. 31, 1676; d. May 7, 1682.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT #Samuel, b. Nov. 5, 1681; d. June 1, 1682.<ref name="GEGris"/>
2 CONT
