2 CONC 45) [https://books.google.com/books?id=ZmZZAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA169 Page 169]
2 CONT * Ancestral File Number:  1LV1-S7* <span id='Welles'></span>Welles, Edwin. ''Space:Births, Marriages,and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield, and Entered in the Early Land Records of the Colony of Connecticut|Bir
2 CONC ths, Marriages, and Deaths Returned from Hartford, Windsor, and Fairfield'' (Case, Lockwood & Brainard Co., Hartford, Conn., 1898) [https://books.google.com/books?id=0woWAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA42 Page 42]* <span id='AGS'></span>''Space:The
2 CONC  Association for Gravestone Studies|The Association for Gravestone Studies'' (1985) "Markers III" [https://archive.org/stream/markersiii00davi#page/3/mode/1up Page 3]: "Griswold's carefully lettered stones in the distinctive reddi
2 CONC sh brown Windsor sandstone mark three graves in Enfield, six graves in Northampton, and five in Westerfield, including that of his son Edward"
