1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see: The Griswold family, England-America : Edward of Windsor, Connecticut, Matthew of Lyme, Connecticut, Michael of Wethersfield, Connecticut by Griswold, Glenn E; https://archive.org/details/griswoldfamily
2 CONC en02gris/page/16 (Steven Ferry, February 8, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~steeles/Steele/d74.htm#P2007
2 CONT *Joseph GRISWOLD was born on 12 Mar 1647/48 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. (10767) 
2 CONT *He died on 14 Nov 1716 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT. (10768) 
2 CONT *Parents: Edward GRISWOLD and Margaret HICKS.
2 CONT *He was married to Mary GAYLORD on 16 Jul 1670 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT.(10769) (10770) *Children were: 
2 CONT # Mary GRISWOLD, 
2 CONT # Joseph GRISWOLD, 
2 CONT # Frances GRISWOLD, 
2 CONT # Matthew GRISWOLD, 
2 CONT # Abigail GRISWOLD.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Griswold, son of Edward and Margaret Griswold of Kenilworth, Warwickshire, England, was baptized at Windsor, Connecticut on 22 March 1647.  ''The Griswold family : England-America'',by Glenn E. Griswold, pages 30 - 31
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Griswold married Mary Gaylord, daughter of Samuel and Elizabeth, at Windsor on 14 July 1670. The estate of Samuel Gaylord names Joseph Griswold and his wife Mary. Their children, Mary, Elizabeth, Joseph, Francis, Matthew an
2 CONC d Abigail were all born at Windsor, Connecticut. Joseph was a Freeman in 1670 and an ensign in 1690.  On the Windsor tax list of 1675, Joseph has "a family, horse, and two oxen".  The will of Joseph Griswold is dated 6 Sept 1716. 
2 CONC  Inventory of his estate is dated 29 Nov 1716.  His will was proved 4 Dec 1716.  Joseph left his wife Mary forty pounds and one third of the estate.  Joseph Griswold names his three sons and two of his daughters,Mary and Abigail, 
2 CONC in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial 14 Nov 1716 Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Griswold, Glenn E.  [http://search.ancestry.com/search/db.aspx?dbid=18575 ''The Griswold family : England-America'']. (Middleboro, Mass.: Griswold Family Association of America, 1935). Available at Ancestry.com. pg 30-31
2 CONT *Phelps, Noah Amherst. ''[[Space:History of Simsbury, Granby, and Canton, from 1642 to 1845|History of Simsbury, Granby, and Canton, from 1642 to 1845]]'' (Case, Tiffany and Burnham, Hartford, 1845) [https://books.google.com/books
2 CONC ?id=ZmZZAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA169 Page 169]
