1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This is the second son of George and Margaret named John. The first, b. 1642, died young. Please see: The Griswold family, England-America : Edward of Windsor, Connecticut, Matthew of Lyme, Connecticut, Michael of 
2 CONC Wethersfield, Connecticut by Griswold, Glenn E; https://archive.org/details/griswoldfamilyen02gris/page/16 (Steven Ferry, February 8, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Griswold''' was the second son named John of Edward and Margaret Griswold. He was baptized Aug. 1, 1652 in Windsor, Hartford, CT, and died 3 Aug 1717 in Killingworth, Middlesex, CT. He married first Mary Bemis, daughter of
2 CONC  James and Sarah (Dimond) Bemis, who became his stepsister by the marriage of his father to Sarah (Dimond) Bemis. Mary died 27 Oct 1679. They had four children.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married second Bathsheba North, daughter of Thomas, born 1654, who died 19 Mar 1736. They had 13 children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The burial places of Mary and Bathsheba are unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Griswold Family" vol II--pg. 32
2 CONT
2 CONT John Griswold was a farmer; prominent & leading citizen. Deacon for many years. Served on important civil committees. Deputy 1690. Captain 1712. Served in the Narragansett War. The town granted him six acres for his services in th
2 CONC e Indian Wars. Died 7 Burial in congregational cemetery, Clinton,CT. It is possible that Bathsheba is buried in vacant space next to his tombstone
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * He removed from Windsor, probably with his father, and went to Killingworth. Evidently a man of intelligence and character, John Griswold was a deacon of the church, had property and was influential in the community. He was depu
2 CONC ty from Killingworth to the CT General Court, 1690, 1697-99, 1701-04, 1707-12, 1715, and 1716. From 1697 to 1702 he was representative from Killingworth. In 1712 he was captain of the train band in Killingworth, and was also a sol
2 CONC dier in the Narragansett War. In 1714 he was a member of the Governor's Council. He married first Mary, died 10/27/1679, 4 children. He married second Bathsheba, died 3/19/1736, 12 children. Ancestral File has death in Windsor, CT
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT _______
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: JANA WELLMAN ULRICH
2 CONT
2 CONT Settled in Killingworth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deacon of the church and member of the General Court for 28 sessions.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT .
2 CONT
2 CONT All children recorded in Killingworth records
2 CONT
