2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT 1.  John was a farmer; prominent & leading citizen. Deacon for many years. Served on important civil committees. Deputy 1690. Captain 1712. Served in the Narragansett War. The town granted him six acres for hisservices in the Indi
2 CONC an Wars. Died 7 Burial in the Indian River Cemetery, Clinton, CT. It is possible that Bathsheba is buried in vacant space next to his tombstone.
2 CONT This is not the same John Griswold who was a twin to Hannah. He may have been named subsequent to the John 1642's death. <ref>Entered by TomBredehoft,  Jan 4, 2013</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT All children recorded in Killingworth records
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: 07 Aug 1652, Windsor, Hartford County, CT, USA Married first Nov 18 1672 to Mary Bemis, daughter of James and Sarah (Dimond) Bemis who became his stepsister when his father married Sarah!Married (2nd) to Bashua/Bathsheba 
2 CONC North. Burial: 07 Aug 1717, Indian River Cemetery/   Clinton, Middlesex County, CT, USA Military service: 1675 - 1676, King Philip’s War (The Great Narragansett War)/  Connecticut, USA Will written 6 Jun 1713, located in the State
2 CONC  Library, Hartford, CT. <ref>Entered by Larry Chesebro'. http://chesebro.net</ref>
2 CONT
