1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The very first Hebron Town Clerk was Timothy Phelps. It was his wife, '''Martha Crow Phelps, who was the heroine behind the Prophet's Rock legend'''. She led a group of women who, searching for their husbands in 17
2 CONC 04, yelled out from the rock, located off Burrows Hill Road. The echoes of their cries were heard by the men, resulting in a reunion of the families, and they decided that Hebron was a good place to settle. The Hebrew name "Hebron
2 CONC " has been translated as "city of refuge." The town was incorporated just four years later, in 1708.
2 CONT
