1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From The Phelps Family of America, p. 98: "Her grave stone may be seen in the ancient burying ground, Centre Church, at Hartford, the only Phelps stone in the yard. The inscription reads:--"Here lies interred ye bo
2 CONC dy of Mrs. Sarah Phelps, ye relict of Mr. Tim Phelps, who died Feb. ye 18th, 1758, in ye 96th year of her age."
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH6 PRATT (DANIEL5, JOHN (HARTFORD FOUNDER)4, WILLIAM (REV)3, ANDREW2, THOMAS1) was born 1662 in Hartford, Hartford, CT, and died February 18, 1758 in Centre Church, Hartford, CT.  She married TIMOTHY (EARLY HARTFORD) PHELPS No
2 CONC vember 13, 1690 in Hartford, Hartford, CT, son of SAMUEL PHELPS and SARAH GRISWOLD.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of SARAH PRATT and TIMOTHY PHELPS are:
2 CONT  i. MARY7 PHELPS, b. August 21, 1692, Hartford, Hartford, CT.
2 CONT  ii. HANNAH PHELPS, b. September 10, 1694, Hartford, Hartford, CT; m. (1) TIMOTHY LOOMIS; m. (2) RICHARD BURNHAM, April 05, 1722.
2 CONT  iii. MABEL PHELPS, b. September 26, 1696, Hartford, Hartford, CT.
2 CONT  iv. ELIZABETH PHELPS, b. September 04, 1699, Hartford, Hartford, CT.
2 CONT  v. TIMOTHY PHELPS, b. May 24, 1702, Hartford, Hartford, CT; d. September 09, 1756, Hartford, Hartford, CT; m. SARAH BROWN.
2 CONT  vi. ESTHER PHELPS, b. October 29, 1703, Hartford, Hartford, CT; d. Farmington, CT; m. WILLIAM HOOKER.
2 CONT  vii. ABIGAIL PHELPS, b. 1690-1713, Hartford, Hartford, CT; d. September 30, 1760, Farmington, Hartford, CT; m. WILLIAM HOOKER, May 20, 1731. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://members.tripod.com/~David_Cooke/pratt/pratt1.html
