1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cabinet maker
2 CONT
2 CONT From a letter dated November 16, 1916, from S. A. McCarthy to Dr. John W. Phelps: "I commenced with Timothy PHELPS, No. 81, the father of John Phelps, No. 253, and traced through the will books and the deed books from Hartford to 
2 CONC Windsor, Conn., where he lived from 1732 to 1744; then to the town of Union in Windham Co. (now Tolland Co.), where he lived from 1744 to 1750, and I have a long list of citations of his various land transactions from the records 
2 CONC showing the family connections which confirm the statements in the "Phelps Family".
2 CONT
2 CONT "After 1750, there is no further record of the PHELPSes in Union; presumably Timothy returned to Hartford, where he died in 1756."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From '''Payne-Joyce Genealogy''':
