1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ◦From The Phelps Family of America:
2 CONT  (#166) Capt. Abel Phelps, b. Windsor, Ct., 19 Feb., 1705, m. 1st, Jerusha, about 1730, b. Goshen, Ct., 1706, d. Simsbury, Ct., 1 Jan., 1736. He m. 2nd, probably Mary Pinnuck of Hebron, 6 July, 1737.
2 CONT  Capt. Phelps served in the French war, where he received his military title. He resided in Simsbury, Ct., for a time, and also in Goshen, Ct., where he was a large real estate owner. He also appears to have resided in Norfolk, Ct
2 CONC ., where he was selectman in 1755. He died either in Goshen or Norfolk, Ct. 
2 CONT  Children by 1st wife, b. Simsbury, Ct. 
2 CONT  i. Abel, b. 8 March, 1732, d. 10 Feb., 1736. 
2 CONT  ii. Joel, b. 3 Dec, 1733. (Note — It is possible that this Joel is 1st child of Lieut. Samuel.) 
2 CONT  iii. David, b. 8 July, 1735, m. Triphena Phelps. 
2 CONT  Children by 2nd wife, Mary : 
2 CONT  iv. Abel, b. 5 July, 1739, m Lucy Beardsley. 
2 CONT  v. Molly, or Mary, b. 5 Nov., 1740, m. Samuel Francis, in Goshen, Ct , about 1760 
2 CONT  vi. Elkanah, b. 3 Feb., 1742-3, m. Abigail Phelps. 
2 CONT  vii. Jerusha, b. 28 June, 1745, m. Capt. Mathew Phelps. 
2 CONT  viii. Elijah, b. 13 June, 1748, m. Phebe Norton.
2 CONT  ix. Joseph, b. 7 Dec, 1751, m. Huldah Wilcox. [2]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://archive.org/stream/phelpsfamilyofam01phel#page/142/mode/2up  Phelps Family, Vol. I, pp142, Ancestor No. 166
2 CONT
