2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: This is the SECOND WIFE of Joseph PHELPS named Sarah. This memorial was for Sarah GILLETT. She was born on 3 Jan 1673 in Windsor, Hartford Co., CT and died 17 Sep 1757 in Windsor.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no known grave markers for Joseph and his two wives, but they were probably buried in this cemetery or on their land.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father's Will and Probate:
2 CONT DIGEST OF THE EARLY CONNECTICUT PROBATE RECORDS.1710 to 1715. Page 81
2 CONT Name: Cornelius Gillett, Sen.
2 CONT Location: Windsor Invt. S44-07-06.
2 CONT Taken 27 July, 1711, by Samuel Moore and John Palmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children: Priscilla, Abigail, Cornelius, Mary, Hester, Sarah, Joanna and Daniel. (W. R.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Will dated 2nd June, 1711:
2 CONT I, Cornelius Gillett, Sen., of Windsor, do make this my last will and testament: My will is that after my debts and funeral expenses be paid, all my personal or moveable estate shall be and remain to my wife Priscilla for her use 
2 CONC and to her own dispose as she shall see cause, which I do give to her as her own. Whereas, I have made over my lands by deed of gift, excepting 4 acres at Wash Brook and 2 acres now in possession of John Grimes, my will is that wh
2 CONC ereas my son-in-law Joseph Phelps is become surety for my son Cornelius for a debt which he owes to Capt. Timothy Thrall, that the sd. 4 acres of marsh at Wash Brook shall be and remain to my son Joseph Phelps and to his heirs and
2 CONC  assigns forever. And I do hereby give to him my sd. son Joseph Phelps, also, the 2 acres of land in John Grimes's possession. And I appoint my wife executrix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness: John Moore, Sarah Enno.
2 CONT Signed by: Cornelius Gillett, Sen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Court Record, Page 37--3 September, 1711: Will proven.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/g/i/l/William-A-Gillette/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0375.html (be aware that this has lots of errors, so do your research!)
