1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Filer-62 Samuel (Filer) Fyler Sr. (1681–1710)]
2 CONT *''' Born''' 20 Sep 1681 in Suffield, Hartford, Connecticut, British Colonial America
2 CONT * '''Husband of''' Abigail (Phelps) Filer — married 19 Nov 1702 [Hebron, Hartford, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America – ''Connecticut, U.S., Town Marriage Records, pre-1870 {Barbour Collection)''. [https://www.ancestry.c
2 CONC om/imageviewer/collections/1062/images/VBMDUSACT1634_0018-0166?pId=96907 Ancestry.com] and ''Connecticut, U.S., Marriage Index, 1620-1926''. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/61367/images/TH-1942-44278-22221-30?pId
2 CONC =17920 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT * '''Died''' 13 Sep 1710 at age 28 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, British Colonial America
2 CONT ** etc....
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ====Hartford, Connecticut Probate Records, 1700-1729, Vol. 2: [https://www.google.com/books/edition/A_Digest_of_the_Early_Connecticut_Probat/XAIMAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Fyler,%20Samuel%22 Google Books]
2 CONT * '''Name: Samuel Fyler''' – Location: Hebron
2 CONT ** Page 56 Invt. £129-06-04. – Taken 25 September, 1710, by Return Strong, Samuel Strong, Nathaniel Phelps and Samuel Palmer. 
2 CONT ** Court Record, Page 20—6 November, 1710: Adms. granted to Thomas Fyler of Windsor, a brother of sd. decd. 
2 CONT ** Page 148—6 July, 1713: Adms. account exhibited and allowed. Thomas Fyler now discharged because of remoteness of place, and letters granted to Timothy Phelps of Hebron, a brother-in-law of the deceased. 
2 CONT ** Page 240—7 March, 1714-15: This Court grant Thomas Fyler a Quietus Est. 
2 CONT ** Page 108 (Vol. IX) 7 July, 1719: This Court appoint Samuel Holcomb to be guardian to Abigail Fyler, a minor about 17 years of age, daughter of Samuel Fyler, late decd. Recog., £50. 
2 CONT ** Page 112—6 October, 1719: This Court also appoint William Phelps of Windsor to be guardian to Samuel Fyler, a minor 10 years of age, son of Samuel Fyler, late of Hebron decd. 
2 CONT ** Page 124—5 April, 1720: Timothy Phelps of Hebron, Adms., exhibits an account of his Adms: £ s d 
2 CONT ** Paid in debts and charges, £24-16-01 
2 CONT ** Inventory, £129-09-04 
2 CONT ** Deducting, £24-16-01 
2 CONT ** There remains to be distributed, £104-13-03
2 CONT ** To Samuel Fyler, only son, £52-06-07
2 CONT ** To Abigail and Ann Fyler, the rest of the children, to each, £26-03-04 
2 CONT ** And appoint Benjamin Skinner, Morris Tillotson and Joseph Phelps distributors.
2 CONT *** '''Original Images at [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/9049/images/007627805_00063?pId=3080836 Ancestry.com].'''
2 CONT
