2 CONT This listing is taken from the 1934 reading of Old Poquonock cemetery by W.J. Bowden as part of the Hale Collection of the CT State Library, published Dec. 1937.
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Benajah HOLCOMB [1644-1737/38] and Sarah ENO [1649-1732], Samuel married Martha PHELPS [1688- ]in Windsor on Oct 13, 1709 [Barbour Collection, Windsor Vital Records, Vol. 2, p. 161]. The couple had at least 8 children: 
2 CONC Martha, Samuel, Deborah, Sarah, Rebecca BARNARD, Sophia CATLIN, Samuel (again) and Mariah. [Barbour Collection and Henry Stiles,"The History of Ancient Windsor, CT".] 
