2 CONT Cemetery: Smithfield Burying Ground Name: Sarah Thompson Death Date: 07 May 1809 Age: 89 yrs., 4 mos. Inscription: Thompson, Sarah, died May 7, 1809, ae. 89 yrs., 4 mos. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: unknown Death: May 7, 1809  ae 89 yrs 4 mos [According to her gravestone, Sarah (Holcomb) Thompson must have been born in January 1719/20. She married Samuel Thompson, III 29 Oct 1744 in Goshen, Litchfield, CT, but she is r
2 CONC ecorded there as "not of Goshen." Indeed, no Holcombs seem to be of record in Goshen at that time. Yet family genealogists who actually knew her as an old woman, referred to her as "Sarah of Goshen." -courtesy Linda Maclachlan] 
2 CONT
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links:  Parents: Samuel Holcomb (1684 - 1722) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Samuel Thompson (1722 - 1799) *
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Benajah Thompson (____ - 1832) * Samuel Thompson (1753 - 1815) *
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Smithfield Cemetery  Smithfield Dutchess County New York, USA  Created by: Jan Franco  Record added: Dec 16, 2007  Find A Grave Memorial# 23424429
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Thompson, oldest son of Samuel and Esther Thompson, was born 15 Dec 1722.  He was married on 29 Oct 1744 to Sarah Holcomb of Goshen, Conn.  She was born January 1710 and died 7 May 1809.  He died 29 May 1799.  both are buri
2 CONC ed in the Smithfield cemetery.  The children of Samuel and Sarah Thompson were: (sixth Generation):  Rebecca, who married Mr. Blount, was born 29 Jan 1749 in Goshen, Conn; Hannah born 25 Aug 1747 In Goshen, married a Mr. Powell;  
2 CONC Sarah, 1748-1768, unmarried; Martha, Flora and Esther, all unmarried; Samuel born about 1753, and Benajah, born in 1760. 
