1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=60735953
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Filley, dau. of William and Margaret (---) Filley of Windsor, Conn., b. there of record Aug. 21 (bp Aug. 28), 1658. She d. Jan. 8, 1706/7 in Windsor, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Aug. 26, 1680 in Windsor, Conn., Abigail m. 1) John Bissell, s. of Samuel Bissell and Abigail Holcomb, b. of record Apr. 5 (bp. Nov. 27), 1659 in Windsor, Conn. He d. before Jan. 27, 1684/5, the date his estate inventory was ta
2 CONC ken. They had two children who are outlined in their father's memorial.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct, 20, 1685 of record in Windsor, Abigail m. as his 1st wife, Samuel Tudor, s. of Owen Tudor and Mary Loomis, b. Dec. 5, 1652 in Windsor. Seven children of the marriage. Samuel m. 2) Feb 7, 1707/8, Joanna Taylor.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=181644660
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bissell, oldest recorded child of Samuel Bissell and Abigail Holcomb, b. of record Apr. 5 (bp. Nov. 27), 1659 in Windsor, Conn. He d. intestate prior to Jan. 27, 1684/5.
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow Abigail (Filley) Bissell m. 2) Oct. 20, 1685 of record in Windsor, Samuel Tudor, by whom she had seven additional children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The two children of John Bissell and Abigail Filley are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * i. Abigail, b. Aug, 3, 1681 in Windsor, d. Feb. 13, 1767 in Mansfield, Conn. (g.s.); m. Dec. 26, 1706 of record in Windsor as his 2nd wife, Joseph Baker, Jr., s. of Joseph Baker and Hannah Cook, b. Apr. 13, 1678 in Windsor. He d
2 CONC . Jan. 29, 1754 in Tolland, Conn. (g.s.). Nine children of the marriage.
2 CONT * ii. Capt. John Bissell, Jr., b. after Mar. 8, 1682/3 in Windsor, d. Mar. 8, 1771 in Bolton, Conn. (g.s.); m. Feb. 22, 1709/10 in Windsor, Hannah Denslow.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=PAExAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA129&ots=_HB_2pnEC0&dq=tudor%20family%20descendants%20of%20loomis&pg=PA129#v=onepage&q&f=false page 129] of The Descendants (by the Female Branches) of Joseph Loomis: Who .
2 CONC .., Volume 1 By Elias Loomis
2 CONT
2 CONT No. 7. TUDOR FAMILY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Loomis, daughter of Joseph Loomis, married for her second husband Owen Tudor, Nov. 13, 1651. She d. Aug. 19, 1680. He d. Oct. 30, 1690. Windsor, Ct.  Children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Samuel, b. Dec. 5, 1652, tn. 1st, '''Abigail (Filley), widow of Bissell''' Oct. 30, 1685. She d. Jan. 8, 1707; m. 2d, Joanna  Taylor Feb. 7, 1708. He d. July 6, 1727. East Windsor, Ct. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Tudor (1), East Windsor.
2 CONT * 6. Abigail, b. Oct. 12, 1686, unmarried.
2 CONT * 7. Mary, b. Aug. 31, 1689, m. Abraham Kilbourn, 1722. She d.Aug. 5, 1751. He d. 1770. Glastonbury.
2 CONT * 8. Sarah, b. Sept. 19, 1692, d. Aug. 12, 1694.
2 CONT * 9. Sarah, b. May 25, 1695, m. Justus Morse.
2 CONT * 10. Margaret, b. Nov. 17, 1697, m. Bartlett of Bolton.
2 CONT * 11. Elizabeth, b. July 8, 1700, m. Thomas Marshall Oct. 9, 1725. He d. Feb. 4, 1772. She d. Feb. 8, 1790. Torrington, Ct.
2 CONT * 12. Rev. Samuel, b. March 8, 1704-5, Gr. Y. C. 1728, m. Mary Smith of Middletown, Dec. 10, 1729. He d. Sept. 21, 1757. She d. June 15, 1785, se. 76. First Pastor of Church in Poquonock.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
