1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Capt. John Bissell, Jr., b. after Mar. 8, 1682/3 in Windsor, d. Mar. 8, 1771 in Bolton, Conn. (g.s.); m. Feb. 22, 1709/10 in Windsor, Hannah Denslow.
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Capt. John Bissell IV (often called Esquire) was appointed King's Attorney for Hartford County, Conn. in 1727. He was a Selectman at Bolton in 1721-22. In October 1722 was elected and confirmed Lieutenant of the Company or Train
2 CONC band of Bolton and later promoted to the Captaincy and in May 1739, was appointed Justice of the Peace.  He also represented the town in Assembly and was otherwise prominent." The above appears on page 942 of the Biographical Reco
2 CONC rds of Hartford County, Conn.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=U_lZ2glvEFQC&lpg=PA80&ots=RY23izUEmR&dq=john%20bissell%20abigail%20wells&pg=PA80#v=onepage&q&f=false page 80] of The History and Genealogies of Ancient Windsor, Connecticut: Genealogies and 
2 CONC biographies Press of the Case, Lockwood & Brainard Company, 1893 - Bloomfield (Conn. : Town)
2 CONT
2 CONT >Fam. 17. John4 (Capt.) (John3, John2, John1), m. (1) Sarah Fowler; rem. to Coventry, of which he was an early settler (deed, Oct., 1715); was the first captain of the C. train-band; owned slaves; wife d. 25 Aug., 1751; he m. (2) 
2 CONC 23 Oct., 1754, Mrs. Abigail Wells of Hartford.â Hart. Town Bee. He d. 1783. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ch:
2 CONT * 1. Abigail, b. 3 Aug., 1681. 
2 CONT * 2. John (Capt.), b. 1683; founder of the Ozias Bissell branch of Bolton, Conn.â See at end of the main Genealogy.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
