1 NOTE From Ancestral File (TM), data as of 5 JAN 1998.
1 NOTE He was only left £7 in his father�s will, and was not mentioned in his mother�s at all. He chose to move to Hebron, where his sisters Remember and Mercy lived. [PERRY.TXT]
1 NOTE Death date from Perry. Enlisted in the War of Revolution in Connecticut and was 1st Lt. in the Fourth Battalion under Colonel John Ely. Lived in Rehoboth and Killingly before settling in Chelsea, Vermont. Brownson, NEHGR 116:37 sa
2 CONC ys he was born in Norwich (but note that Eliakim was said to have moved to Norwich after 1746). 1790 census lists him in Shrewsbury, VT, with a family of 1 male over 16, one under 16, and one female. Said to have lived in Rehoboth
2 CONC , Mass, as well as in Killingly, Ct., before settling in Chelsea, Windsor, Ct. Trim, Unrecorded Vital Records of Rehoboth (1980), 51. [BINGHAM.GED]
2 CONT
2 CONT David5 Perry (Eliakim4, Benjamin3, Ezra2, Edmund1) was born in Norwich, New London, Conn August 8, 1741.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Rebecca Bliss in Killingly, Windham, Conn, January 12, 1764. Rebecca was born in Killingly, Windham, Conn December 20, 1744. She was the daughter of John Bliss and Rebecca Whittaker. [Awerkamp homepage]
