2 CONT Phebe was the daughter of Col. Robert Denison and his second wife, Prudence Sherman. In 1760 her father was a leader in the migration of several thousand New Englanders to Nova Scotia. She was married in either Horton or Cornwalli
2 CONC s, Kings County, Nova Scotia on 19 Nov 1766 to Rev. Benjamin (or Benajah--he was called both) PHELPS, the son of Nathaniel Phelps and Mary Curtis of Hebron, CT. Her husband was a graduate of Yale College in 1761, became ordained i
2 CONC n 1765 and preached in Cornwallis, NS until 1778. As a US patriot, he left Canada and was soon installed at the Congregational church in Manchester, CT, where he preached until 1793. Phebe and Benajah had seven known children, bor
2 CONC n 1768 to 1787.
