1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Links
2 CONT * http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/16046700/person/343520655
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT REUBEN WILLIAM STRONG,was born April 20, 1820 in the state of New York to John Strong and his 2nd wife Luany (Hoard) Strong  John Strong and First Wife Hannah 1. Ezra 2. Seth 3. Mary    
2 CONT     John and his 2nd wife Luany { Hoard } Strong 4. *Reuben William Strong ** My 3x great grandfather 5. Lydia  6. Simeon  memorial #13172576 7. John Jr 8. Daniel 9. Hannah ?
2 CONT
2 CONT  REUBEN married Hannah Galland,around 1841 Nauvoo Hancock county ILL.Per Nauvoo Temple Endowment Register p-353 A page353 A-1  Latter Day Saints Moorman Faith
2 CONT
2 CONT (NOTE: Per the State of Iowa's 1850 census,taken 10 th day of October Pottawattamie county Iowa
2 CONT  Reuben 30 Born NY 
2 CONT  Hannah 26 Born Iowa,   Hannah (Galland) Strong
2 CONT  Joseph 4 Born Iowa
2 CONT  Hiram Less than a year old Hiram's head stone 1/22/1849
2 CONT
2 CONT      After his first wife,(Hannah Galland) Strong died in 1852 somewhere by the Loup River in Platte County NE (They were on a Morman Wagon Train headed for Salt Lake City Utah},of cholera after crossing the Loup River there were 
2 CONC also 3 other women that died around the same time. (( THE WAGON MASTER OF THE WAGON TRAIN THEY WERE ON WAS HEADED BY JOHN B. WALKER MORMON RECORDS SHOWS THAT THEY ARRIVED SALT LAKE CITY EARY OCTOBER IT STATES THAT REUBAN  ARRIVED 
2 CONC WITH TWO SONS HIRAM AND JOSEPH ))) After the death of Hannah Reuben and his 2 sons continued on to Salt Lake City. He married Louisa Markson, a member of the wagon train they were on.To this marriage there were no children.They se
2 CONC parated and Reuben moved back to Iowa before 1855 He next married Hannah Kemp of Shelby, County IA. NOTE When  Hannah( Kemp } married Reuben She had 2 children from a previous marriage Reuben and Hannah ( KEMP ) Strong had two Chi
2 CONC ldren Samuel  AND  David And Effie
2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben and Hannah (Kemp) were married 1857 (Iowa)
2 CONT ****1860  Census Taken 6/15/1860  Gallon Grove IOWA Reuben Strong Head of house  Age 40 Hannah (Kemp}Strong Wife      Age 32    New York   Joseph  Son   Age  12  Born  Iowa Hiram   Son   Age  10  Born  Iowa
2 CONT     Step Daughters  Alice         Age 6  ****Born Illinois Rosetta       Age 4 Born Iowa 
2 CONT     Reuben and Hannah {Kemp) Strong 1. Samual S. Birth: Sep/23/1858
2 CONT
2 CONT  1870 Census Gallands Grove (Shelby County Iowa} Reuben Strong   Age 50 Jane            Age 36  This would be Jane (ENGLISH) Joseph          Age 23  Son of Reuben & Hannah Galland Hiram           Age 20  Son Of Reuben & Hannah Gal
2 CONC land Samual          Age 13  Son of Reuben & Hannah Kemp David           Age  7  Son of Reubem & Hannah Kemp Effie           Age  5  Daughter of Reuben & Hannah Kemp Lucinda  Craig    Age  8    STEP Daughter James    Craig    Age 
2 CONC  5    Step Son
2 CONT
2 CONT       REUBEN, married Jane maiden name English first husband (Davenport) (NO CHILDREN) Third husband (Craig )Two children Lucinda and James  Jane was from Nodaway, MO. To this union there were no children. Reuben and Jane homestea
2 CONC ded farm ground South of Meadow Grove Nebraska
2 CONT
2 CONT       REUBEN is believed to be buried in Madison County NE South of Meadow Grove NE 
2 CONT   This is the description of the land we think he is buried on West 1/4 of section 2,Township 23n,Range 4,,West of the 6th Principal Meridian  Madison county Nebraska,
2 CONT  There is also believed to be a grandson buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriages
2 CONT   1  Hannah Galland      MY 3 x Great Grandmother
2 CONT   2  Louisa Markson      NO Children
2 CONT   3  Hannah Kemp         Married OCT.15 1859
2 CONT   4  Lucinda Jane Craig  No Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben and Hannah {Kemp) Child Effie May (Strong)Galland Birth March 7 1865 Died 1958 Grand Island NE her daughter Elva lived there..  Effie's husband was Charles Galland B.1851 D 1929 There children were #1 Una May B.1889 D. 1969
