2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Phelps Hadden BIRTH	21 Oct 1845 Alden, McHenry County, Illinois, USA DEATH	May 1923 (aged 77) Janesville, Rock County, Wisconsin, USA BURIAL	 Oak Hill Cemetery Janesville, Rock County, Wisconsin, USA PLOT	71-10-6 MEMORIA
2 CONC L ID	139658714 · View Source MEMORIAL PHOTOS 1 FLOWERS 3 Daughter of Waterman Phelps and Mary Ann Marble.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Janesville Daily Gazette", Janesville, Wisconsin, Friday, May 18, 1923, p 9.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Sarah Elizabeth Hadden, 76, for the past 35 years a resident of Janesville, died Thursday afternoon at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Arthur M. Fisher, 435 North Terrace street, after a brief illness of pneumonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born at Harvard, Ill., the daughter of Waterman and Mary Phelps, coming with the family to Jefferson county, where her father located on a farm near Sumner. The marriage of William Hadden, whose death occurred in January, 
2 CONC 1922, and Miss Sarah Elizabeth Phelps, occurred Oct. 5, 1873 at Sumner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Hadden is survived by her daughter and two grandchildren, Cleland and Ruth Fisher, all of Janesville. The funeral, which will be private, will be held at 4 p. m. Saturday, from the residence of Mr. and Mrs. Arthur M. Fisher, 
2 CONC 435 North Terrace street. The Rev. F. J. Scribner, Congregational church, will officiate and burial will be made in Oak Hill cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT transcribed by Jon Saunders, contributor 47674050
