3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 OCCU Physician; apothecary
1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Dr. Peter Bulkeley''' (1643 – 1691) was a third-generation New England colonist and physician who resided in Fairfield, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Born August 12, 1643, in Concord, Massachusetts, Peter was the son of Rev. Peter Bulkeley and his second wife, Grace Chetwood. He attended Harvard College with the class of 1662, though he did not graduate, and trained in medicine
2 CONC . He settled in Fairfield, Connecticut, where he practiced as a physician and apothecary. He died in Fairfield in 1691, leaving an estate inventory that included Latin and English medical books and a collection of simple and compo
2 CONC und medicines.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT * Rev. Peter Bulkeley (1583 – 1659)
2 CONT * Grace Chetwood (1602 – 1669)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT
2 CONT * Margaret [maiden name unknown] (m. c. 1670). She was not Margaret Foxcroft.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT * Grace Bulkeley (b. c. 1670 – d. unknown)
2 CONT * Margaret Bulkeley (b. c. 1673 – d. after 1712)
2 CONT * Gershom Bulkeley (b. c. 1676 – d. unknown)
2 CONT * Peter Bulkeley "ye First" (b. December 25, 1683 – d. c. 1753), the '''cooper''' (barrel maker)., m. Margaret. 
2 CONT ** Peter "ye Second" (1684–1752): Son of Peter "ye First" (and husband of Hannah Ward) — the '''Weaver'''
2 CONT * Dorothy Bulkeley (b. c. 1686 – d. 1734), m. David Osborne (Sergt.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Primary & Archival Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT * Concord Town Records (Concord, Massachusetts):
2 CONT * Birth Record: Peter Bulkeley, born August 12, 1643, son of Peter Bulkeley and Grace his wife.
2 CONT * Fairfield Probate Records (Fairfield, Connecticut):
2 CONT * Inventory of the Estate of Dr. Peter Bulkeley: Taken March 9, 1690/91 (recorded Vol. 1689–1701, p. 58); includes medical library ("Books in Inglish and Lattin") and "medicene simple & in Composition" valued at 25 pounds.
2 CONT * Massachusetts Archives & Harvard College Records:
2 CONT * Harvard College Class Records (Class of 1662): Entry for Peter Bulkeley (non-graduating student).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Secondary & Compiled Reference Works
2 CONT
2 CONT * Anderson, Robert Charles. The Great Migration: Immigrants to New England, 1634–1635, Volume I, A–B. Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1999, p. 462.
2 CONT * Jacobus, Donald Lines. The Bulkeley Genealogy: Rev. Peter Bulkeley. New Haven, CT: Tuttle, Morehouse & Taylor Co., 1933, pp. 111, 127–128. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=2k87AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA127 GoogleBooks] > 
2 CONT * Sibley, John Langdon. Biographical Sketches of Graduates of Harvard University, in Cambridge, Massachusetts, Volume II (1659–1677). Cambridge, MA: Charles William Sever, 1881, pp. 118–119.
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bulkeley-73 (2nd Generation): Dr. Peter Bulkeley (1643–1691), who moved from Concord to Fairfield, Connecticut, and married Margaret.
