1 TITL Lt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas was skilled Indian interpreter and  served as a deputy to the Gerneral Court. He also fought in Queen Anne's War. One of the original settlers of Wethersfield, Connecticut, the family farm located at Nayaug 
2 CONC in Glastonbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aetatis about 44 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieutenant Thomas Treat, son of Corporal Richard and Sarah (Coleman) Treat, was born December 12, 1668 in Wethersfield, Hartford, Connecticut. On July 5, 1693 he married at Wethersfield Dorothy Bulkeley, daugher of Dr.-Rev. Gersho
2 CONC m and Sarah (Chauncy) Bulkeley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Dorothy Treat had 5 sons and 3 daughters from 1694-1710. Thomas died January 17, 1712/13 and was buried in Green Cemetery in Glastonbury. His wife Dorothy died before June 7, 1757.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents Richard Treat 1623–1693
2 CONT
