1 NOTE {geni:about_me} THE GROTON AVERY CLAN, Vol. I, by Elroy McKendree Avery and Catherine Hitchcock (Tilden) Avery, Cleveland, 1912.  p. 103
2 CONT ----
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 202
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT VITAL RECORDS OF NEW LONDON, NEW LONDON CO., CONN. Hannah - dau. Joshua & Elizabeth Raymond born 8th August 1668. VITAL RECORDS OF NEW LONDON, NEW LONDON CO., CONN. Wethersfield March 13- 1692/3. This may certify whome it may conc
2 CONC erne that Mr. Thomas Avery & Mrs. Hannah Buckley both of New London in their Majesties Colony of Conn. in New England married at Wethersfield afor'sd on the said day of the date of those presents. By or bofore me - John Chester, J
2 CONC ustice of Peace. True Copy. Sources: The Groton Avery Clan; Montville. Clan: Hannah (Raymond) Bulkley, daughter of Joshua and Elizabeth (Smith) Raymond and widow of Dr. Charles Bulkley. She was born 8 Aug. 1668 at Norwich. She and
2 CONC  Thomas Avery had seven children: Joshua, Mary, Elizabeth, Jonathan, Charles, Isaac and Peter. Montville: Hannah Raymond, had five children: Joshua, Elizabeth, Mary, Isaac and Charles by Thomas Avery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Raymond-26 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 15 2016, 13:54:36 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/142616987/hannah_avery
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, first, Dr. Charles Bulkley.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, second, on Mar 13,1693 at Wethersfield,CT, Thomas Avery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by first marriage): Hannah Bulkley Goodrich.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(by second marriage): Joshua Avery, Mary Avery Baker, Elizabeth Avery Baldwin, Jonathan Avery(whose first wife was Elizabeth Waterman Avery), Charles Avery, Isaac Avery, and Peter Avery.
