2 CONT Hester (Nichols) Prentice is a part of Connecticut History.
2 CONT Join: Connecticut Project
2 CONT Discuss: CONNECTICUT
2 CONT NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile was set as a PPP so that Hester would not be merged with her cousin Esther, who also married John Prentice.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st wife Hester Nichols - Stratford Fairfield, Connecticut. Daughter of John Nichols and his first un-named wife, NOT of his second wife Grace (unknown). Married John Prentis around 1651. Mother of most of the children.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd wife Esther Nichols - New London County, Connecticut. Daughter of Caleb Nichols and Anne Ward. Second wife of John Prentice, married in 1680 a year after his first wife Hester Nichols died.
2 CONT
2 CONT These two women are often thought of as the same person but in fact were first cousins (fathers were brothers). Esther was the mother of Valentine Prentice b. 1681.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester [Esther] Nichols was born about 1635 (Jacobus says only this, he does not say 18 Feb 1635 as was originally written on this profile)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the first wife of John Prentice, son of Valentine Prentice, who married her about 1651 in Roxbury, Massachusetts.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Bradstreet's Journal says: "Goodwife Prentice, aged about 44, or 40 dyed. She was a pious woman, and a very sweet nature, an excellent neighbor" She died 6 Jan 1679 New London, Middlesex, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT After Hester died, John married two more times and had two more children. He married, 2nd, 1685, Esther Nichols (Hester's 1st cousin); m., 3rd, Rebecca Parker, dau. of Ralph Parker. John died in 1691.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and his first wife, Hester Nichols:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Prentice b. 6 Aug. 1652; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 21 March 1714/15, New London, Ct.
2 CONT Joseph Prentice b. 2 Apr. 1655, New London, New London, Ct.; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 1 June 1676, New London, Ct., at 21 yrs.
2 CONT Jonathan Prentice b. 15 July 1657; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 28 July 1727.
2 CONT Hesther Prentice b. 20 July 1660; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 17 May 1751, Stonington, New London, Ct.; m., 1682, Boston, Suffolk, Mass., Benadam Gallup.
2 CONT Peter Prentice b. 31 July 1663; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 14 May 1670, at 7 yrs.
2 CONT Stephen Prentice b. 26 Nov. or Dec. 1666; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 30 April 1737, Niantic Ferry, New London, Ct.
2 CONT Mercy Prentice b. Dec. 1668, in New London, Ct.; d. Dec. 1689, at 21 yrs.
2 CONT Hannah Prentice b. June 1672, in New London, Ct.; d. 2 March 1717/18, Stonington, New London, Ct.; m., 15 Feb. 1693/94, Lieut. John Frink of Stonington.
2 CONT Thomas Prentice (twin), b. 6 Nov. 1675, in New London, Ct.; d. 5 Feb. 1740/41; m. 1st Mary Rogers; m. 2nd widow Elizabeth (--) Palmes; m3rd Bethiah Chapel
2 CONT Elizabeth Prentice (twin), b. 6 Nov. 1675, in New London, Ct.; d. 13 Dec. 1770, ae. 95. She m., 23 May 1700, Daniel Comstock.
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ HISTORY AND GENEALOGY OF THE FAMILIES OF OLD FAIRFIELD Compiled and Edited by DONALD LINES JACOBUS Originally Published Fairfield, Connecticut 1930-1932 Vol 1. p. 435
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 2.2 2.3 Donald Lines Jacobus, "John Prentice of New London, Conn. and His Two Nichols Wives" TAG 34(1958):81 $subscription
2 CONT S56 The American Genealogist. (TAG) New Haven, CT: D. L. Jacobus, 1937-. (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2009 - .)
2 CONT Find A Grave: Memorial #38851854
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Torrey's New England Marriages Prior to 1700, page 601
2 CONT
2 CONT Torrey's NE Marriages says:  Esther / Hester [Williams?] Nichols?  died 6 January 1679/80 at age 44.  Married 1652 in New London.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first Hester Nichols, who was the daughter of John Nichols and his wife Grace. He married second Esther Nichols, daughter of Caleb Nichols and his wife Anne Ward. Hester and Esther were first cousins. (John and Caleb we
2 CONC re brothers.) His third wife was Rebecca Parker, with whom he had no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hester Nichols about 1651 and they had issue:
2 CONT # John P. Prentice who married Sarah Jones
2 CONT # Joseph Prentice
2 CONT # Jonathan Prentties, who married Elizabeth
2 CONT # Esther Prentice, who married Benadam Gallup
2 CONT # Peter Prentice
2 CONT # Stephen Prentice
2 CONT # Mercy Prentice
2 CONT # Hannah Prentice
2 CONT # Thomas Prentice, twin
2 CONT # Elizabeth Prentice, twin
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Esther Nichols 1680 in Connecticut and they had issue:
2 CONT # Valentine Prentice (note; she died shortly after his birth)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Born on Feb. 18, 1635 on Fairfield, Fairfield County, Connecticut,and died Jan. 6, 1679 age 44 in Mystic, New London County, Connecticut.  Buried in White Hall Graveyard, Mystic, New London County, Connecticut.  She was the daught
2 CONC er of John Nichols and his wife Grace. She was the first wife of John Prentice (1628 - 1691), who married her 1651/1652 in Roxbury, Massachusetts (or New London, CT).
2 CONT
2 CONT Torrey's New England Marriages Prior to 1700, page 601
2 CONT
2 CONT Torrey's NE Marriages says:  Esther / Hester [Williams?] Nichols?  died 6 January 1679/80 at age 44.  Married 1652 in New London.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Prentice  married first Hester Nichols, who was the daughter of John Nichols and his wife Grace. He married second Esther Nichols, daughter of Caleb Nichols and his wife Anne Ward. Hester and Esther were first cousins. (John 
2 CONC and Caleb were brothers.) His third wife was Rebecca Parker, with whom he had no issue.
2 CONT
