2 CONT Biography[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hester [Esther] Nichols was the daughter of John Nichols and his wife. She was born on February. 18, 1635, Fairfield, Fairfield, Connecticut.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the first wife of John Prentice, son of Valentine Nichols, who married her 1651 in Roxbury, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John and his first wife, Hester Nichols:
2 CONT
2 CONT John, b. 6 Aug. 1652; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 21 March 1714/15, New London, Ct. Joseph3, b. 2 Apr. 1655, New London, New London, Ct.; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 1 June 1676, New L
2 CONC ondon, Ct., at 21 yrs. Jonathan, b. 15 July 1657; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 28 July 1727. Hesther, b. 20 July 1660; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 17 May 1751, Stonington, New London, C
2 CONC t.; m., 1682, Boston, Suffolk, Mass., Benadam Gallup. Peter, b. 31 July 1663; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mass.; d. 14 May 1670, at 7 yrs. Stephen, b. 26 Nov. or Dec. 1666; bapt. 19 Apr. 1668, at Roxbury, Suffolk, Mas
2 CONC s.; d. 30 April 1737, Niantic Ferry, New London, Ct. Mercy, b. Dec. 1668, in New London, Ct.; d. Dec. 1689, at 21 yrs. Hannah, b. June 1672, in New London, Ct.; d. 2 March 1717/18, Stonington, New London, Ct.; m., 15 Feb. 1693/94,
2 CONC  Lieut. John Frink of Stonington. Thomas (twin), b. 6 Nov. 1675, in New London, Ct.; d. 5 Feb. 1740/41; m. 1st Mary Rogers; m. 2nd widow Elizabeth (--) Palmes; m3rd Bethiah Chapel Elizabeth (twin), b. 6 Nov. 1675, in New London, C
2 CONC t.; d. 13 Dec. 1770, ae. 95. She m., 23 May 1700, Daniel Comstock. Hester died on January 6, 1679, Mystic, New London, Connecticut, and was buried White Hall Graveyard, Mystic, New London, Connecticut, USA.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT After Hester died, John married two more time and had two more children. He married, 2nd, 1685, Esther Nichols (Hester's 1st cousin); m., 3rd, Rebecca Parker, dau. of Ralph Parker. John died in 1691.
2 CONT
