2 CONT * married (1) Esther/Hester Nichols in 1652 in New London, CT and she died January 1679/80; (2) her cousin Esther Nichols, daughter of Caleb after 1680; (3) Rebecca Parker, daughter of Ralph, married June 19 1685 New London, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born May 6, 1628, England and died Jan. 1, 1691 in Mystic, New London County, Connecticut, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Chelmsford, Essex, England to Valentine Prentice and his wife Alice B_____.  John arrived at the age of three in Massachusetts aboard the Lyon with his parents November 2, 1631.
2 CONT
2 CONT His occupations were recorded as being both a blacksmith and seaman. He lived in Boston in 1631; Roxbury in 1632; and New London in 1652. He retained his membership in the Roxbury church and baptized his children there.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first Hester Nichols, who was the daughter of John Nichols and his wife Grace. He married second Esther Nichols, daughter of Caleb Nichols and his wife Anne Ward. Hester and Esther were first cousins. (John and Caleb we
2 CONC re brothers.) His third wife was Rebecca Parker, with whom he had no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hester Nichols about 1651 and they had issue:
2 CONT # John P. Prentice who married Sarah Jones
2 CONT # Joseph Prentice
2 CONT # Jonathan Prentties, who married Elizabeth
2 CONT # Esther Prentice, who married Benadam Gallup
2 CONT # Peter Prentice
2 CONT # Stephen Prentice
2 CONT # Mercy Prentice
2 CONT # Hannah Prentice
2 CONT # Thomas Prentice, twin
2 CONT # Elizabeth Prentice, twin
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Esther Nichols 1680 in Connecticut and they had issue:
2 CONT # Valentine Prentice (note; she died shortly after his birth)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Rebecca Parker 1685, there was no issue from this marriage. (Note: I have found no record for a Ralph Prentice, who some believe was a son of his third marriage. Rebecca was 57 years old when she married John.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=38754941
2 CONT
