2 CONT [hide] 1 Biography 1.1 Baptism 1.2 Marriage 1.3 Death 1.4 Burial 1.5 Notes 1.6 Notes 2 Sources 2.1 Footnotes Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Valentine Prentice was born 6 May 1628 at Chelmsford, Essex, England and died 1691 at New London, New London Co., CT. “John Prentice, son of Valentine & Alice (_______) Prentice, born in England, came from Roxbury, Mass., to 
2 CONC New London, Conn. He married first, about 1651, Hester[Esther] Nichols, born about 1635, died at New London, 6 Jan. 1679/80, daughter of John Nichols of Fairfield, Conn., by his unknown first wife; she was mother of his first eigh
2 CONC t children. He married second, probably by 1683, Esther Nichols, born at Stratford, Conn., 18 Feb. 1652/3, daughter of Caleb and Anne (Ward) Nichols of Stratford and Woodbury, Conn., and his first wife’s first cousin although much
2 CONC  younger; she was mother of his ninth child, Valentine, and presumably died at his birth or shortly after. He married third, by contract dated 12 June 1685 [New London Deeds, 4:51], Rebecca Parker, the jointure referring to any ch
2 CONC ildren he may have by her. John Prentice apparently died late in 1691. Rebecca was mother of his tenth child, Ralph.”[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Prentice, New London's blacksmith, who turned ship captain, became a consummate sailor capable of journeying to Europe and outsailing pirates. He owned the largest boat built in New London during the seventeenth century, but
2 CONC  died fairly young at the age of sixty-three in 1691. He had eleven children with his first wife Hester Nichols, and one more child with his second wife Esther Nichols. Three of his sons continued the maritime activities he initia
2 CONC ted and his eldest son, John, was also Commander of Fort New London for many years." [2]
2 CONT
