1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 376
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Hannah Prentice was the daughter of Capt. John and Hester (Nichols) Prentice born Jun 1672 and baptized 7 July 1672 in New London, New London Co., Connecticut. She married Lieut. John Frink on 15 February 1693/94 at Stonington, Ne
2 CONC w London Co., Connecticut. She died [March 2, 1718 (see https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/219088066/hannah-frink)] at Stonington, New London Co., Connecticut. (TAG 34:81-5)(Caulkins p. 389)
2 CONT
2 CONT Frink Family in America pp. 4-5
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN FRINK (2): John (1)
2 CONT B. May 18,1671 at Stonington. D. Nov.14,1753. His will was proved June 26, 1754 in New London, Conn. He is buried in the Burdick Yard, Betsy Kenyon Farm, near Stonington. M. Hannah Prentice (Prentiss) Feb. 15,1694, daughter of Cap
2 CONC t. John Prentice and Hester Nichols Prentice of New
2 CONT London. She was b. in June, 1672.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Ensign, 3rd Co., Stonington, in May,1728 and was promoted to Lt. of the company in October,1729. In the 1850's a whaling ship company still sailed out of New London under the name Frink & Prentis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT i. John, b. Oct. 7, 1694. D. March 2, 1718.
2 CONT ii. Nicholas, b. Dec. 17,1696. D. July 8,1749. M. Deborah Pendleton Nov. 30,1715. 9 children.
2 CONT iii. Thomas, b. Jan. 15,1700. Died unmarried, probably in 1781; his will was probated in 1782.
2 CONT iv. Hannah, b. Nov. 27,1701. Thomas' will indicates that she was already dead when it was made.
2 CONT M. Samuel Utley Aug. 22, 1723. 10 children.
2 CONT v. Zachariah, b. Nov. 4, 1702. D. Dec. 28, 1777. M. Elizabeth Gallup March 4, 1730. 10 children.
2 CONT vi. Mary, bapt. April 19, 1705. Died before her brother Thomas, according to his will. M. Jeremiah
2 CONT Utley Nov. 9, 1725. 1 son.
2 CONT vii. Joseph, bapt. June 6, 1708. Died before his brother, Thomas. M. Judith Palmer June 12, 1732.
2 CONT Thomas' will indicates that Joseph had heirs, but there is no record of them so far.
2 CONT viii. Benjamin, b. Jan. 25, 1710. M. Tacy Burdick Jan. 12, 1732. 9 children.
2 CONT ix. William, b. 1712, bapt. March 10, 1714. D.y.
2 CONT x. Thankful, b. Feb. 8, 1714. M. Richard Crouch
2 CONT xi. Esther (Easter), bapt. Jan. 23, 1716/17. M. Peter Crandall Dec. 22,1740, Westerly, R.I.
2 CONT 6 children.
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Stone Missing
