1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DENISON GENEALOGY, ANCESTORS AND DESCENDANTS OF CAPTAIN GEORGE DENISON, Of Stonington Connecticut, by John Denison Baldwin and William Clift, Worcester, MA, 1881, p 8
2 CONT ----
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, county of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 293
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1. From the records of the First Church of Preston, Connecticut: "May 1 4, 1702, spouse of Joseph Prentice owned the Covenant." Our best definition of "Covenant" is: An agreement among members of church to hold to points of doctri
2 CONC ne, faith, etc. It appears then that Hannah had the responsibility to carry out the duties and obligations set down in the Covenant or in other words the "Covenator."
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Also from the records of the First Church of Preston: "July 8, 170 5, Hannah, spouse of Joseph Prentice, admitted to communion"
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 4 children 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Hannah the daughter of Nathaniel and Hannah (Denison) Chesebrough was born in 1671.<ref name="Wildly">Wildly, Mary Chesebrough. ''Genealogy of the Descendants of William Chesebrough of Boston, Rehoboth, Mass.  The Founder and Firs
2 CONC t White Settler of Stonington, Conn….'' New York: Press of T.A. White, 1903</ref> Hannah Cheesebrough married Joseph Prentice Nov 25 or 26 1700.<ref>Stonington Vital Records. Apparently it has been interpreted as both overthe year
2 CONC s. The Barbour Collection of Stonington Vital records lists it as the 25th.</ref>  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: According to Wildly in the Descendants of William Chesebrough...<ref name="Wildly"/> All Baptized at the First Church of Preston.
2 CONT # [[Prentice-572|Joseph]], bap. March 14, 1703
2 CONT # Nathaniel, bap. Oct 14, 1705 Error ? see note below
2 CONT # Josiah, bap. Oct 14, 1705  ERROR? see note below.
2 CONT # Hannah, bap. March 21, 1708
2 CONT # [[Prentice-208|Elihu]], bap. July 20, 1712; m. Abigail Jamison Josiah # 3 & Nathaniel # 2 may be errors. There is no Josiah listed inthe Church index.<ref>Connecticut Church Records, State Library Index, Preston First Congregati
2 CONC onal Church 1698-1883. Hartford: ConnecticutState Library, 1943. Available online at Ancestry.</ref> There is Nathaniel, son of Josiah and Hannah baptized Oct 14, 1705. The original records would need to be checked to see if both 
2 CONC Josiah and Nathaniel were baptized the same day, and someone along the way put Josiah in as father of Nathaniel instead of two sons of Joseph.[[B-404|B-404]] 17:58, 11 May 2014 (EDT)  
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
