1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John, son of David Lamb (of) Ston(ingto)n bpt 13 Jul. 1740 by Rev. Treat, Preston First Church Records 1-34, P-151 (Church Records, CT State Library - Barbour Collection) 
2 CONT
2 CONT John was born to David Lamb and his second wife, Esther Smith, of Stonington, CT.  
2 CONT
2 CONT WOUND RECEIVED OFF COAST OF SPAIN: John Lamb (David, John) born in Stonington, 2 Jun 1740, was a sea captain. Died in Preston 4 Mar 1804 "in consequence of a wound received in a shipwreck on the coast of Spain". Gave service on se
2 CONC a for the Revolution, married Lucy Bulkely, one child, Henry F. went to Wilkes-Barre, PA. ... ("Lamb Families in CT Before 1800" Pg 58, by Frank B. Lamb)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Capt) John Lamb born in Stonington, CT 2 Jun. 1740; died in  Preston, CT 4 Mar 1804. Mr. Lamb was a sea captain and gave service at sea during the Revolution. He was of New London, 1774, Stonington, 1781, Norwich 1783 and 1792. H
2 CONC e died in consequence of a wound received in a shipwreck on the coast of Spain, and was then a resident of Groton, CT. Administration was granted to his widow Lucy, 1 Sep. 1807. ("The Bulkeley Genealogy" by Donald Lines Jacobus, 1
2 CONC 933, Pg 290)* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18330823/john-lamb Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 30 2023, 6:08:20 UTC''
