2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/77641291/person/32378071703 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 25 2017, 23:17:06 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT There is an erroneous note on the Findagrave page for this man that his father was Eliphalet Bulkeley. Primary documentation listing him as Charles Jr., as well as existing genealogies for the Bulkeley family, support that he was 
2 CONC indeed the son of Charles Bulkeley, Sr., and Elizabeth "Betsey" Taintor. For a complete accounting of this man's multiple wives and children, see Jacobus, Donald. The Bulkeley genealogy; Rev. Peter Bulkeley, being an account of hi
2 CONC s career, his ancestry, the ancestry of his two wives, and his relatives in England and New England, together with a genealogy of his descendants through the seventh American generation. Available here [https://babel.hathitrust.or
2 CONC g/cgi/pt?id=wu.89080561269;view=1up;seq=308] and here [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89080561269;view=1up;seq=730]. 
2 CONT Son of Charles Bulkley and Betsey Taintor.
2 CONT .
2 CONT Husband of:
2 CONT .
2 CONT 1) Lucy Beman, whom he married on Dec. 9, 1801, in Hampton, Washington, NY, and with whom he had six known children: 
2 CONT Betsey Taintor Bulkley
2 CONT Charlotte Abigail Bulkley
2 CONT Anna Maria Bulkley
2 CONT Charles Addison Bulkley 
2 CONT Frances Caroline Bulkley
2 CONT Nathan Beman Bulkley.
2 CONT .
2 CONT 2) Cynthia (Powers) Rossiter, whom he married on Dec. 25, 1813, in Williamstown, Berkshire, MA, and with whom he had one known child: 
2 CONT Melissa Cynthia Bulkley.
2 CONT .
2 CONT 3) Chloe Beebe, whom he married July 12, 1816, and with whom he had five known children: 
2 CONT Infant son Bulkley
2 CONT Sarah Beebe Bulkley
2 CONT Frances Caroline Bulkley
2 CONT Edward Henry Bulkley (1823-1827), 
2 CONT Edward Henry Bulkley
2 CONT .* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/68624903/charles-bulkley Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 30 2023, 2:27:24 UTC''
