3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Gershom Taintor Bulkley'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Monroe Port Commissioner
2 CONT * City Merchant
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom Taintor was the great-grandson of Rev. Peter Bulkley, D.D. who was one of the first clergymen of Massachusetts and Connecticut, coming from England to Cambridge, Massachusetts. in 1635. One of the many Puritans that left E
2 CONC ngland because of the oppressions of the church. The families of New York, Massachusetts, and Connecticut are all descended from Dr. Peter Bulkley. He moved with his family to Monroe, Michigan. In 1836, coming from Williamstown, M
2 CONC assachusetts. He was one of the commissioners of the Government Works at the Harbor of Monroe, and in the constructing of the canal. He engaged in mercantile affairs and farming until the later years of his life. In 1843 and 1844,
2 CONC  and again in 1846, Gershom served as Supervisor of Monroe Township, Monroe County, Michigan before the re-organization of the townshp.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his 83rd year, death occurred at Monroe, Michigan.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom Taintor was the father of ten children, six sons and four daughters, all of whom, survived him.  Gershom  preceded his wife Julia in death.  The middle name of Taintor derives from his mother's maiden name; she was Betsey 
2 CONC Taintor of Williamstown, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gershom Taintor Bulkley was laid to rest in Woodland Cemetery in the Bulkley family lot.
2 CONT
