1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Rev. David Lord Perry=
2 CONT * BIRTH 21 Jun 1777
2 CONT * DEATH 25 Oct 1835 (aged 58) Sharon, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Hillside Cemetery Sharon, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA GPS-Latitude: 41.8821302, Longitude: -73.477672
2 CONT * PLOT Section A Plot 10
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  21045199 Pictures added by Jim Lawson
2 CONT
2 CONT Ordained Jun 6, 1804
2 CONT Married 1805 to Anna Strong in CT.
2 CONT Listed in the 1820 and 1830 census records for Sharon, Litchfield Co., CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Obituary==  
2 CONT DIED, In Sharon, on Sunday, the 25th ult. Rev. David L. Perry, aged 59. He had for some weeks been suffering from an attack of paralysis, but was comfortable till a renewed attack just before his death. He was the father of Rev. J
2 CONC . M. S. Perry, missionary to Ceylon, and is taken from a widow and numerous children, and from an affectionate people whom he has thirty years faithfully served in the ministry. His people have never before, for more than 80 years
2 CONC , been destitute of a settled pastor.[2]
2 CONT
