1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Deborah Warren
2 CONT * Birth: about 1652 in Exeter, Rockingham, New Hampshire
2 CONT * Death: 15 Feb 1718 at about age 66 in Little Compton, Rhode Island
2 CONT *Parents: John Warren and Deborah Wilson
2 CONT * Wife of William Hilliard — married 12 Jun 1671 in Hingham, Plymouth, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hilliard (son of William Hilliard and Hester) married before 26 JAN 1671/2 to Deborah Warren (daughter of John Warren and Deborah Wilson).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # [--?--] HILLIARD b: 26 JAN 1671/2 in Hingham, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT # William HILLIARD b: 21 JAN 1672/3 in Hingham, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT # John HILLIARD b: 16 FEB 1674/5 in Hingham, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT # Simon HILLIARD b: 14 MAR 1675/6 in Hingham, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT # David HILLIARD b: 25 FEB 1677/8 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Deborah HILLIARD b: 7 JUN 1680 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Isaac HILLIARD b: 19 APR 1683 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Esther HILLIARD b: 8 MAR 1684/5 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Mary HILLIARD b: 3 APR 1687 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Abigail HILLIARD b: 12 JUL 1690 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Sarah HILLIARD b: 28 JUN 1692 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT # Jonathan HILLIARD b: 8 NOV 1696 in Little Compton, Newport, RI
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Deborah was recorded in Taunton, book 3, part 1 page 385 made 21 JAN 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT ". . .to my beloved son David Hilliard two shillings. To my beloved son Jonathan Hilliard two shillings. To my beloved daughter Deborah the wife of John Padduck fifty shillings. To my beloved daughter Esther the wife of Jerimiah G
2 CONC eers twenty shillings. To mty beloved daughter Abigail wife of Warren Gibbs five shillings. To my beloved daughter Sarah Hilliard one cow & all my iron pewter & brass. To my foure grand children that are the children of my daughte
2 CONC r Mary Palmer deceased ten shillings apiece. The remainder of my estate shall be equally divided between my two youngest daughters viz. Abigail & Sarah. Executor to be son David Hilliard . . . ." Deborah Hilliard
2 CONT
2 CONT
