1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patriot of the American Revolution
2 CONT https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A124836
2 CONT WHITING, WILLIAM JR  DAR Ancestor #: A124836
2 CONT Service:  CONNECTICUT    Rank(s): PRIVATE
2 CONT Birth:  12-16-1758    HARTFORD HARTFORD CO CONNECTICUT
2 CONT Death:  3-22-1849     WARSAW WYOMING CO NEW YORK
2 CONT Pension Number:  *S11746
2 CONT Service Source:  *S11746
2 CONT Service Description:  1) CAPTS KIMBALL, NEHEMIAH RICE; COLS CHANDLER, RUSSELL, JOSEPH HOYT
2 CONT 2) 8TH REGT, CT LINE
2 CONT
2 CONT All Children by 1st Wife
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives of William Whiting II
2 CONT
2 CONT  1) ABIGAIL FLOWER  
2 CONT  2) LUCINDA X WHITING  
2 CONT  3) PHEBE X RICH  
2 CONT  4) ELIZABETH NOBLE  
2 CONT
2 CONT Find A Grave link
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/19360653/william-whiting
2 CONT
2 CONT William WHITING, Sen., was born in Hartford, CT, in 1748 or ‘49, & married Abigail Flower, of the same place. They removed, with several children, to Granville, NY thence to Hampton, & from there to Warsaw about the year 1820. Mr.
2 CONC  WHITING was a soldier of the Revolution, a good citizen & a member of the Baptist church. His wife died 25 Aug 1882, aged 73 years. After her death he was married three times. His second wife was Mrs. Lucinda WHITING, a brother's
2 CONC  widow, who died 10 Sep 1838, aged 67; this third, Mrs. Phebe RICH, widow of Peter RICH; his fourth, the widow of Lyman NOBLE, who also is dead. He died March 22, 1849, aged 90 years. He had eight children all by his first wife, v
2 CONC iz: Lucy, Catharine, William, Abigail, Nathan, Sophrona, Demmon, Timothy.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1818 granted pension from the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT Soldier of the Revolution In a pension request, William Whiting stated he was living in a house owned by Silas C. Fargo "which in stormy weather does not protect our gray hairs from the wind & rain." Mr. Whiting appears to have be
2 CONC en at or near destitution. The Warsaw vital records show William as being a carpenter who died of old age.
2 CONT
2 CONT For more info Our Folk - Hart family Web Site.
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT Wm. Whiting died Mar 22, 1849 Aged 90yrs
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Revolutionary War soldier marker, 1759 - 1849
