1 NAME Daniel /Henry/ Jr.
2 GIVN Daniel
2 NSFX Jr.
2 _MARNM Henry
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1630
2 ADDR
3 CITY Farnham Parish
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1708
2 ADDR
3 CITY St. Anne's Parish
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daniel was born about 1650, probably at Farnham Parish, Old Rappahannock County, Virginia Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Henry married in 1706 at South Farnham Parish, Essex County, to Dorothy Unknown. Dorothy had previously married, as her 1st, to Augustine North.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy and Augustine North had three known children, but Dorothy and Henry had no known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 10 March 1706/7, Daniel Henry, of St. Ann's Parish Essex County, gave to Susannah Ley my Grand-daughter in Law of same. For Love, good will and affection Two negoes Jenny and Rachel.
2 CONT Daniel Henry
2 CONT Wit William Thompson. John Butler, Garrett Neaill, Joseph (M) Winge.
2 CONT 10 March 1706/7 Acknowledged by Daniel Henry
2 CONT Death and Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT On 10 April 1708, Dorothy Henry petitioned the Essex County Court for administration of the estate of her late husband, Daniel Henry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 Torrence, Clayton, (1927) "Winston of Virginia" Richmond: Whittet & Shepperson HathiTrust.org (Pages 183-87).
2 CONT ↑ Dorothy MNU North Early Colonial Settlers of Southern Maryland and Virginia's Northern Neck Counties, citing 1706-1718 Essex County Deed & Will Book. by John Frederick Dorman, Page 371.
