1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas Gouldman was born about 1670[1], a son of Captain Thomas Gouldman and Alice (Unknown) Gouldman (p 171).[2] After the death of his father, Captain Thomas, in December 1684, mother Alice married, as her 2nd, t
2 CONC o Arthur Forbes.[2] Alice died in Essex County in 1698 (p 170).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Very little is known about Thomas Gouldman. As Torrence writes, "His name does not appear in the records in any official capacity and quite evidently he followed the simple life of a planter, dying a young man in the later part of
2 CONC  the year 1698 (p 174).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married about 1697, as her 2nd, to Dorothy (North) Awbrey, widow of Richard Awbrey, and daughter of Augustine and Dorothy (Unknown) North (p 174).[2] After Thomas died, Dorothy married, as her 3rd, to Peter Ransone.[2][3]
2 CONT Death and Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas died a young man, in the later part of 1698 in Essex County.[2] Transcription of Thomas's Last Will & Testament, written on 22 May 1698 and proved on 10 November 1698, is published in Torrence (pp 176-77).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 11 August 1699, Essex County court, Dorothy Gouldman, executrix appeared to return the inventory and appraisement for the estate of Thomas. This was continued to the next court, 11 September 1699, when Peter Ransone and his wif
2 CONC e, Dorothy, widow of Thomas Gouldman, appeared.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Elizabeth and Thomas Gouldman (p 175):[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Gouldman, posthumous b c. 1698; m c. 1713/4 to Thomas Waring of Essex County, Virginia
2 CONT Will
2 CONT
2 CONT Date of will: 22 May 1698
2 CONT Date of Probate: 10 November 1698
2 CONT In the name of God Amen I Thomas Gouldman being Sick and weak of Body but of South & perfect memory blessed & praised by Almighty God for ye same do make & ordaine this my last will & tesamt. in manner & forme following first & pr
2 CONC incipally I comend my Soul to Almighty God my Creatre. that gave it assuredly believing that shall receive full pardon & remission of all my Sinns and to saved by ye precious death & merits of my blessed Savior & redeemer Christ J
2 CONC esus and my body to ye earth from whence it was taken to be buried in Such decent & Christian manner as to my Exrs. hereafter named Shall be thought meet & convenient and as for Such worldly Goods that it hath pleased God to lend 
2 CONC me I will bequeath dispose of & give in manner & forme following. I. First I give & bequeath my Lands unto my child that my wife is now with Child off and to ye heirs of its body lawfully begotten but if it Shall please God that m
2 CONC y said child die without such heirs then I give ye said Land to my brother Robert Gouldman & to ye heirs of his body lawfully begotten and for want of Such heirs to ye next Succeeding heirs of the name of Gouldman. And it is my wi
2 CONC ll that my sd. Land after my death be in ye possession of my Sd. brother Robt. Gouldman until my child aforesd. come to age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give to my brother Robt. Gouldman one servant Boy named Patrick one ffeather bed & ffurniture now at my mothers Mrs. Alice fforbesses one Suit of Cloathes with plate buttons a Caster Hatt a pr. of Legg Bootes Twelve Shillin
2 CONC gs to buy a Ring & all ye Goods at my Mothers ye Molasses excepted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give unto my dear Mother Mrs. Alice fforbes twenty shillings to buy a Ring.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give unto my brother ffra Gouldman twelve shillings to buy a Ring.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item I give unto my brother Edward Gouldman one Servant Man named Kelly & twelve Shillings to buy a ring.
2 CONT
2 CONT As for ye rest of ye estate wch. it hath pleased God to bless me withall in this life I give & bequeath to be equally divided between my beloved wife Dorothy Gouldman & my Child or Children that my sd. wife now is with Child off.
2 CONT
2 CONT And of this my last will & Testamt. I make my beloved wife Dorothy Gouldman and my loveing brother ffrancis Gouldman exrs. desiring Mr Tho Grgeson that he will see this my last will & Testamt. truely p. formed & I do hereby utterl
2 CONC y disallow revoke & annul all & every other former Testamt. wills Legacies bequests & Exrx. by me in anywise heretofore named willed & bequeathed ratifieing & confirming this & none other to be my last will & Testamt. In witness w
2 CONC hereof I have hereunto Set my hand & Seale this twenty Second day of May in ye year of our Lord one thousand and Six hundred ninety eight. Thom. Gouldman (Seal)
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed published pronounced & declared be ye d. Tho. Gouldman as his last will & Testamt. in presence of John (his--X--marke) Moodies William T. (his mark) Dear, Thomas (his--X--marke) Hucklescott. 1698. Proved by ye oaths 
2 CONC of ye witnesses hereto in Essex County Court ye 10th Day of November 1698 & truely Recorded. Test Francis Meriweather Cl Cur. (Essex County Records, Volume 1695-99, pages 272-4.)
2 CONT
