1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biographical Summary===
2 CONT Peter Ransom (c. 1672 – 1759) was an 18th-century planter in Virginia, documented primarily through land records and court proceedings in Gloucester and Essex Counties. He is the son of Captain James Ransome (c. 1645–1706) and gra
2 CONC ndson of the immigrant Peter Ransome. He is perhaps best known for his marriage to Dorothy North, a woman who had previously been widowed twice before their union. Like many of his ancestors, his life is documented through fragmen
2 CONC tary colonial court records, and while his lineage to the immigrant Peter Ransome is supported by legal testimony, the specifics of his personal life remain largely obscured by the destruction of early county archives.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==•Parentage===
2 CONT Father: Captain James Ransome (c. 1645 – c. 1706).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Mary Baldwin (identified in some secondary reconstructions; verification remains difficult due to lost records).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical Note: Peter’s connection to his father, James, and his grandfather, the immigrant Peter Ransome, is supported by historical evidence, including land patent records and court litigation (e.g., Booth vs. Dudley).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Vital Statistics===
2 CONT Birth: c. 1672, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: After February 1759 (date of a land record documenting his residence in York County).  
2 CONT
2 CONT Place of Death: Likely Gloucester or York County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and Issue===
2 CONT Spouse: Dorothy North (c. 1669 – after 1748).  
2 CONT (Note: Dorothy was the daughter of Augustine North and Dorothy (Unknown) Henry. She married three times: (1) Richard Awbrey, (2) Thomas Gouldman, and (3) Peter Ransome.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children (Attributed):
2 CONT  1. Elizabeth Ransome (c. 1700 – 1776)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Ann June Ransome (c. 1709 – 1778)  
2 CONT
2 CONT )Note: Some sources also associate a Richard Ransom (1680–1759) with this family line, though further primary documentation is needed to confirm the exact parentage of all children in this group.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Documented Facts & Sources===
2 CONT Marriage Context: Court records from Essex County, Virginia, identify Peter Ransome as the third husband of "Mrs. Dorothy (North) Awbrey Gouldman." Their union followed her tenure as the executrix of her second husband's estate.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Legal Records: On July 11, 1706, an action was brought against Peter Ransome by Daniel Henry and Dorothy (North) Henry regarding the estate of Augustine North, demonstrating the complex legal entanglements of the families in Essex
2 CONC  County.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence: Records from 1759 place Peter living in York County, Virginia, which is the final known primary documentation of his life.  
2 CONT Historical Context and Research Challenges
2 CONT
2 CONT The "North" Connection: Dorothy North’s background links this branch of the Ransome family to the North and Henry families of St. Anne's Parish, Essex County. Understanding her legal maneuvers as a widow provides insight into how 
2 CONC colonial women managed property and family estates.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Data Collision: Because "Peter Ransome" is a name passed down through three generations of this family, researchers often encounter confusion between the immigrant Peter (d. 1663) and this Peter (the grandson). Always cross-refere
2 CONC nce dates and geographic locations—Gloucester vs. York vs. Essex—to ensure you are tracking the correct individual.
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Status: This profile reflects a reconstruction based on extant court orders and land records. Due to the loss of parish registers, the birth dates of his children and the exact timeline of his later years remain estimates
2 CONC  rather than confirmed facts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Variant spelling of the name===
2 CONT The name was spelled variously (like many of our 17th C. ancestors), but most often "Ransone" and sometimes "Ranson." "Ransone" is the spelling used by researchers and writers: The William and Mary Quarterly article is titled, "Ra
2 CONC nsone Family," and Tyler and Torrence use the "Ransone" spelling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the later generations (about 1800 and later) used the spelling "Ransom," such as Gen. Matt Ransom (b 1826).
2 CONT
2 CONT Origin:
2 CONT Peter Ransone was born about 1670 in Gloucester County, apparently named after his grandfather who was the immigrant. Peter was the son of Capt James Ransone and an unknown mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter married, as her 3rd, to Dorothy (North) Awbrey Gouldman, widow of 1) Richard Awbrey, 2) Thomas Gouldman, and daughter of Augustine North.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === Peter’s Will===
2 CONT "September 11, 1699, Peter Ransone and Dorothy, his wife, executrix of Thomas Gouldman, deceased, to return the inventory and appraisement of the said decedent's estate ..." (Page 174).
2 CONT
2 CONT 1699-1702 Essex Co VA Order Book; Antient Press: Page 14) Essex County Court 11th of September 1699
