1 NAME Richard /Straughan/ IV
2 GIVN Richard
2 SURN Straughan
2 NSFX IV
2 _MARNM Strawn
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Ledbetter Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 STAE Tennessee
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 MAR 1761
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1841
2 ADDR
3 STAE Tennessee
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Farmer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Enlisted in the North Carolina Line during the Revolutionary War using Straughan as his surname as he was born. However, he signed his discharge papers both as Straughan and as Strawn and thereafter went by Strawn.
2 CONC  Both surnames are variations of the name Strachan which comes from a small town in Aberdeenshire named Strachan but pronounced Strawn. Buried in Ledbetter Cemetery in Hardin County, Tennessee where he moved after the war. A monum
2 CONC ent furnished by the Federal government marks his grave as veteran of the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Richard (Straughan) Strawn shortened his name to Strawn.  He signed his name both ways to his discharge papers from the Revoluntionary War and later moved west to Hardin Co., Tenn.  He is buried in Ledbetter Cemetery; one of the f
2 CONC irst, if not the first, buried there.  A monument furnished by the Federal Government, was erected there by Lloyd Strawn (brother of Emmet Dee Strawn) of the New Hope Community, RFD Adamsville, Tenn.  (The Strawn Genealogy (1680-1
2 CONC 964) compiled by Emmet Dee Strawn and Published by J. Frank Strawn, 1965.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard  was in the Revolution War in Halls Company of the North Carolina Line.  His wife was Celia and he had a son William H. Strawn & William was said to have moved to Hardin Co. or Mc Nairy Co. Tenn. William had a daughter Reb
2 CONC ecca who was married to Thomas Jefferson Hurley Sr.  When he died Rebecca married John G. W. Hagy and she is buried in Ledbetter Cemetery in Hardin Co. Tenn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth and Andrew Ledbetter donated the land for Ledbetter Cemetery; land formerly owned by her grandfather, William Strawn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard and Celia had 8 children: William, Stephen, Sarah, James, Richard, Joel and Greenberry (Green).
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=61454186 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 17 2018, 17:52:10 UTC''
