1 NAME Robert /Craig/
2 GIVN Robert
2 _MARNM Craig
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1792
2 ADDR
3 CITY Christiansburg
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 NOV 1852
2 PLAC Green Hill Plantation
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 TITL Rep.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT U.S. Congressman. He graduated from Lewisburg Academy and then engaged in planting on his estate. He was a member of the Virginia State House of Delegates, (1817-18, 25-18) and a member of the Virginia Board of Public Works, (1820
2 CONC -23). In 1829, he was elected as a Jacksonian to the Twenty-first and Twenty-second Congresses, serving until 1833. He was again elected as a Jacksonian to the Twenty-fourth Congress and reelected as a Democrat to the Twenty-fifth
2 CONC  and Twenty-sixth Congresses, serving (1835-41). Not seeking a re-nomination, he resumed his agricultural pursuits and was a member of the Virginia State House of Delegates, from 1850, until his death at age 60.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/31357198/robert-craig
