1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth:  May 31, 1807 Bunker Hill (Bedford County) Bedford County Virginia, USA  Death:  Jan. 3, 1870 Bunker Hill (Bedford County) Bedford County Virginia, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT US Congressman. He attended Tucker's Law School in Winchester, Virginia, was admitted to the bar, and established a legal practice in Bedford, Virginia. After serving in the Virginia House of Delegates, he was elected as a Whig to
2 CONC  Congress in 1838 and served from 1839 to 1843. Defeated for reelection in 1842, he was again elected to fill the vacancy caused by the resignation of Thomas W. Gilmer, and served from 1844 to 1845. He would serve one more term, f
2 CONC rom 1847 to 1849. He was the unsuccessful Whig candiate for Governor of Virginia in 1859. During the Civil War, he was a captain of Home Guards in the Confederate Army. Following the war, he returned to his legal practice in Bedfo
2 CONC rd. (bio by: Garver Graver) 
2 CONT
