1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth was the daughter of Polly and George Shelton, who spent their last years in Fentress Co., Tennessee.  Some say Polly's last name was Fletcher but there does not seem to be any proof this is correct.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth's father, George Shelton, received a pension in Fentress County, Tennessee for his services as a soldier in the Revolutionary War on the Virginia Line. In his pension file, George listed all the places and approximate nu
2 CONC mber of years he had lived since the war. From this information it seems most likely Elizabeth was born in Anderson County, Tennessee. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Betsy, as she was often called,  married Michael Brown, probably in Fentress Co., Tennessee about 1829. Unfortunately, all marriage records prior to 1905 for that county were destroyed in fires.  Elizabeth and Michael were parent
2 CONC s of at least 10 children: Sarah, William, Mary, Amanda Jane, Enoch C., Elijah, John Matt, Rosena, Eli H., and Thomas Jefferson Brown. 
2 CONT She outlived her husband but has not yet been found on any record after the 1870 Federal Census for Clinton Co., Kentucky. Her approximate death year, 1874, is based on the fact her son, Eli H. Brown, sold what appeared to be most
2 CONC  or all of the land that had belonged to Michael Brown, to his first cousin, George Shelton in 1874. She was not the Mrs. Brown who died in Barren County, Kentucky, as some have said. That person was listed as born in Monroe Count
2 CONC y, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT  She is probably buried next to her husband in an unmarked grave on the small farm they owned in Clinton Co., Kentucky, very near the Wayne Co., Kentucky line and the old Fentress Co., Tennessee line before Pickett Co., Tennessee 
2 CONC was created. Graves have not been found for most members of this family that lived near the border between Kentucky and Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are no pictures of Elizabeth or her husband, Michael, although some people have posted the picture of their son, Elijah Brown, with his wife, Jane (Bertram) and their first three children, as representing Michael and Elizabe
2 CONC th.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/66861247/elizabeth-brown Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 12 2026, 21:11:04 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
