1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Amanda Jane "Mandy" was the daughter of Elizabeth (Shelton) and Michael Brown. Census records show she was born in Kentucky. The earliest ones (1850 with parents, and 1860 with husband) indicate she was born in 183
2 CONC 6 in Kentucky. These are probably correct. Her father was listed on the 1833 Enumeration of Voters in Fentress Co., Tennessee so it is not likely she was born in Kentucky in 1833. She married Martin Rigney, son of Lucinda and Bluf
2 CONC ord Rigney, about 1857 but their marriage record has not been found. (Many records have not survived in the area in which she and Martin lived.) Mandy and Martin were the parents of at least six children: James, Andrew Jackson, Ma
2 CONC ry Ann "Polly", John Anderson, Wyatt, and Pleasant "Ples" Rigney.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is known from a courthouse record that Amanda's father died in Clinton County, Kentucky on 01 Mar 1858. From census records  we  conclude  that her mother died between 1870 and 1880, probably in Clinton Co., Kentucky.  It is no
2 CONC t known where either parent is buried. No inscribed tombstones, old letters or documents have been found with this information.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9035430/amanda_jane-rigney Find A Grave Memorial] - [
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 12 2026, 21:11:04 UTC''
