1 BIRT
2 DATE 1839
2 PLAC Jackson County, Tennessee, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1886
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was the son of Elizabeth (Shelton) and Michael Brown of Clinton Co., Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 1, 1863, in Wayne County, Kentucky, Enoch C. BROWN posted a Bond to marry Sarah Ann JONES. The bond gives the following information: Enoch C. BROWN is 26 ears old, was born in Jackson County, Tennessee and is the son of Mi
2 CONC chael and Elizabeth BROWN.  Sarah Ann JONES is 30 years old, born in Fentress Co., Tennessee, the daughter of  Nancy JENNINGS. She is a widow with nine (9) children. They are to be married at William BUTTRAMS on  1 July 1863. Ther
2 CONC e are no returns or other proof that the marriage actually took place. Sarah's previous husband, James Jones, was still living in Fentress County, Tennessee after this Bond was posted. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Only the Marriage Bond exists. There is not Minister's Return or Marriage Certificate so there is no proof that the marriage of Enoch C. BROWN to Sarah Ann (JENNINGS) JONES was solemnized. However, when Enoch later married Louisa 
2 CONC J. (Shelton) Keith he indicated on the Bond that it was his 2nd marriage.  Sarah and her husband, James JONES,  were later enumerated together and were both listed as heirs of her father, Griffith RIGNEY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1870 Adair County, Kentucky Enoch was living next to the widow, Louisa Keeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 Adair Co., Kentucky; Harmony; Glensfork Post Office; Written Page 19; Stamped Page 87-A; Roll M593_444; July 6th; Line 15; Household and Visit #139-139; BROWN, Enoch C., age 35, male, white, farm laborer, born in Tennessee, c
2 CONC an't read or write (Next to his widowed cousin, Louisa (SHELTON) KEATH, and her children.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was in Louisa's household, and listed as a cousin, when the 1880 census was enumerated. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  1880 Adair Co., Kentucky Census; Harmony; Page 75-B
2 CONT  Harmony 075B Eliza J. KEITH Self F W W 45 Tennessee Keeping House, Tennessee Tennessee 
2 CONT  Harmony 075B George W. KEITH Son M S W 17 KY Tennessee Tennessee 
2 CONT  Harmony 075B John A. KEITH Son M S W 16 KY  KY KY 
2 CONT  Harmony 075B James W. KEITH Son M S W 16 KY  KY KY 
2 CONT  Harmony 075B E. C. BROWN Cousin M S W 50 KY  KY KY   (NOTE: This is Enoch C. BROWN, son of Michael BROWN.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Enoch Brown married the widow, Louisa J. Keith,  on Apr 12, 1886, in Columbia, Adair County, Kentucky. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adair Co., KY Marriage Bond, page #118: Enoch Brown as Principal and Junius Hancock (male) as Surety (Bondsman) for the marriage of Enoch Brown to Louisa J. Keith "both being over the age of 20 years"
2 CONT
2 CONT Louisa (Shelton) Keith Brown  died in Adair Co.,Kentucky in June 1895. It is not know exactly when Enoch died but it was after their marriage in 1886.  Family members think he was buried at Fair Play near Louisa but no inscribed m
2 CONC arker has been found.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/201292672/enoch_c-brown Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 12 2026, 21:11:04 UTC''
