1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Matt Brown was the son of Elizabeth "Betsy' Shelton and Michael Brown. On earlier census in their home he was born about 1842/1843, but after he was out on his own census shows his birth year about 1846. This 
2 CONC is not an uncommon occurence with the old census. His exact year of birth is unknown but probably was about 1843. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Matt Brown married Mary Jane Fletcher on Jan. 6, 1864 in the home of his widowed mother, "Betsy" BROWN. She apparently had moved to Adair Co., Kentucky during the Civil War to be near her brother, Elijah Shelton. The marriage
2 CONC  was performed by G.T. Rigney, Minister of the Gospel, and witnessed by J.A. Rigney and Jacob Rigney. The couple had 5 children: Robert B., Arminta, Mary M., Mistie L., and Julia Ann Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT His tombstone says he served in Company D during the Civil War. Military Records for John Brown in Company D of the 13th Kentucky Cavalry say he mustered in on December 23, 1863 at Columbia, Kentucky, joined for duty and enrolled 
2 CONC for one year at Adair Co., Kentucky shortly thereafter, and was mustered out at Camp Nelson, Kentucky on January 10, 1865, having served his one year. There is no mention of a disability, his being missing in action or of his bein
2 CONC g a Prisoner of War.    
2 CONT ______________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From Find-A-Grave Contributor #47402250, Judy Lynn, on his   wife's memorial page:
2 CONT
2 CONT "This couple is supposed to be buried in a cemetery on Harvey Ridge in Adair County. Someone listed her husband here so I am listing the wife here. There were a lot of broken stones and fieldstones in this cemetery so they might v
2 CONC ery well be here."
2 CONT
2 CONT "John served in the 13 Ky Cav during the Civil War. John and Mary Jane owned several acres of land in 1879 on Burns Creek. Service records state John Mac may have been a prisoner of war or missing in action, but family members cla
2 CONC im he died from injuries when a goat butted him over a hill." [NOTE: THESE COMMENTS ARE FROM JUDY LYNN AND DIFFER FROM THE DATA ON JOHN'S MILITARY SERVICE CARDS.]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Their children were:
2 CONT Julia Ann 1879-1952, married June (J.C.) Spoon.
2 CONT Robert married Sallie Pat Lewis and Mary Willis. Robert died 4-02-1952.
2 CONT Vesy married Lander McIntyre (McTier).
2 CONT Minnie Arminta married Henry Clay Bardin." 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Most of the Brown descendants live in Adair County but some live in Russell County." 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Joyce Reed: "Arminita Brown [daughter of John Matt Brown] married Henry Clay Bardin Feb 12, 1888, they had 5 children, and she died of T. B.in Sept 4,1899."* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/43468235/john_matt-
2 CONC brown Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 12 2026, 21:10:46 UTC''
