2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Warner Sr. was the son of John Warner Sr., and Pharaby Warner. He was the brother of three sisters and three brothers, John Jr., William Mears Warner, and Samuel A. Warner. Richard was one of the first commissioners of Mar
2 CONC shall county, and he was a member of the 23rd, 24th, and 26th Tennessee General Assembly, for the years 1839-1843, and 1845-1847 respectively. His first marriage was to Sarah Ann Sutton who bore him two daughters. One was Henriett
2 CONC a who died at a young age. The other daughter is buried with Sarah and Henrietta at Bell Buckle. His second wife was Lucy Brown, daughter of Shadrach Brown. They were parents of eight. Oddly enough they named one of them Henrietta
2 CONC  as well. Richard was married a third time to Ella Choate. Richard was wounded at the battle of New Orleans and was a cripple the rest of his life. At some point in time, they lived on Warner Bridge road, Shelbyville, Bedford Co.,
2 CONC  TN.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/131714836/richard-warner
