1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Suggested edit: 
2 CONT I am assisting a family who has an ancestor buried in El Dorado County, California in 1850. As he surely came out for the great Gold Rush, we have agreed to advise the family as to how to address the condition of the many old ceme
2 CONC teries their ancestors rest in today. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The cemetery in El Dorado County is one of the earliest cemeteries of the county but was actually "lost" for many years due to overgrowth of brush and grasses. The ancestor in this cemetery still has a grave marker which is likely
2 CONC  one of the earliest remaining gravestones in the county. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In agreeing to help the descendant, we have been researching to try to determine how many of his family members may be buried in a little cemetery in north of Gallatin, in Davies County. The ancestor buried in El Dorado County wen
2 CONC t to Missouri from Kentucky and while there served in the War of 1812 under Captain James Martin with the Kentucky Volunteers. He then removed his family to Ray County and, while living there, joined the Missouri Volunteers under 
2 CONC Captain William C. Pollard in the Second Seminole War (aka Florida War) between 1837 and 1842. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From written accounts, the family moved to Daviess County around 1840-1842, where they are enumerated on the 1850 Census done in September of 1850. The patriarch, of course, was already in California as he died the following month
2 CONC  in El Dorado County, but he was still listed with the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you for posting George W. Vallandigham, whose father, William N. Vallandigham was the oldest son of the man buried in El Dorado County. I am attempting to link the family members together so that our efforts may be made avai
2 CONC lable to other descendant family that may come "looking."
2 CONT
2 CONT Best regards,
2 CONT Sue Silver* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21324331/george-w-vallandigham Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 6 2023, 17:48:42 UTC''
