2 CONT * Son '''William G Jr Woodford''' 7
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary for '''Eva Mildred Woodford''' from the '''News & Daily Advance''', Lynchburg, Virginia, 7 December 1980, Sec B, Pg 2, Col 3:
2 CONT
2 CONT >===Eva Laughon Woodford===
2 CONT
2 CONT >HUDDLESTON -- Mrs. '''Eva Laughon Woodford''', 82, died Friday in Medical Care Center, Lynchburg. She was the widow of '''W. Garrett Woodford Sr.''' Born in Bedford County, she was a daughter of the late '''John J. Laughon '''and
2 CONC ''' Elizabeth Hackworth Laughon'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >She was a member of Mentow Baptist Church. She is survived by two sons, '''Marcus K. Woodford''' of Atlanta, Ga., and '''William G. Woodford Jr.''' of Lynchburg; two daughters, '''Mrs. Louis M. (Sibyl) Newton''' of Roanoke and ''
2 CONC 'Mrs. Marvin L. (Betty Jo) Bates''' of Culpeper; a brother, Lloyd Laughon of Lynch Station; three sisters, Mrs. Victor E. (Thelma) Arthur of Huddleston, Miss Mallie Laughon of Lynch Station and Mrs. Beulah Martin of Lynchburg, and
2 CONC  12 grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Funeral services will be conducted at 3 p.m. today from the Mentow Baptist Church by the Rev. Bert Browning. Interment will follow in the church cemetery.
