2 CONT
2 CONT *Born by 1603, based on estimated date of marriage. 
2 CONT *Came to Massachusetts Bay in 1630. First settled in Dorchester; moved to Winsor in 1638. 
2 CONT *Died in Windsor 18 Sep 1677.
2 CONT *Married ____ ____ by about 1628 (assuming that she was the mother of all his children). (Ben M. Angel notes: This presumption, that John's first wife was the mother of all children, is probably incorrect. She was probably the mot
2 CONC her of his first child only. It's uncertain whether she came to the New World.)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Moore was probably brother of Thomas Moore of Dorchester & Windsor. They appear together as witnesses to the uncupative will of John Russell on 3 Sep 1633. Most of the parcels of land in Windsor granted to John Moore were adj
2 CONC acent to parcels ranted to Thomas Moore. 
2 CONT
