1 NOTE !Information on the Drake families comes from the books: Mary and John
2 CONT Passengers.  New England Families, Genealogy and Memories, William Richard
2 CONT Cutter, Vol I-IV, New York, Lewis Pub Co, 1915.
1 NOTE Janet Wind Nixon has 16 Sep 1689, the same date as for his wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 154, Stiles.  Job had a lot of 4 acres, parallel and adjoining his brother John.  In 1659, he bought most of the Roger Ludlow lot.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The Descendants of John Drake, Windsor, Connecticut"  
2 CONT
2 CONT Job Drake (John), born, probably in England; married in Windsor, Conn., June
2 CONT 25, 1646, Mary, daughter of Henry Wolcott, of Windsor.  She died Sept. 16,
2 CONT 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT Job Drake served on the Jury of the Particular Court, Oct. 1655, and for six
2 CONT sessions after that.  He was constable in the town of Windsor in 1652.  Was
2 CONT fence viewer south side of the river 1655.  Was chosen to perambulate the
2 CONT Hartford line in 1656, and was appointed to take a list of the town in 1658.
2 CONT In the year 1661 he with others was chosen to see about timber cut on the
2 CONT common land by Hartford men.  Job Drake died Sept. 16, 1689.
1 NOTE RFN: 43524
2 CONT Emigrant ancestor.
