1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Thomas Marshall, Jr.
2 CONT * MyHeritage Family Trees
2 CONT * Birth:	Feb 6 1693 - Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT * Death:	Feb 4 1772 - Torrington, Litchfield, Connecticut
2 CONT * Parents:	Thomas Marshall, Mary Drake
2 CONT * Wife: Elizabeth Tudor - Married Oct. 9, 1725, divorced 1766
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From ''The history and genealogies of ancient Windsor, Connecticut'': by Stiles, Henry Reed, 1832-1909 Publication date 1891.  Page 467 - 468.  < [https://archive.org/details/historygenealogi02stil/page/467/mode/1up?view=theater A
2 CONC rchive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT Fam. 8.  '''Thomas'''3 (Dea. Thomas2, Capt. Sam’l1) res. at Torrington, Conn.; married 9 October 1725,  Elizabeth (sister of Rev. Samuel) Tudor, b. East Windsor, 8 July 1700.  
2 CONT
2 CONT It was said she was divorced from her husband in 1766. [For interesting documents relating to the case, see Conn. Archives, Lotteries and Divorces, Fol. I, No. 107, et alias, Stale Library.] Her granddau., Rachel Marshall, became 
2 CONC the wife of Levi Munsell of Torrlngton. Mrs. Elizabeth (Tudor) Marshall d. at the house of her son. Capt. Thomas Marshall, in Torrington (Newfield Soc), 8 Feb. 1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:	
2 CONT #Thomas Marshall, b 13 Oct 1726 
2 CONT # Gad Marshall, b 18 Feb 1731/2
2 CONT # Job Marshall, b 22, bp 25 April 1736
2 CONT # Thomas Marshall (again), b 24, bp 27 Aug 1738
2 CONT # Luke Marshall, bp 8 March 1740/1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
