1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John is called a "labourer" in 1609, and a "yeoman" later. Yeomen were small land owners, a step up from labourers, but below “gentry”.  John and Elizabeth lived first in St George Parish, Stamford, Lincoln County,
2 CONC   which is the part of Stamford adjacent to Uffington, and later in All Saints Parish on the other side of Stamford.  Stamford is about 80 miles north of London.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barber Sr. born May 1563 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT (f/g) John Barber Birth: 	Apr. 6, 1580 Death: 	Apr. 30, 1620
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barber lived in Southill Bedfordshire .John married Elizabeth Lumley Oct 17 1608 .John died at the young age of forty.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children 1.Rebecca Barber chr. 17 Apr 1609 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England bur. 6 Aug 1609 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Sarah Barber chr. 16 Sep 1610 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Sgt. Thomas Barber chr. 25 Dec 1612 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England 11 Sep 1662 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Elizabeth Barber chr. 10-11 Nov 1616 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. John Barber chr. 4 Aug 1620 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England bur. 11 March 1632/33 Stamford, Lincolnshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barber, "England Births and Christenings, 1538-1975" Name: John Barber Gender: Male Christening Date: 06 Apr 1580 Christening Place: Dymchurch, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barber, "England, Cheshire Bishop's Transcripts, 1598-1900" Name: John Barber Event Type: Burial Event Date: 30 Apr 1620 Event Place: Prestbury, Cheshire, England Gender: Male
2 CONT
2 CONT John Jr. was baptized at All Saints Parish aug 4 1620 and died Mar 22 1632 See Memorial number 88409417
2 CONT
2 CONT Sgt Thomas Barber was baptized at St George Parish b. Dec 25 1612. "St. Thomas Day" was named after him. He died in Windsor Connecticut 11 September 1662 See Memorial number 38520644 Thomas Barber 1612 for John And Elizabeth's son
2 CONC  John
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Barbar, "England Births and Christenings, 1538-1975" Name: Thomas Barbar Gender: Male Christening Date: 25 Dec 1612 Christening Place: SAINT GEORGE, STAMFORD, LINCOLN, ENGLAND Father's Name: John Barbar Father's Birthplace:
2 CONC  Father's Age: Mother's Name: Elsabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Found in a chat room: The oldest known Barber in the family tree is John Barber, who was born in 1563, lived in Southill, Bedfordshire,England, and married Agnes Cawper on April 21, 1579. John's ( b. 1563) son Edward Barber B.1588
2 CONC  may have been brother to John 1580 ? 
