2 CONT ===Samuel Barber (1673 - 1725)===
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Barber
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 17 May 1673 in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Thomas Barber II and Mary (Phelps) Barber
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Barber, Mary Barber, Sarah (Barber) Robe, Joanna (Barber) Colt, Anna Barber, Thomas Barber III, Ann (Barber) Higley and Unnamed Barber
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Holcombe) Barber — married 17 Dec 1712 (to 18 Dec 1725) in Simsbury, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Samuel Barber, Thomas Barber, Jonathan Barber, John Barber, Mercy (Barber) Buel and Sarah (Barber) Case
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 18 Dec 1725 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Barber was born in Connecticut.
2 CONT Samuel, the third son and seventh of eight children of Thomas BarberII and Mary Phelps was born on 17 May 1673 at Simsbury, Connecticut Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married Sarah Holcombe, the daughter of Nathaniel and Mary (Bliss) Holcombe on 17 December 1712 at Simsbury, Connecticut Colony by Rev. Mr. Timothy Woodbridge Clerke.[1][2] They had seven children born at Simsbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Samuel Barber (b. 1714; d. 1797), m. 11 Jun 1739 at Simsbury, CT, Tryphena Humphrey (1722-1752) Thomas Barber (b. 1716; d. 1792), m. 8 Dec 1737 at Hartford, CT, Elizabeth Adams (1715-1809) Jonathan Barber (b. 1717; d. 1745), m
2 CONC . 28 May 1740 at Simsbury, CT, Jemima Cornish (1718-1791) John Barber (b. 4 Dec 1719; d. 1797),[3] m. 22 Jan 1746 at Simsbury, CT, Lydia Reed (1726-1806) Mary Barber (b. 1720; d, 1742), Mercy Barber (b. 1721; d. 1745), m. Ephraim 
2 CONC Buell (1717-) Sarah Barber (b. 1 Apr 1722; d. 1785),[4] m. 7 Nov 1745 at Simsbury, CT, Capt. John Case IV (1719-1776) Samuel Barber died on 18 December 1725 in his 52nd year at Windsor, Connecticut Colony.[5]His buriel location is
2 CONC  not known; however, there is a Find-A-Grave memorial for him.[6] His Will was entered into probate on 7 December 1725. Bequests were made to wife, Sarah, sons Samuel, Thomas and Jonathan, daughters Sarah and Mary, and brother Ben
2 CONC jamin.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
