1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Note on Thomas Hale's first wife: Before marrying Thankful Jones, Thomas was first married to Experience Burt (1677–1719) in 1705. After Experience passed away, he married Thankful Jones, who is the direct ancestor
2 CONC  in the line leading to Cummings Pease's second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT At least four of the sons of Thomas Hale and Experience Burt served in the Revolutionary War or local militias. While many members of the broader Hale family (including the famous Nathan Hale) were active patriots, Thomas’s direct
2 CONC  children contributed significantly to the local war effort in Massachusetts and Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Hale II (1705–1797): Although he was in his late 60s and early 70s during the war, he is recognized for Patriotic Service. In small communities, older men often served in the local "Home Guard" or on committees that provide
2 CONC d supplies and oversight for the Continental Army.
