1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Rev Benjamin Trumbull
2 CONT * BIRTH	19 Dec 1735, Hebron, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH	2 Feb 1820 (aged 84), North Haven, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL	Old Cemetery, North Haven, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA, 
2 CONT *MEMORIAL ID 23872108, Photos by Jan Franco & Suzanne
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Trumbull (19 December 1735 – 2 February 1820) was an early American historian and preacher.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was graduated at Yale College A.D. 1759 and ordained Pastor of the Congregational Church in North Haven, Conn., A.D. 1760, in which relation he continued until his death, a period of almost sixty years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He composed during his ministry nearly four thousand sermons and published essays on the inspiration of the Scriptures- a history of Connecticut- a history of United States and other works for which he was honored by his Alma Mate
2 CONC r and esteemed by his countrymen as an able Divine and an accurate historian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Firm humble and devout He sustained with Dignity all his relations in life and died a firm and joyful Believer in his God and Savior Anticipating with expressions of praise the coming of the Lord.
2 CONT He married Martha Phelps in 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT Benjamin Trumbull, 1712–1793
2 CONT Mary Brown Trumbull, 1708–1763
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse
2 CONT Martha Phelps Trumbull, 1732–1825
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings
2 CONT Asaph Trumbull, 1738–1821
2 CONT Mary Trumbull Phelps, 1741–1799
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT David Trumbull, 1762–1762
2 CONT Mary Trumbull Eastman, 1765–1841
2 CONT Benjamin Trumbull, 1769–1850
2 CONT Sarah Trumbull Tuttle, 1772–1817
2 CONT Elizabeth Trumbull, 1774–1775
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The Phelps Family of America, and Their English Ancestors, With Copies of Wills, Deeds, Letters, and Other Interesting Papers, Coats of Arms and Valuable Records,'' Compiled By Judge Oliver Seymour Phelps, of Portland, Oregon, a
2 CONC nd Andrew T. Servin of Lenox.  Fourth generation, p. 143.  < [https://archive.org/details/phelpsfamilyofam01phel/page/142/mode/2up Archive.Org] >; p. 234. < [https://archive.org/details/phelpsfamilyofam01phel/page/234/mode/1up Arc
2 CONC hive.Org] > 
2 CONT
2 CONT 168. Capt. Ichabod Phelps, b. Windsor, Ct., 3 April, 1708, m. 10 Dec, 1730, Martha Tillotson, b. 17 15, d. Hebron, Ct., 3 Feb., 1786. aged 71 years. He m. 2nd widow Hubbell of Bolton; by her he had no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, b. Hebron, Ct., by 1st wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 542. I.  Martha Phelps, b. Hebron, Ct. , 23 Sept. , 1732, m. Rev. Benjamin Trumbull, D. D., 4 Dec, 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Dr. Trumbull graduated at Yale, studied theology, and settled in North Haven, Ct., where he had seven children and where he died. His wife died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 children, b. North Haven, Ct.   (Only person # 1619 I. Benjamin Trumbull, a lawyer, is mentioned.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Trumbull was elected a member of the American Antiquarian Society in 1814.[3] AAS holds original copies of over 40 titles related to, or authored by Trumbull, as well as the manuscript of his General History of the United States[4
2 CONC ][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT The manuscript collections from which this history is compiled are in the Yale library. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Martha Phelp's brother, https://www.geni.com/people/Ichabod-Phelps-Jr/6000000010094443283?through=6000000001353920325, married her husband's Benjamin Trumbull's sister, https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Phelps/6000000148092870858?t
2 CONC hrough=6000000010094443283.
2 CONT
2 CONT His grandson [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lyman_Trumbull Lyman Trumbull], son of Benjamin Trumbull Jr. and Elizabeth Mather, was a U.S. Senator from Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT ...somewhat confused by this... Benjamin Trumbull appears to marry Abigail Loomis in Bolton, CT (May 29, 1764) - two years prior to her marriage to Jordan Phttps://www.geni.com/people/Rev-Benjamin-Trumbull-II-D-D/60000000063485680
2 CONC 01#ost in 1766.   The record below taken from the internet indicates ".wid" beside her name.   Benjamin Trumbull appears to be a significant historian in early New England.¡¡
