1 NOTE Notes from Alt. Birth event: Regarding George Washington Loomis: he is listed as being born in Windsor, Hartford County, Connecticut.  However, George was born in Town of Union, County of Tolland, Connecticut.  His paternal grandf
2 CONC ather moved to Union in 1741 when George's father, Daniel Loomis, was two years old. See the book "History of Union, Connecticut" for the data.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Loomis, born 1739 in Windsor, moved with his father, Daniel Loomis, to Union in 1741. The father Daniel, was married to Sarah Enos. Sarah Enos's father was James Enos, the only original owner of land in Union, given by the 
2 CONC government, who went to live in Union. The other individuals given land to start the town of Union sold their property and never lived on it.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Daniel Loomis born 1739 was a Lt. in the American Revolution, responding to the Lexington Alarm in April 1775 and serving through 1778 under Captain Thomas Lawson of Union, County of Tolland, CT. The town of Union is still sma
2 CONC ll, having a population, as I recollect, of 630 individuals.
