2 CONT Capt Matthew Phelps BIRTH	6 Jun 1746 Harwinton, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA DEATH	26 Feb 1816 (aged 69) New Haven, Addison County, Vermont, USA BURIAL	 Evergreen Cemetery New Haven, Addison County, Vermont, USA MEMORIAL ID
2 CONC 	43894305 · View Source SHARE  SAVE TOSUGGEST EDITS MEMORIAL PHOTOS 2 FLOWERS 1 In the spring of 1776 Matthew and family settled on his plantation in New Orleans and lost his family there. He used up all of his available means, wa
2 CONC s in the Army two years, and returned to Harwinton CT in the fall of 1879 in broken health. He remarried in CT and in 1788 moved to New Haven VT where he died.  Lee Ashmore sent the following information; He kept journals (1773-17
2 CONC 80) of his voyages by sea from the Connecticut River (Saybrook) to the Mississippi (New Orleans). They were compiled into a book in 1802 and titled "Memoirs and Adventures of Captain Matthew Phelps".
