1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Loanna Barber Cooley Born 1768 Mar 9 Windsor, CT Died 1813 Mar 31 Granville, MA Age COD Burial Woodland Cemetery, Granville, Ma
2 CONT
2 CONT Father JERIJAH BARBER (John3) b 26 Dec 1738 Windsor CT d 7 Feb 1792 Windsor, CT Burial Headstone Palisado Cemetery Windsor CT FAG 8554404 m 5 Dec 1765 Windsor, CT Mother Loannah FILLEY b 19 Oct 1744 Windsor,CT d 9 Jul 1793 Windsor
2 CONC , CT Burial Headstone Palisado Cemetery Windsor, CT FAG 55516324 daughter of Amos and Eda (COOK) FILLEY Family residence Windsor, on Shady Lane (now Pleasant St)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jerijah and 4 others from Windsor were drafted and served in the Revolutionary War at New York City and Westchester in August and September of 1776. This put him in the disastrous Battle of Long Island, 27 Aug 1776, then White Pla
2 CONC ins and the subsequent retreat through Westchester. After that he found it preferable to pay someone else to serve in his place.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the War he founded a tannery at Mill Brook near Poquonock Avenue, and near his home, where he was in business for many years. Here skins of horses, cattle and sheep were brought for processing into leather for boots, saddles
2 CONC , etc. In addition to the tannery, Jerijah had a sizeable farm. [~ 1909 Barber Gen; Barbour Index; Jerijah Barber Manuscript; Stiles:Windsor; Hartford County:Beers ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jerijah and Loannah, born at Windsor-Loanna's siblings:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 JERIJAH, b 23 Aug 1766; m/1 Deborah DEXTER; m/2 Anna HAYDEN.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 LOANNAH5, b 9 Mar 1768; d 31 Mar 1813; m Jan 1789 Capt. William COOLEY Jr, b East Granville MA 19 Dec 1763, d 27 Jul 1845, son of Capt. William and Sarah (MATHER) COOLEY; r Granville. [~ Godfrey Mem Lib:Cooley Gen; LBBarbour Man
2 CONC uscript ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 1789 Jan William Cooley Born Died
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Loannah Barber/William Cooley, born Granville:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Loanna Barber COOLEY b 19 Dec 1789 Granville, Mass d 1869 Apr 28 Granville, Mercer, Ohio age 78 Burial Maple Grove Cemetery, Granville, Ohio married 1815 Nov 14 age 25 at Granville, MA Reuben ENO of Simsbury CT b 1790 Nov 13 d 1
2 CONC 865 May 27 Licking Co, Ohio Children Amelia, Amelia, Charlotte, Frederick & William residence- Granville MA, and also at Homer and Granville, both in Licking Co OH. [~ CSL:Eno Gen ~]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 William Henry COOLEY b 13 Jan 1792; ?married .
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Amanda COOLEY b 14 Apr 1794 m Heaton GRANGER of Granby CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Sophia COOLEY b 8 Mar 1796
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 John COOLEY b 10 Jan 1798 m Persis MORGAN Residences-Brimfield MA, and in New York State.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Rhoda Augusta COOLEY b 26 Jan 1800
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 Sally Maria COOLEY b 12 May 1802
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Abby Laurinda COOLEY b 25 Mar 1804
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 Charlotte Lucina COOLEY b 30 Dec 1805 d 20 Mar 1838.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Cotton Mather COOLEY b Mar 1808 m Palmer MA Eunice TINKER
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Timothy Franklin COOLEY b 23 Aug 1810 d 28 Mar 1813.
