1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/176680271/andrew-barnett-peters
2 CONT Andrew Barnett Peters
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 29 Jan 1764
2 CONT Hebron, Tolland County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 10 Aug 1851 (aged 87)
2 CONT Bradford, Orange County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Upper Plain Cemetery
2 CONT Bradford, Orange County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID
2 CONT 176680271 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Col. John Peters, and Anna or Ann Barnet, whose burial locations have not been located.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col. Peters died January 11, 1788 in London, England, and was interred in the burial ground which was then associated with St George's, Hanover Square. This graveyard was closed, and sold for redevelopment in the 1960's. Col. Pete
2 CONC rs served with the British during the American Revolution. Family history accounts indicate Andrew served in the British Navy during the American Revolution from 1780 -1783, including service on Lake Champlain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bradford Town Clerk 1798 - 1815 . Represented Bradford in the Vermont State Legislature 1798
2 CONT
2 CONT married Anna White 1780 (b.1764-1788)
2 CONT
2 CONT married Lydia Bliss December 16, 1790
2 CONT
2 CONT married Keziah Howard September 15, 1816
