2 CONT
2 CONT ===Generation Three===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17  v.  Martha3 BUSHNELL (Francis2, Francis1)'''; 
2 CONT * '''born''' circa 1640 in Salem?, Essex Co., MA; 
2 CONT * '''married''' Jonathan SMITH, son of Richard SMITH, 1 Jan 1663 in Saybrook, Middlesex Co., CT; [201,202,203,204,205]
2 CONT * '''died''' after 1705. [206]
2 CONT * She and Jonathan SMITH were residing on 14 Jan 1689 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT.[207]
2 CONT ** Jonathan Smith was born in 1635?.[208]	
2 CONT ** He was admitted a freeman in 1657 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT.[209]
2 CONT ** He '''married Hannah Adams''', daughter of Jeremy Adams, circa 1660?.[210]
2 CONT ** Land transaction(s): 
2 CONT *** 1. "'James Tappin, Sr. of Middletown, on 13 Mar. 1682/3, sold 9 acres on the east side of "The Great River" to Jonathan Smith, Sr. ... on 15 Jan 1699/1700 Jonathan "asssigned this deed for love" to his son'in-law. 
2 CONT *** 2. "'On 29 Jan 1708, Joshua Gill of Middletown, in consideration of a half mile lot which the grantees purchased from John Clark and his wife of Farmington and also for 4 pounds, sold to John Gill, Sr., George Stocking, Willia
2 CONC m Cornel, Sr., Joseph Warner, Jonathan Smith, Ebenezer Smith, Francis Smith, Joseph Long, Jonathan Stedd, Jonas Wright, Thomas Wright, John Miller, Ephraim Wilcox, James Stanelift, Nathaniel Savage, Samuel Bidwell, Jr., Jacob Corn
2 CONC el, Jr., Thomas Buck, Ebenezer Hurlbutt, Richard Gill, Ebenezer Gill, John Gill, Jr., and the said Joshua Gill, 18 acres on east of Great River 'where all the above purchaser do now inhabit and dwell.'(vol. 2, p. 396.)".[211]	
2 CONT *** Land transaction(s): From Bates' Gen. of Sarai Stow Ellis the Middletown Land Records researched by Donald Lines Jacobus: "...on 15 Jan. 1699/1700 'Jonathan Smith, Sr., of Glossenbury' assigned this deed for love to 'my son in
2 CONC  Law Joseph long of middletown'".[212]
2 CONT ** He was residing in 1699/0 in Glastonbury, Hartford Co., CT.[213]
2 CONT ** He died after 1711.[214]
2 CONT * '''Known children of Martha3 BUSHNELL and Jonathan SMITH were''' as follows: 
2 CONT ** 25 i. '''Jonathan4 SMITH'''; born 20 Nov 1664 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT.[215]
2 CONT ** 26 ii. '''Mary SMITH'''.[216]
2 CONT ** 27 iii.'''Richard SMITH'''; born 2 Nov 1667 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT.
2 CONT ** 28 iv.'''Samuel SMITH'''.[216]
2 CONT ** 29 v.  '''Joseph SMITH'''; born 14 Oct 1672 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT;[217]
2 CONT *** married Sarah HOUSE 2 Jan 1695/96.[218]
2 CONT ** 30 vi.  '''Martha SMITH'''; born 14 Nov 1674 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT;[219,220,221]
2 CONT *** married Joseph LONG, son of Thomas LONG and Sarah WILCOX, before 1699/0 
2 CONT *** (Bates says they were married c1689, Torrey bef 1701, and according to a land deed of 15 Jan 1699/1700 he was already Jonathan Smith, Sr.'s son-in-law; therefore, I'm entering their DOM as before the DOB of their 1st child. <s
2 CONC ee footnotes>).[222,223]
2 CONT ** 31 vii. '''Ebenezer SMITH'''; born 18 Mar 1676 in Wethersfield, Hartford Co., CT.[224]
2 CONT ** 32viii. '''Gershom SMITH'''; born Nov 1679 in Middletown, Middlesex Co., CT;[225]
2 CONT *** married Hannah JUDD before 1701.[226]
2 CONT ** 33 ix. '''Deborah SMITH'''; born 23 Sep 1682 in Middletown, Middlesex Co., CT.[227]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''End Notes & Sources''': (Good notes & resources!)
2 CONT * [201] George Eleazer Bushnell, Bushnell Family Genealogy, Ancestry and Posterity of Francis Bushnell (1580-1646) of Horsham, England and Guilford, Connecticut, Including Genealogical Notes of other Bushnell Families, whose conne
2 CONC ctions with this branch of the family tree have not been determined (Nashville, TN: George Eleazer Bushnell, 1945), , I:511 [Source: SayVR7]. 
2 CONT * [202] Bushnell, Bushnell Family Genealogy, p. 33. [Source: Transcript of the Horsham Church Register, by E.G. Rice, Sussex Record Society Pub., vol. 21].
2 CONT * [203] Torrey, Clarence Almon, New England Marriages Prior to 1700 (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc., 1985), p. 685. 
2 CONT * [204] NEHGR IV, "Saybrook", p. 141.
2 CONT * [205] James Savage, A Genealogical Dictionary of The First Settlers of New England showing Three Generations of Those Who Came Before May, 1692, on the Basis of Farmer's Register, Vol. IV (1st Edition; Boston: Little, Brown and 
2 CONC Company, 1862), Repository: The University of Miss. Library, p. 124.
2 CONT * [206] Torrey, p. 685.
2 CONT * [207] Bushnell, Bushnell Family Genealogy, p. 33, "Savage says they moved to Middletown, Conn. but they were in Wethersfield on 14 Jan. 1689".
