2 CONT "Frances was born about 1602, England; d. Feb. 15, 1675, Hartford, CT; bur. Center Church Cemetery (Ancient Burying Ground), Hartford, CT (marker). Mother of the known children of Thomas Hosmer."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Frances Hosmer formerly [surname unknown] aka Bushnell (unproven) Born 1602 in England Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown] [sibling(s) unknown] Wife of Thomas Hosmer — married April 6, 1635 in Kent, England Mother of
2 CONC  Hannah Hosmer, Clemence Hosmer and	Stephen Hosmer Died February 15, 1675 in Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut, United States Profile managers: Tami Osmer  [send private message], Jillaine Smith  [send private message], and Rich Dav
2 CONC is  [send private message] This page has been accessed 145 times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nominate for Profile of the Week by posting the link http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/UNKNOWN-55237 in our G+ Community. Vote by clicking the +1 button above. Categories: Puritan Great Migration.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	 This person was part of the Puritan Great Migration.  If you are interested in this profile, please check out the Puritan Great Migration Project!
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances, maiden name not known ("Bushnell" not proven), was born about 1602 in England; she died 15 Feb 1675 in Hartford, Connecticut where she's buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married about 1635 Thomas Hosmer and was the mother of his children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ronald Longaker Roberts, The Hosmer Heritage: Ancestors and Descendants of the Emigrant Thomas Hosmer, South Lake Tahoe, CA: 1984 Find A Grave Memorial# 11436082', Frances Bushnell [unproven Hosmer, Ancient Burying Ground, Hartfor
2 CONC d, Hartford County, Connecticut.
