1 NOTE He came in 1633 to Cambridge, then removed to  Hartford, Farmington, and Hartford again. He was a freeman in Cambridge, 6 May 1635, and on the list of freemen at Farmington on 12 Oct 1669. His will was dated 7 Feb 1685/6 and prove
2 CONC d 1 Sept 1687; his inventory of 14 July 1687 came to £1036. He m(2) on 6 May 1679 Catherine, widow of David Wilton, who survived him. GMB has much information on his real estate dealings and the provisions of his will. I won't dwe
2 CONC ll on it here since it is not absolutely certain that his granddaughter married Gideon Buckingham.
