1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Clemant “Clemence” Hosmer
2 CONT *Born abt 1642, probably in Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT *Died 20 Sep 1705 in Milford, Middlesex, Connecticut
2 CONT * second child born to Thomas and Francis (Busnell?) Hosmer.
2 CONT *Wife of Jonathan Hunt — married 3 September 1662 in Northampton.
2 CONT *Wife of John Smith of Milford —- married in 1694 or 1695.
2 CONT *Mother of Jonathan Hunt Jr, Thomas Hunt, Thomas Hunt Sr, Jonathan Hunt Jr, John Hunt, Hannah (Hunt) Wright, Clemence Hunt, Ebenezer Hunt, Ebenezer Hunt, Mary (Hunt) Sheldon, Sarah (Hunt) Platt and Samuel Hunt
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/15319836/clemant-smith
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. in the 63 year of hir age
2 CONT
2 CONT [born about 1642, daughter of Thomas Hosmer, 1st wife of John Smith]
2 CONT [CLEMENCE, 2nd known child of Thomas & Frances Hosmer, was born about 1642 ("Osmer, Clements, she is 15 years old" 12 December 1657. She married (1) at Northampton 3 September 1662 Jonathan Hunt. She married (2) in 1694 or 1695 Jo
2 CONC hn Smith of Milford. Source: Anderson's Great Migration Begins]
2 CONT
