1 NAME John /Jordan/ Sr.
2 GIVN John
2 SURN Jordan
2 NSFX Sr.
2 _MARNM Jordan
2 NICK John Jordon of Guilford
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1618
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE JAN 1649
2 PLAC Guilford, New Haven, Connecticut
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Signer of Covenant
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =John Jordan=
2 CONT * BIRTH 1613 Lenham, Maidstone Borough, Kent, England
2 CONT * IMMEGRATED 1639 to Guilford
2 CONT * DEATH 29 Mar 1650 (aged 36–37) Guilford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Village Green Cemetery, Guilford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 160372264  
2 CONT
2 CONT John Jordan immigrated to Guilford, CT on the first ship "St. John" in 1639. His younger brother, Thomas, may have come in the same ship and was not listed, being underage. Thomas went back home in 1655, but his daughter Elizabeth
2 CONC  m. Andrew Leete of Guilford and had six children, all living at the time of the death of their parents.  John is listed in this book as marrying a second time to Ann (no last name), of Guilford, but no documentation is given for 
2 CONC this statement. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Oct 1639 in Menunkatuck to Anne Bishop, daughter of John Bishop (1590-1661) and Ann Stevens (1592-1676).  Anne was born in 1622 in England and died on 3 Jan 1671/1672 in Killingworth, New Haven, Connecticut.   After J
2 CONC ohn Jordan's death she married Thomas Clarke (1605-1668) and had two more children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Jordan and Anne Bishop:
2 CONT # Joanna 
2 CONT # Mary 
2 CONT # Elizabeth 
2 CONT # John JORDAN was born in Mar 1646/1647.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gravesite Details'''
2 CONT Time and weather had erased the location of this grave when the cemetery was moved
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Ann Bishop Clark 1622–1672 (m. 1639)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Joanna Jordan Chittenden 1639–1683
2 CONT Mary Jordan Post 1643–1683
2 CONT Elizabeth Jordan Hubbard 1644–1720
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes=== 
2 CONT * Don't confuse him with John Jordan of Plymouth 
2 CONT * Parents are NOT James Jordan (1592 England - 29 Mar 1655 in Dedham, Norfolk, Massachusetts) and ??
2 CONT * His son was *NOT* the John of Massachusetts as shown here. His son John married Deborah and stayed in CT.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==  
2 CONT 1 https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/160372264/john_jordan
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 "History of the Colony of New Haven" by Edward Atwater, p. 633.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~wayland/fowler/pafg40.htm#1085
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Guilford Hist 25, 45; FOOF 1 :346-47; NEHGR 62:333; Ackley-Bosworth 97
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 Great Migration Directory: John Jordan origins and parents are still Unkqown; Arrived 1639 to Guilford 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 [https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=wu.89062958764;view=1up;seq=145 The ancestry of Lorenzo Ackley & his wife Emma Arabella Bosworth]
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=129351-2-16482&action=showRecord&indId=externalindividual-1afda5c0641e6f9a10463577809ba1b5&mrid=004eb4a64288d70c492ae37dac512f82]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Additional Data==
2 CONT '''John Jordan'''  was born about 1618 in *UNKNOWN*. He died in Jan 1650 in Guilford, New Haven, Connecticut. 
