1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Joanna Jordan Chittenden=
2 CONT * BIRTH 9 Dec 1639 Guilford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH Oct 1683 (aged 43) Guilford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Village Green Cemetery, Guilford, New Haven County, Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 160371789
2 CONT
2 CONT Joanna Jordan, dau. of John Jordan and Anne Bishop, b. in Guilford (date not recorded), m. there Thomas Chittenden, son of William Chittenden and Joanna Schaeffe, 1662. He was one of the witnesses to the deed from the Mohegan Sach
2 CONC em for additional land for the colony, Jan. 13, 1683 at Guilford, New Haven, Connecticut, d. Guilford, October, 1683[1]  Their children were Samuel, William, Joanna, Thomas, Mehitable, Josiah and Abigail Chittenden
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gravesite Details'''
2 CONT Although this person was likely interred in Guilford's original village cemetery (now the commons and public park in downtown Guilford), no surviving gravestone was known in 1818 when all gravestones at the Village Green, but not 
2 CONC the people's remains, were dispersed to other town cemeteries.  Time and weather had erased the location of this grave when the cemetery was moved
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT John Jordan 1613–1650
2 CONT Ann Bishop Clark 1622–1672
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Thomas Chittenden 1635–1683 (m. 1663)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Mary Jordan Post 1643–1683
2 CONT Elizabeth Jordan Hubbard 1644–1720
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Half Siblings'''
2 CONT Sarah Clark Cornwall 1654–1717
2 CONT Richard Clark 1659–1744
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Samuel Chittenden 1664–1694
2 CONT William Chittenden 1666–1738 m Hannah 
2 CONT Joanna Chittenden 1668–1752
2 CONT Abigail, m Caleb Bennett 
2 CONT Thomas Chittenden 1674–1722
2 CONT Mehitabel Chittenden 1675–1675
2 CONT Josiah, m Hannah Sherman
2 CONT
