2 CONT
2 CONT "He was twice married: 1st to Frances Alexander, prior to his arrival at Guilford, and, according to Dr. Talcott, before his emigration; and 2nd to Katharine Chalker. "John Hill of Guilford m. Katern Chalker 23 September, 1673." [
2 CONC 3]  "probably the widow of Alexander Chalker" [1] [who] was an early settler in Saybrook where he married Kathrine Post, Sept. 29, 1649, and had issue," among others, "4. Catern, b. Sept. 8, 1657; m. John Hill, of Greenfield [Guil
2 CONC ford], 1673." If we follow Hinman, she was only sixteen years old when she became John Hill's second wife, at which time his eldest son was nearly thirty-three years old; but Savage is most likely correct."
2 CONT
2 CONT An inventory of her estate was exhibited and accepted at a session in New London on 18 September 1694. Administration was granted to Abraham Chalker, expressly called "her Son."
2 CONT
