1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elizabeth Stevens Chittenden=
2 CONT * BIRTH 14 Jul 1668 Killingworth, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 15 Nov 1738 (aged 70) Killingworth, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Old Killingworth Cemetery, Killingworth, Middlesex County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 171661719 [1], 161580473 [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Chittenden II and Elizabeth Stevens were married about 1690, probably in Killingworth, Connecticut. They had four known children: Phebe, Timothy, Elizabeth, and Nathaniel III.
2 CONT
2 CONT There has been some speculation that this Elizabeth Stevens is the one who married Abraham Post and had nine children with him. None of this adds up with the births of the children with overlapping dates. Stevens seems to have bee
2 CONC n a fairly common name during this time period, so having two unrelated or related Elizabeth Stevens is entirely possible.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gravesite Details'''
2 CONT Time and weather has possibly erased the location of this grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Thomas Stevens 1628–1685
2 CONT Mary Fletcher Stevens 1632–1679
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Nathaniel Chittenden 1669 – unknown (m. 1690)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
