2 CONT Per Holcombe Genealogy 
2 CONT
2 CONT LT. SILAS HOLCOMBE  (Judah4, Nathaniel3, Nathaniel2, Thomas1) born 27 Nov 1734 Granby, Hartford Co., CT married Mary Post DO Stephan Post& Mary Downer died 6 Oct 1806 North Granby, Granby, Hartford Co., CT age 71 buried Lee Cemete
2 CONC ry, Granby, Hartford Co., CT
2 CONT
2 CONT Silas served as a lieutenant in the 2nd Battalion under Col. Thaddeus Cook, 1776, Connecticut troops. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lt. Silas Holcombe & Mary Post: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. MARY born 1763 Granby, Hartford Co., CT died 2 Oct 1803 Granby, Hartford Co.,CT buried Lee Cemetery, Granby, Hartford Co., CT married 21 Apr 1784 at First Congregational Church, Simsbury, Hartford Co., CT Job Case Jr. SO Capt. 
2 CONC Job Case & Joanna Wilcox
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. LUCY/LUCYNA born 1764 died 31 Aug 1800 Southwick, Hampden Co., MA married 17 Oct 1781 at East Granby, Hartford Co., CT Elijah Holcombe SO Elijah Holcombe & Violet Cornish Lucy's gravestone reads "Lucyna." 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. ANNA  born 1767 Granby, Hartford Co., CT married Lt. Ferdinand Clemmons died 24 Aug 1827  buried Lee Cemetery, Granby, Hartford Co., CT
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. SABRA  born 1768 died 19 Sep 1777 buried Lee Cemetery, Granby, Hartford Co., CT
