1 NAME Judson /Webb/
2 GIVN Judson
2 SURN Webb
2 _MARNM Webb
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Onondaga Valley Cemetery, Syracuse, Onondaga County, New York, USA
2 ADDR
3 CITY Syracuse
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 APR 1775
2 PLAC Stamford, Fairfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stamford
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 JAN 1848
2 ADDR
3 CITY Onondaga Hollow
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Member of Onondaga Valley Presbyterian Church at the time of organization - March 20 1810. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional children:  Eshelinda Jane, with Jerusha
2 CONT
2 CONT JUDSON WEBB. Born in Stamford. Conn.. April 11th, 1775. About the year 1800 removed to Lansingburg. N. Y., and commenced the manufacturing of boots and shoes. In 1808 removed to  Onondaga Hollow and kept a tavern on the west side 
2 CONC of the Hollow. He was captain in the State militia and went with his company to Oswego in 1812, when threatened by British invasion. In 1835 removed to Syracuse and kept the Onondaga Temperance House, later a grocery store, corner
2 CONC  Lock and Water St. Died January 24th, 1848, aged 73, buried in Valley cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Syracuse Daily Journal 2/20/1897
2 CONT
