0 @N6000000002339097491@ NOTE Bruce graduated from Montevideo High School in May 1940.  He earned a BSdegree in Animal Husbandry from the College of Agriculture, Forestry, and Home Economics at the University of Minnesota.  He graduated on 21 Dec 1944 and went
1 CONC  to work for the South St Paul office of the US Department of Agriculture as a livestock market news reporter.  After marriage, he was transferred to the Des Moines, IA office and while there Bruce and Marilyn lived in a trailer o
1 CONC n the Earl Short property.  In August 1948 he was promoted to "officer in charge" of the South Memphis Stockyards in Memphis, TN.  After seven years he was transferred to Sioux City, IA (September 1955) and in August 1960 he was p
1 CONC romoted to the position of Eastern Area Supervisor of Livestock Market News.  His job transferred him to the central office in Washington, DC.  The family moved to Springfield, VA.  He retired after 34 years and 10 days on January
1 CONC  12, 1979.  In July 1981 he and Marilyn moved to Lynchburg,VA.[CRONE Family-1.FTW]
