0 @N6000000001657844497@ NOTE
1 CONT http://pages.cthome.net/firstchurchnl/history/bulkeley.htm
1 CONT Pastorate of Gershom Bulkeley
1 CONT 1661-1665
1 CONT
1 CONT     Son of the Rev. Peter Bulkeley, the first minister (non-Conformist) of Concord, Massachusetts.  Never ordained as pastor of the church, although the town wished it.  Married Sarah, daughter of President Cauncey of Harvard Coll
1 CONC ege.  Became pastor (1667) of Wethersfield Church.  
1 CONT
1 CONT     Author of pamphlet, "Will and Doom, or The Miseries of Connecticut by and under an Usurped and Arbitrary Power," (1692); also of a volume on the divinity of the Scriptures.  Inscription upon his tombstone in Wethersfield reads
1 CONC : "He was honorable in his descent; of rare abilities, extraordinary industry, excellent learning, master of many languages, exquisite in his skill in divinity, physic and law, and of a most exemplary and Christian life.  In certa
1 CONC m beatae resurrectionis repositus." 
1 CONT
1 CONT Interesting note!
1 CONT Gershom Bulkeley was an able physician and surgeon, and he left the ministry in 1677 to practice medicine in Glastonbury, Connecticut.
