1 CONT Text: From Rt. 460 between Bedford and Lynchburg, turn on to Rt. 715 Krantzs Corner Rd. 1/4 mile house on left. 
1 CONT Once in a lifetime opportunity to purchase Historic Plantation, built by Colonel David Saunders Circa 1785.
1 CONT
1 CONT The Home of Mr. and Mr. H. B. Copenhaver was built by Colonel David Saunders, an important Bedford pioneer, circa 1785. Saunders is believed to have owned a plantation of 5,000 acres between Big an d Little Otter rivers in eastern
1 CONC  Bedford County. He married Lockey Leftwich and they had 16 children. Saunders, a busy man, fought with George Washington at Valley Forge, served as a magistrate, a s a member of the General Assembly, as county sheriff and he foug
1 CONC ht in the War of 1812. He was a presiding justice when he died and he was buried in the yard at Pleasant Grove.
1 CONT
1 CONT Situated on 60 beautiful acres offered in 5 +/- tracts, the federal style brick home features 3 bedrooms 2 1/2 baths, Pine Hard Wood floors, formal living room, formal dinning room, den, study, basem ent, summer kitchen and much m
1 CONC ore.[CRONE Family-1.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [CRONE Family-1.FTW.GED.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT RootWeb source shows David Saunders and W. David Saunders.
