1 CONT iiiInfant, bur. Crewkerne 8 January 1623[/4].
1 CONT ivNATHANIEL, bp. Crewkerne 6 March 1624[/5]; m. Windsor 17 September 1650 Elizabeth (_____) Copley [Grant 55].
1 CONT With second wife
1 CONT vCORNELIUS, bp. Crewkerne 13 October 1627; no further record.
1 CONT viJOSEPH (twin), bp. Crewkerne 13 November 1628; m. (1) Windsor 20 September 1660 Hannah Newton [Grant 57; TAG 65:13-16]; m. (2) Northampton 19 December 1676 Mary (_____) Salmon [Pynchon VR 20].
1 CONT viiMARY (twin), bp. Crewkerne 13 November 1628; d. soon.
1 CONT viiiMARY, bp. Crewkerne 6 December 1629; no further record.
1 CONT ixSARAH, b. say 1632; m. Windsor 9 June 1658 William Wade [Loomis 1:63].
1 CONT xTIMOTHY, b. Windsor Aug. or 1 September 1639 [Grant 55]; m. Windsor 19 March 1661[/2?] Mary Griswold [Grant 56].
1 CONT xiMARY, b. March 1644 [Grant 55]; m. Windsor 17 December 1663 Thomas Barber [Grant 25].
1 CONT ASSOCIATIONS:  George Phelps of Dorchester and Windsor (not to be confused with GEORGE PHILLIPS of the same two places) may have been a brother of William Phelps [TAG 65:165-66].  This George Phelps married as his first wife Philu
1 CONC ra Randal, daughter of PHILLIP RANDALL; he was also, in some manner as yet undetermined, an uncle of Elisha Hart, son of EDMUND HART.
1 CONT
1 CONT COMMENTS:  In 1919 Mary Lovering Holman prepared a brief account of the family of William Phelps [Scott Gen 252-53].  In 1990 Myrtle S. Hyde resolved the problem of the identity of the wives of William Phelps and was also able to 
1 CONC find the baptisms of his children in England [TAG 65:161-66].  All the Crewkerne records cited above are taken from her article.
1 CONT
