1 CONT Notes for DAVID MARSHALL:
1 CONT David Marshal will date 22 June 1694
1 CONT
1 CONT I david Marshall of Windsor doe make this my last will and testament: I
1 CONT give to my little son David Marshall at the age of 21 years, half of my
1 CONT housing & Homested, and the whole after my wife's decese. Also I give
1 CONT unto my son my swamp or meadow land lying by Hoyt's Meadow. Also my
1 CONT Great Lott, 65 rods in Breadth, & to take his part on the westerly side
1 CONT next to George Griswold's Land, and the length to run the whole length
1 CONT of said lott, excepting only 4 or 5 acres, which I have exchanged with
1 CONT Benajah Holcomb for the land where my house now stands, to be to him
1 CONT forever; only the said David Marshall is hereby bound to pay unto his
1 CONT two sisters 5 pd apeice in Country pay within 2 years after he comes to
1 CONT be possessed of the premises. I give unto my wife Abigail Marshall,
1 CONT after just debts & all Expenses are paid, the Use & Benefit of my whole
1 CONT estate Personal or Real, until my children come of age; and half of all
1 CONT the movable estate to be at her own dispose forever; and also half the
1 CONT house & homested during her natural life, & 1-3 part of the benefit of
1 CONT the Real Estate. I give unto my two daughters Abigail and Hannah
1 CONT Marshall, to be equally divided betwixt them, all my other land not
1 CONT herein disposed otherwise, and also half of my Moveable Estate. It is my
1 CONT will that my wife Abigail Marshall shall be sole executrix, and that my
1 CONT bretheren Thomas Marshall & William Phelps, with Benajah Holcomb sen.,
1 CONT shall be overseers.       David Marshall LS
1 CONT Witness: Daniel Griswold
1 CONT John Griswold
1 CONT
