1 CONT
1 CONT Became an inhabitant of New London, in 1652, and probably brought his wife, Hester, with him from Roxbury.  
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #2:  Leslie Mahler, "The English Origin of Valentine Prentice of Roxbury, Massachusetts" in "The American Genealogist, July, 2002, pp 173-175.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source#3: Robert Charles Anderson. The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to New England, 1620-1633 [database online] Provo, UT: Ancestry.com, 2000. Original data: Robert Charles Anderson. The Great Migration Begins: Immigrants to
1 CONC  New England, 1620-1633, vols. 1-3. Boston, MA: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1995
1 CONT
1 CONT JOHN, b. say 1627; m. (1) about 1651 Hester Nichols; m. (2) by 1683 Esther Nichols; m. (3) by contract dated 12 June 1685 Rebecca Parker. (See TAG 34:81-89 for a detailed account of his wives and children; the first two wives were
1 CONC  first cousins.)
1 CONT
1 CONT Source #4:  Donald Lines Jacobus, "John Prentice of New London, Conn. and His Two Nichols Wives,"  in "The American Genealogist" (TAG 34: 81-89) January, 1958.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married (3rd) Rebecca Parker, 12 June 1685.
