0 @N6000000001720866803@ NOTE Lived at one time in Charity, Tennessee. After the death of his father, Jesse
1 CONT bought each sibling's inherited share.  He served as Constable of Lincoln Co
1 CONT until 02 SEP 1839.  He died a few weeks before the birth of his 8th child.
1 CONT Two of his children died in the Civil War, another lost and arm in the Battle
1 CONT of Atlanta.  Wife Jane lived on the original Neece homestead until her death.
0 @N6000000001720870559@ NOTE Littleberry enlisted as a Private in Co. A, 41st Tenn Infantry on 01DEC1862.
1 CONT At that time, his wife was pregnant with their forth child.  He deserted on
1 CONT January 12, 1863 near Port Hudson, Louisiana to return home for the birth of
1 CONT his son.  James Berry Neece was born on January 20.  Littleberry stayed with
1 CONT his family until he rejoined his unit in June 5, 1863.  On November 27 he was
1 CONT captured at the Battle of Ringgold Gap (near Chattanooga,TN). He was sent to KY
1 CONT then to Rock Island, ILL, where he died 14APR1864 of an infection on his arm.
0 @N6000000001720866212@ NOTE Harrison served in the 41st Tennessee Infantry in the Civil War from 1861
1 CONT until it's conclusion in 1865.  His brother, Littleberry, was in the same unit
1 CONT but was captured in 1863.  Harrison was wounded in the battle of Atlanta by a
1 CONT canon ball and lost his right arm.
0 @N6000000001720866711@ NOTE Civil War record: Member of LtGen N B Forrest's Escort Company.
1 CONT Surrendered at Gainsville Alabama on May 5, 1865; paroled May 9th.
1 CONT Records give his name as James K. P. Neece.  Thanks to Russell ONeal who
1 CONT pointed out that many boys of this era were named for U S Presidents.
1 CONT James Knox Polk was the 11th President, was from Tennessee, and was elected in
1 CONT 1844, the same year James Knox Polk was born.
0 @N6000000001720872506@ NOTE There is some uncertainty about Rebecca's marriage to N H Marby.  It is
1 CONT recorded in the Lincoln County Marriage Book Jan 01, 1867.  She had been
1 CONT married to  Littleberry Leftwich III in 1864.  She is referred to as Rebecca
1 CONT Leftwich in her mother's will in 1876, and her 1906 gravestone shows her as
1 CONT Catherine Leftwich.  Perhaps the marriage to N H Marby was very short and she
1 CONT resumed the Leftwich name sine she had children under that name.  Or....?
