0 @N6000000004548322633@ NOTE REFN: 5145
1 CONT JOHN HIGLEY-b. 7-22-1649, Frimley, Surrey, England; d. 8-25-1714,
1 CONT Simsbury, CT.  An importer land holder, public office holder, and Captain
1 CONT of the train band (1698), his will was dated 5-6-1714, naming wife, sarah
1 CONT and a ll 15 of his surviving children.  Son of JONATHON HIGLEY and
1 CONT KATHERINE BREWST ER, who were married 1-3-1648.  Katherine was the
1 CONT daughter of REV. JOHN BREWS TER (d. 8-14-1656) and reportedly a relative
1 CONT of ELDER WILLIAM BREWSTER of the Mayflower fame.  JOHN HIGLEY may have
1 CONT been a run away apprentice at the time he left England and evidence
1 CONT suggests that upon his arrival at Windsor, CT a bout 1666, he entered the
1 CONT service of JOHN DRAKE, JR.  He married first 11-9-1 671, Windsor, CT
1 CONT HANNAH DRAKE (b. 8-8-1653, Windsor, CT; d. 8-4-1694, Simsbur y, CT),
1 CONT daughter of JOHN DRAKE, JR. and HANNAH MOORE.  Though currently in
1 CONT question, in the past JOHN DRAKE, JR. has been connected with the DRAKE
1 CONT famil y in England,  which included the noted SIR FRANCIS DRAKE (JOHN
1 CONT DRAKE, SR. be ing the great grandson of John, brother of Sir Frandis'
1 CONT father, Edmund), and SIR WALTER RALEIGH (he being the husband of JOAN
1 CONT DRAKE, sister of John and Ed mund, and aunt of Sir Francis).  JOHN HIGLEY
1 CONT obtained land at Windsor, CT fro m his father-in-law, and operated a
1 CONT business importing rum and other commodit ies from Barbados.  He purchased
1 CONT additional Land in Windsor, and in 1684 move d to Simsbury, CT where he
1 CONT became active in public life, excepting that of th e church.  He married
1 CONT second about 1696 Simsbury, CT, SARAH STRONG, b. 3-14-1 666 Windsor, CT;
1 CONT d. 5-27-1739, Windsor, CT.  Daughter of RETURN STRONG and SA RAH WARHAM,
1 CONT widow of JOSEPH BISSELL (d. 8-3-1689).  Sarah and Joseph had two sons:
1 CONT Joseph (b. 3-21-1687) and Benoni (b. 12-7-1689; d.8-6-1761).
