0 @N6000000003796030678@ NOTE Post Family Genealogy
1 CONT http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/htm/post.htm#name3012
1 CONT 4.Lt. Stephen Post - was born in 1596 in Chelmsford, England and died on 16 Aug 1659 in Saybrook, CT . He was the son of Abraham Post and Ann Hunter.
1 CONT Lt. Stephen married Eleanore Panton on 17 Oct 1625 in Hollingbourne, Kent, England. Eleanore was born in Chelmsford, England. She died on 13 Nov 1670 in Saybrook, CT .
1 CONT
1 CONT Lt. Stephen - and Eleanore came to America in the ship "Griffin" arriving in Boston on September 4, 1633. Stephen was a carpenter. He lived at Otham, Kent, England, where most of his children were born. He was a follower and adjer
1 CONC ent of the Rev. Thomas Hooker.
1 CONT
1 CONT His name appears on the monument as one of the founders of Hartford, CT. He migrated first to Newtowne (Cambridge), MA in 1634, then joined Rev. Hooker's group at Hartford, CT, then to Saybrook, CT, where he purchased his first la
1 CONC nd in Oyster Rever in 1648. (from: lth1424_1 Florida, USA)
1 CONT Children: (Quick Family Chart)
1 CONT i. John Post was born on 16 Sep 1629 in Otham, Kent, England and died on 27 Nov 1711 in Norwich, CT . See #5. below
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Post Family Genealogy
1 CONT http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/htm/post.htm#name3012
1 CONT 5.John Post - was born on 16 Sep 1629 in Otham, Kent, England and died on 27 Nov 1711 in Norwich, CT . He was the son of Lt. Stephen Post and Eleanore Panton.
1 CONT John married Hester Hyde on 31 Mar 1652/1653 in Saybrook, CT. Hester was born about 1625 in England. She was the daughter of William Hyde. She died on 13 Nov 1703 in Norwich, CT .
1 CONT
1 CONT John - was in Hartford by 1636; to Saybrook 1649; to Norwich 1660. An original proprietor of Norwich; accepted freeman 1663, townsman 1674.
1 CONT Children: (Quick Family Chart)
1 CONT i. Margaret Post was born on 21 Feb 1653 in Middlesex, Ct and died Nov 1700 in Norwich, Ct .
1 CONT Margaret married Sergt. Caleb Abell Jul 1669 in Norwich, MA. Sergt. Caleb was born in 1646 in Rehobeth, Ma. He was the son of Robert Abel. He died on 17 Aug 1731 in Norwich, Ct .
1 CONT See Abell family for children.
1 CONT ii. Mary Post was born Jun 1669 in Norwich, New London, Ct and died Nov 1705 in Norwich, New London, Ct .
1 CONT Mary married Nathaniel Rudd. Nathaniel was born about 1655 in Saybrook, Middlesex, CT. He died on 18 Apr 1727 in Franklin, New London, CT .
1 CONT See Rudd family for children.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Hyde Family Genealogy
1 CONT http://www.renderplus.com/hartgen/htm/hyde.htm
1 CONT 16.William Hyde - was born in 1600 in Stockport, England and died on 6 Jan 1681 in Norwich, CT . He was the son of William Hyde and Eleanor Molineux.
1 CONT William married Mrs..\\  (first wife)
1 CONT   Then William married Joanna \\ (second wife). She died after 1682 .
1 CONT No children from his second marriage to Joanne, the widow of Robert Abell
1 CONT
1 CONT William - came to America from Chestershire (Cheshire), England.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Founder and original proprietor of Hartford, 1636. Selectman 1637." (This is stated on a monument in an old graveyard of First Church of Hartford, Conn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT William Hyde came to New England from old England in 1633 in company with the Rev. Thomas Hooker, the first minister at Hartford. For a short time they remained at Newton, mass., and then both came to Hartord in 1636.
1 CONT
1 CONT At a later period, William Hyde went to Saybrook, where his daughter was married in 1652; still later, Mr. Hyde and son Samuel were among the thirty-five original proprietors of Norwich.
1 CONT
1 CONT There he died in 1781, a man of considerable importance in colonial affairs.
1 CONT
1 CONT (Biographical Record of Tolland and Windham Counties, page 301)
1 CONT (Sources: - 5)
1 CONT Children with Mrs. (Quick Family Chart)
1 CONT i. Hester Hyde was born about 1625 in England and died on 13 Nov 1703 in Norwich, CT .
1 CONT Hester married John Post on 31 Mar 1652/1653 in Saybrook, CT. John was born on 16 Sep 1629 in Otham, Kent, England. He was the son of Lt. Stephen Post and Eleanore Panton. He died on 27 Nov 1711 in Norwich, CT .
1 CONT See Post family for children.
1 CONT ii. Samuel Hyde was born about 1637 in Hartforf, CT and died Jul 1677 in Norwich, CT . See #17. below.
